{"surah": 12, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "الٓرۚ تِلْكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ٱلْمُبِينِ ", "translation": "Alif, Lām, Rā.[1] These are the verses of the clear Book.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "الٓر", "translit": "rٓlā", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِt", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُبِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِbُmْlٱ", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "إِنَّآ أَنزَلْنَٰهُ قُرْءَٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ ", "translation": "Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur’ān[1] that you might understand.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنزَلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قُرْءَٰنًا", "translit": "āًnَٰءْrُq", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَرَبِيًّا", "translit": "āًّyِbَrَʿع", "root": "عرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّعَلَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّlَʿعَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْقِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِqْʿعَt", "root": "عقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "نَحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ أَحْسَنَ ٱلْقَصَصِ بِمَآ أَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَيْكَ هَٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانَ وَإِن كُنتَ مِن قَبْلِهِۦ لَمِنَ ٱلْغَٰفِلِينَ ", "translation": "We relate to you, [O Muḥammad], the best of stories in what We have revealed to you of this Qur’ān although you were, before it, among the unaware.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَقُصُّ", "translit": "ُّṣُqَn", "root": "قصص"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَصَصِ", "translit": "ِṣَṣَqْlٱ", "root": "قصص"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَوْحَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَḥْwَaʾ", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرْءَانَ", "translit": "َnāَءْrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰفِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِfَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غفل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ يُوسُفُ لِأَبِيهِ يَٰٓأَبَتِ إِنِّى رَأَيْتُ أَحَدَ عَشَرَ كَوْكَبًا وَٱلشَّمْسَ وَٱلْقَمَرَ رَأَيْتُهُمْ لِى سَٰجِدِينَ ", "translation": "[Of these stories mention] when Joseph said to his father,[1] \"O my father, indeed I have seen [in a dream] eleven stars and the sun and the moon; I saw them prostrating to me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِأَبِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِbَaʾِl", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَتِ", "translit": "ِtَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَأَيْتُ", "translit": "ُtْyَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَحَدَ", "translit": "َdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَشَرَ", "translit": "َrَhsَʿع", "root": "عشر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كَوْكَبًا", "translit": "āًbَkْwَk", "root": "كوكب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٱلشَّمْسَ", "translit": "َsْmَّhslٱَw", "root": "شمس"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَٱلْقَمَرَ", "translit": "َrَmَqْlٱَw", "root": "قمر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَأَيْتُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُtْyَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سَٰجِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِjgَٰs", "root": "سجد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "قَالَ يَٰبُنَىَّ لَا تَقْصُصْ رُءْيَاكَ عَلَىٰٓ إِخْوَتِكَ فَيَكِيدُوا۟ لَكَ كَيْدًاۖ إِنَّ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنَ لِلْإِنسَٰنِ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "He said, \"O my son, do not relate your vision to your brothers or they will contrive against you a plan. Indeed Satan, to man, is a manifest enemy.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰبُنَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَnُbَٰy", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَقْصُصْ", "translit": "ْṣُṣْqَt", "root": "قصص"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رُءْيَاكَ", "translit": "َkāَyْءُr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِخْوَتِكَ", "translit": "َkِtَwْhkِiʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَيَكِيدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdyِkَyَf", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كَيْدًا", "translit": "āًdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيْطَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰṭْyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لِلْإِنسَٰنِ", "translit": "ِnَٰsnِiʾْlِl", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَدُوٌّ", "translit": "ٌّwُdَʿع", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ يَجْتَبِيكَ رَبُّكَ وَيُعَلِّمُكَ مِن تَأْوِيلِ ٱلْأَحَادِيثِ وَيُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهُۥ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَىٰٓ ءَالِ يَعْقُوبَ كَمَآ أَتَمَّهَا عَلَىٰٓ أَبَوَيْكَ مِن قَبْلُ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ وَإِسْحَٰقَۚ إِنَّ رَبَّكَ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ", "translation": "And thus will your Lord choose you and teach you the interpretation of narratives [i.e., events or dreams] and complete His favor upon you and upon the family of Jacob, as He completed it upon your fathers before, Abraham and Isaac. Indeed, your Lord is Knowing and Wise.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَجْتَبِيكَ", "translit": "َkyِbَtْjgَy", "root": "جبي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَيُعَلِّمُكَ", "translit": "َkُmِّlَʿعُyَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَأْوِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِwْaʾَt", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحَادِيثِ", "translit": "ِhtyِdāَḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَيُتِمُّ", "translit": "ُّmِtُyَw", "root": "تمم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "نِعْمَتَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَtَmْʿعِn", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَعَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ءَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَء", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَعْقُوبَ", "translit": "َbwُqْʿعَy", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "كَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَتَمَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّmَtَaʾ", "root": "تمم"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَبَوَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَwَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَإِسْحَٰقَ", "translit": "َqَٰḥْsِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "حَكِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِkَḥ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "لَّقَدْ كَانَ فِى يُوسُفَ وَإِخْوَتِهِۦٓ ءَايَٰتٌ لِّلسَّآئِلِينَ ", "translation": "Certainly were there in Joseph and his brothers signs for those who ask, [such as]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَّقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَإِخْوَتِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِtَwْhkِiʾَw", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتٌ", "translit": "ٌtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِّلسَّآئِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِyʾٓāَّslِّl", "root": "سال"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "إِذْ قَالُوا۟ لَيُوسُفُ وَأَخُوهُ أَحَبُّ إِلَىٰٓ أَبِينَا مِنَّا وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ إِنَّ أَبَانَا لَفِى ضَلَٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "When they said, \"Joseph and his brother[1] are more beloved to our father than we, while we are a clan. Indeed, our father is in clear error.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَيُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُyَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَأَخُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُhkَaʾَw", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَحَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَḥَaʾ", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَبِينَا", "translit": "āَnyِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عُصْبَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَbْṣُʿع", "root": "عصب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَبَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "ٱقْتُلُوا۟ يُوسُفَ أَوِ ٱطْرَحُوهُ أَرْضًا يَخْلُ لَكُمْ وَجْهُ أَبِيكُمْ وَتَكُونُوا۟ مِنۢ بَعْدِهِۦ قَوْمًا صَٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "Kill Joseph or cast him out to [another] land; the countenance [i.e., attention] of your father will [then] be only for you, and you will be after that a righteous people.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱقْتُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُtْqٱ", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَوِ", "translit": "ِwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱطْرَحُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُḥَrْṭٱ", "root": "طرح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَرْضًا", "translit": "āًḍْrَaʾ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَخْلُ", "translit": "ُlْhkَy", "root": "خلو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَجْهُ", "translit": "ُhْjgَw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَبِيكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkyِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَتَكُونُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnwُkَtَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَعْدِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قَوْمًا", "translit": "āًmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "صَٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "قَالَ قَآئِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ لَا تَقْتُلُوا۟ يُوسُفَ وَأَلْقُوهُ فِى غَيَٰبَتِ ٱلْجُبِّ يَلْتَقِطْهُ بَعْضُ ٱلسَّيَّارَةِ إِن كُنتُمْ فَٰعِلِينَ ", "translation": "Said a speaker among them, \"Do not kill Joseph but throw him into the bottom of the well; some travelers will pick him up - if you would do [something].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَآئِلٌ", "translit": "ٌlِyʾٓāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَقْتُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُtْqَt", "root": "قتل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَلْقُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُqْlَaʾَw", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "غَيَٰبَتِ", "translit": "ِtَbَٰyَغ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْجُبِّ", "translit": "ِّbُjgْlٱ", "root": "جبب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَلْتَقِطْهُ", "translit": "ُhْṭِqَtْlَy", "root": "لقط"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بَعْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلسَّيَّارَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrāَّyَّslٱ", "root": "سير"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَٰعِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِʿعَٰf", "root": "فعل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَا مَا لَكَ لَا تَأْمَ۫نَّا عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ وَإِنَّا لَهُۥ لَنَٰصِحُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"O our father, why do you not entrust us with Joseph while indeed, we are to him sincere counselors?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَأْمَ۫نَّا", "translit": "āَّnَ۫mْaʾَt", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَنَٰصِحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥِṣَٰnَl", "root": "نصح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "أَرْسِلْهُ مَعَنَا غَدًا يَرْتَعْ وَيَلْعَبْ وَإِنَّا لَهُۥ لَحَٰفِظُونَ ", "translation": "Send him with us tomorrow that he may eat well and play. And indeed, we will be his guardians.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَرْسِلْهُ", "translit": "ُhْlِsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَعَنَا", "translit": "āَnَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "غَدًا", "translit": "āًdَغ", "root": "غدو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَرْتَعْ", "translit": "ْʿعَtْrَy", "root": "رتع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَيَلْعَبْ", "translit": "ْbَʿعْlَyَw", "root": "لعب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَحَٰفِظُونَ", "translit": "َnwُẓِfَٰḥَl", "root": "حفظ"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "قَالَ إِنِّى لَيَحْزُنُنِىٓ أَن تَذْهَبُوا۟ بِهِۦ وَأَخَافُ أَن يَأْكُلَهُ ٱلذِّئْبُ وَأَنتُمْ عَنْهُ غَٰفِلُونَ ", "translation": "[Jacob] said, \"Indeed, it saddens me that you should take him, and I fear that a wolf would eat him while you are of him unaware.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَيَحْزُنُنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnُnُzْḥَyَl", "root": "حزن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَذْهَبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَhْhdَt", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَaʾَw", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَأْكُلَهُ", "translit": "ُhَlُkْaʾَy", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلذِّئْبُ", "translit": "ُbْyʾِّhdlٱ", "root": "ذاب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَأَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "غَٰفِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِfَٰغ", "root": "غفل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "قَالُوا۟ لَئِنْ أَكَلَهُ ٱلذِّئْبُ وَنَحْنُ عُصْبَةٌ إِنَّآ إِذًا لَّخَٰسِرُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"If a wolf should eat him while we are a [strong] clan, indeed, we would then be losers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَئِنْ", "translit": "ْnِyʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَكَلَهُ", "translit": "ُhَlَkَaʾ", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلذِّئْبُ", "translit": "ُbْyʾِّhdlٱ", "root": "ذاب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عُصْبَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَbْṣُʿع", "root": "عصب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِذًا", "translit": "āًhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَّخَٰسِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِsَٰhkَّl", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "فَلَمَّا ذَهَبُوا۟ بِهِۦ وَأَجْمَعُوٓا۟ أَن يَجْعَلُوهُ فِى غَيَٰبَتِ ٱلْجُبِّۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَيْهِ لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُم بِأَمْرِهِمْ هَٰذَا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ", "translation": "So when they took him [out] and agreed to put him into the bottom of the well...[1] But We inspired to him, \"You will surely inform them [someday] about this affair of theirs while they do not perceive [your identity].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذَهَبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَhَhd", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَأَجْمَعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعَmْjgَaʾَw", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَجْعَلُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُlَʿعْjgَy", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "غَيَٰبَتِ", "translit": "ِtَbَٰyَغ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْجُبِّ", "translit": "ِّbُjgْlٱ", "root": "جبب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَوْحَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَḥْwَaʾَw", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَتُنَبِّئَنَّهُم", "translit": "mُhَّnَyʾِّbَnُtَl", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِأَمْرِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِrْmَaʾِb", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "يَشْعُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُʿعْhsَy", "root": "شعر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "وَجَآءُوٓ أَبَاهُمْ عِشَآءً يَبْكُونَ ", "translation": "And they came to their father at night, weeping.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَآءُوٓ", "translit": "ٓwُءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَبَاهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِشَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَhsِʿع", "root": "عشو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَبْكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkْbَy", "root": "بكي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَآ إِنَّا ذَهَبْنَا نَسْتَبِقُ وَتَرَكْنَا يُوسُفَ عِندَ مَتَٰعِنَا فَأَكَلَهُ ٱلذِّئْبُۖ وَمَآ أَنتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لَّنَا وَلَوْ كُنَّا صَٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"O our father, indeed we went racing each other and left Joseph with our possessions, and a wolf ate him. But you would not believe us, even if we were truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذَهَبْنَا", "translit": "āَnْbَhَhd", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَسْتَبِقُ", "translit": "ُqِbَtْsَn", "root": "سبق"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَتَرَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَrَtَw", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَتَٰعِنَا", "translit": "āَnِʿعَٰtَm", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَأَكَلَهُ", "translit": "ُhَlَkَaʾَf", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلذِّئْبُ", "translit": "ُbْyʾِّhdlٱ", "root": "ذاب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِمُؤْمِنٍ", "translit": "ٍnِmْwʾُmِb", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "صَٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَٰṣ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَجَآءُو عَلَىٰ قَمِيصِهِۦ بِدَمٍ كَذِبٍۚ قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًاۖ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيلٌۖ وَٱللَّهُ ٱلْمُسْتَعَانُ عَلَىٰ مَا تَصِفُونَ ", "translation": "And they brought upon his shirt false blood.[1] [Jacob] said, \"Rather, your souls have enticed you to something, so patience is most fitting. And Allāh is the one sought for help against that which you describe.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَآءُو", "translit": "wُءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَمِيصِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِṣyِmَq", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِدَمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَdِb", "root": "دمو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَذِبٍ", "translit": "ٍbِhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَوَّلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَّwَs", "root": "سول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَنفُسُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُsُfnَaʾ", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَمْرًا", "translit": "āًrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَصَبْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْbَṣَf", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "جَمِيلٌ", "translit": "ٌlyِmَjg", "root": "جمل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْتَعَانُ", "translit": "ُnāَʿعَtْsُmْlٱ", "root": "عون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تَصِفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfِṣَt", "root": "وصف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَجَآءَتْ سَيَّارَةٌ فَأَرْسَلُوا۟ وَارِدَهُمْ فَأَدْلَىٰ دَلْوَهُۥۖ قَالَ يَٰبُشْرَىٰ هَٰذَا غُلَٰمٌۚ وَأَسَرُّوهُ بِضَٰعَةًۚ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌۢ بِمَا يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "And there came a company of travelers; then they sent their water drawer, and he let down his bucket. He said, \"Good news! Here is a boy.\" And they concealed him, [taking him] as merchandise;[1] and Allāh was Knowing of what they did.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَآءَتْ", "translit": "ْtَءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَيَّارَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrāَّyَs", "root": "سير"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَأَرْسَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَارِدَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَdِrāَw", "root": "ورد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَأَدْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْdَaʾَf", "root": "دلو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دَلْوَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَwْlَd", "root": "دلو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَٰبُشْرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrْhsُbَٰy", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "غُلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlُغ", "root": "غلم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَأَسَرُّوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُّrَsَaʾَw", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِضَٰعَةً", "translit": "ًẗَʿعَٰḍِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "وَشَرَوْهُ بِثَمَنٍۭ بَخْسٍ دَرَٰهِمَ مَعْدُودَةٍ وَكَانُوا۟ فِيهِ مِنَ ٱلزَّٰهِدِينَ ", "translation": "And they sold him for a reduced price - a few dirhams - and they were, concerning him, of those content with little.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَشَرَوْهُ", "translit": "ُhْwَrَhsَw", "root": "شري"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِثَمَنٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnَmَhtِb", "root": "ثمن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَخْسٍ", "translit": "ٍsْhkَb", "root": "بخس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "دَرَٰهِمَ", "translit": "َmِhَٰrَd", "root": "درهم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَعْدُودَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَdwُdْʿعَm", "root": "عدد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَكَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلزَّٰهِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِhَّٰzlٱ", "root": "زهد"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِى ٱشْتَرَىٰهُ مِن مِّصْرَ لِٱمْرَأَتِهِۦٓ أَكْرِمِى مَثْوَىٰهُ عَسَىٰٓ أَن يَنفَعَنَآ أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُۥ وَلَدًاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوسُفَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلِنُعَلِّمَهُۥ مِن تَأْوِيلِ ٱلْأَحَادِيثِۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَالِبٌ عَلَىٰٓ أَمْرِهِۦ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And the one from Egypt[1] who bought him said to his wife, \"Make his residence comfortable. Perhaps he will benefit us, or we will adopt him as a son.\" And thus, We established Joseph in the land that We might teach him the interpretation of events [i.e., dreams]. And Allāh is predominant over His affair, but most of the people do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱشْتَرَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَrَtْhsٱ", "root": "شري"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّصْرَ", "translit": "َrْṣِّm", "root": "مصر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِٱمْرَأَتِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِtَaʾَrْmٱِl", "root": "مرا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْرِمِى", "translit": "àِmِrْkَaʾ", "root": "كرم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَثْوَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَwْhtَm", "root": "ثوي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَsَʿع", "root": "عسي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَنفَعَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَʿعَfnَy", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَتَّخِذَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَhdِhkَّtَn", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَدًا", "translit": "āًdَlَw", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مَكَّنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَّkَm", "root": "مكن"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لِيُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُyِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَلِنُعَلِّمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmِّlَʿعُnِlَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "تَأْوِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِwْaʾَt", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحَادِيثِ", "translit": "ِhtyِdāَḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "غَالِبٌ", "translit": "ٌbِlāَغ", "root": "غلب"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "أَمْرِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "وَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُۥٓ ءَاتَيْنَٰهُ حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "And when he [i.e., Joseph] reached maturity, We gave him judgement and knowledge. And thus We reward the doers of good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلَغَ", "translit": "َغَlَb", "root": "بلغ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَشُدَّهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَّdُhsَaʾ", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حُكْمًا", "translit": "āًmْkُḥ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَعِلْمًا", "translit": "āًmْlِʿعَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "وَرَٰوَدَتْهُ ٱلَّتِى هُوَ فِى بَيْتِهَا عَن نَّفْسِهِۦ وَغَلَّقَتِ ٱلْأَبْوَٰبَ وَقَالَتْ هَيْتَ لَكَۚ قَالَ مَعَاذَ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّهُۥ رَبِّىٓ أَحْسَنَ مَثْوَاىَۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يُفْلِحُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ", "translation": "And she, in whose house he was, sought to seduce him. She closed the doors and said, \"Come, you.\" He said, \"[I seek] the refuge of Allāh. Indeed, he[1] is my master, who has made good my residence. Indeed, wrongdoers will not succeed.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَرَٰوَدَتْهُ", "translit": "ُhْtَdَwَٰrَw", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيْتِهَا", "translit": "āَhِtْyَb", "root": "بيت"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَغَلَّقَتِ", "translit": "ِtَqَّlَغَw", "root": "غلق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَبْوَٰبَ", "translit": "َbَٰwْbَaʾْlٱ", "root": "بوب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَقَالَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "هَيْتَ", "translit": "َtْyَh", "root": "هيت"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَعَاذَ", "translit": "َhdāَʿعَm", "root": "عوذ"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مَثْوَاىَ", "translit": "َàāَwْhtَm", "root": "ثوي"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يُفْلِحُ", "translit": "ُḥِlْfُy", "root": "فلح"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "وَلَقَدْ هَمَّتْ بِهِۦۖ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوْلَآ أَن رَّءَا بُرْهَٰنَ رَبِّهِۦۚ كَذَٰلِكَ لِنَصْرِفَ عَنْهُ ٱلسُّوٓءَ وَٱلْفَحْشَآءَۚ إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ ", "translation": "And she certainly determined [to seduce] him, and he would have inclined to her had he not seen the proof [i.e., sign] of his Lord. And thus [it was] that We should avert from him evil and immorality. Indeed, he was of Our chosen servants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَمَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّmَh", "root": "همم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَهَمَّ", "translit": "َّmَhَw", "root": "همم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهَا", "translit": "āَhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "رَّءَا", "translit": "āَءَّr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بُرْهَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰhْrُb", "root": "برهن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لِنَصْرِفَ", "translit": "َfِrْṣَnِl", "root": "صرف"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلسُّوٓءَ", "translit": "َءٓwُّslٱ", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَٱلْفَحْشَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَhsْḥَfْlٱَw", "root": "فحش"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "عِبَادِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdāَbِʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ", "translit": "َnyِṣَlْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خلص"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "وَٱسْتَبَقَا ٱلْبَابَ وَقَدَّتْ قَمِيصَهُۥ مِن دُبُرٍ وَأَلْفَيَا سَيِّدَهَا لَدَا ٱلْبَابِۚ قَالَتْ مَا جَزَآءُ مَنْ أَرَادَ بِأَهْلِكَ سُوٓءًا إِلَّآ أَن يُسْجَنَ أَوْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "And they both raced to the door, and she tore his shirt from the back, and they found her husband at the door. She said, \"What is the recompense of one who intended evil for your wife but that he be imprisoned or a painful punishment?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَبَقَا", "translit": "āَqَbَtْsٱَw", "root": "سبق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْبَابَ", "translit": "َbāَbْlٱ", "root": "بوب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَقَدَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّdَqَw", "root": "قدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَمِيصَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَṣyِmَq", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُبُرٍ", "translit": "ٍrُbُd", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَلْفَيَا", "translit": "āَyَfْlَaʾَw", "root": "لفو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَيِّدَهَا", "translit": "āَhَdِّyَs", "root": "سود"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَدَا", "translit": "āَdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْبَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَbْlٱ", "root": "بوب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَالَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "جَزَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَzَjg", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَرَادَ", "translit": "َdāَrَaʾ", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بِأَهْلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlْhَaʾِb", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "سُوٓءًا", "translit": "āًءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يُسْجَنَ", "translit": "َnَjgْsُy", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "عَذَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَaʾ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "قَالَ هِىَ رَٰوَدَتْنِى عَن نَّفْسِىۚ وَشَهِدَ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْ أَهْلِهَآ إِن كَانَ قَمِيصُهُۥ قُدَّ مِن قُبُلٍ فَصَدَقَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ ", "translation": "[Joseph] said, \"It was she who sought to seduce me.\" And a witness from her family testified, \"If his shirt is torn from the front, then she has told the truth, and he is of the liars.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَٰوَدَتْنِى", "translit": "àِnْtَdَwَٰr", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَّفْسِى", "translit": "àِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَشَهِدَ", "translit": "َdِhَhsَw", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شَاهِدٌ", "translit": "ٌdِhāَhs", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَهْلِهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhِlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَمِيصُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُṣyِmَq", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قُدَّ", "translit": "َّdُq", "root": "قدد"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "قُبُلٍ", "translit": "ٍlُbُq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَصَدَقَتْ", "translit": "ْtَqَdَṣَf", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِhdَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "وَإِن كَانَ قَمِيصُهُۥ قُدَّ مِن دُبُرٍ فَكَذَبَتْ وَهُوَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "But if his shirt is torn from the back, then she has lied, and he is of the truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَمِيصُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُṣyِmَq", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قُدَّ", "translit": "َّdُq", "root": "قدد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُبُرٍ", "translit": "ٍrُbُd", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَكَذَبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَhdَkَf", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "فَلَمَّا رَءَا قَمِيصَهُۥ قُدَّ مِن دُبُرٍ قَالَ إِنَّهُۥ مِن كَيْدِكُنَّۖ إِنَّ كَيْدَكُنَّ عَظِيمٌ ", "translation": "So when he [i.e., her husband] saw his shirt torn from the back, he said, \"Indeed, it is of your [i.e., women's] plan. Indeed, your plan is great [i.e., vehement].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَءَا", "translit": "āَءَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَمِيصَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَṣyِmَq", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قُدَّ", "translit": "َّdُq", "root": "قدد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "دُبُرٍ", "translit": "ٍrُbُd", "root": "دبر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كَيْدِكُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُkِdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَيْدَكُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُkَdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَظِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "يُوسُفُ أَعْرِضْ عَنْ هَٰذَاۚ وَٱسْتَغْفِرِى لِذَنۢبِكِۖ إِنَّكِ كُنتِ مِنَ ٱلْخَاطِـِٔينَ ", "translation": "Joseph, ignore this.[1] And, [my wife], ask forgiveness for your sin. Indeed, you were of the sinful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَعْرِضْ", "translit": "ْḍِrْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عرض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَنْ", "translit": "ْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱسْتَغْفِرِى", "translit": "àِrِfْغَtْsٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِذَنۢبِكِ", "translit": "ِkِbۢnَhdِl", "root": "ذنب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّكِ", "translit": "ِkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنتِ", "translit": "ِtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْخَاطِـِٔينَ", "translit": "َnyِٔـِṭāَhkْlٱ", "root": "خطا"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "وَقَالَ نِسْوَةٌ فِى ٱلْمَدِينَةِ ٱمْرَأَتُ ٱلْعَزِيزِ تُرَٰوِدُ فَتَىٰهَا عَن نَّفْسِهِۦۖ قَدْ شَغَفَهَا حُبًّاۖ إِنَّا لَنَرَىٰهَا فِى ضَلَٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "And women in the city said, \"The wife of al-ʿAzeez is seeking to seduce her slave boy; he has impassioned her with love. Indeed, we see her [to be] in clear error.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نِسْوَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَwْsِn", "root": "نسو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَدِينَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَnyِdَmْlٱ", "root": "مدن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱمْرَأَتُ", "translit": "ُtَaʾَrْmٱ", "root": "مرا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزِ", "translit": "ِzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تُرَٰوِدُ", "translit": "ُdِwَٰrُt", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَتَىٰهَا", "translit": "āَhٰàَtَf", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شَغَفَهَا", "translit": "āَhَfَغَhs", "root": "شغف"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "حُبًّا", "translit": "āًّbُḥ", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَنَرَىٰهَا", "translit": "āَhٰàَrَnَl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "فَلَمَّا سَمِعَتْ بِمَكْرِهِنَّ أَرْسَلَتْ إِلَيْهِنَّ وَأَعْتَدَتْ لَهُنَّ مُتَّكَـًٔا وَءَاتَتْ كُلَّ وَٰحِدَةٍ مِّنْهُنَّ سِكِّينًا وَقَالَتِ ٱخْرُجْ عَلَيْهِنَّۖ فَلَمَّا رَأَيْنَهُۥٓ أَكْبَرْنَهُۥ وَقَطَّعْنَ أَيْدِيَهُنَّ وَقُلْنَ حَٰشَ لِلَّهِ مَا هَٰذَا بَشَرًا إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا مَلَكٌ كَرِيمٌ ", "translation": "So when she heard of their scheming, she sent for them and prepared for them a banquet and gave each one of them a knife and said [to Joseph], \"Come out before them.\" And when they saw him, they greatly admired him and cut their hands[1] and said, \"Perfect is Allāh![2] This is not a man; this is none but a noble angel.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَمِعَتْ", "translit": "ْtَʿعِmَs", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمَكْرِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِrْkَmِb", "root": "مكر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَرْسَلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَعْتَدَتْ", "translit": "ْtَdَtْʿعَaʾَw", "root": "عتد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُتَّكَـًٔا", "translit": "āًٔـَkَّtُm", "root": "وكا"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَءَاتَتْ", "translit": "ْtَtāَءَw", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كُلَّ", "translit": "َّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَٰحِدَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَdِḥَٰw", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مِّنْهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سِكِّينًا", "translit": "āًnyِّkِs", "root": "سكن"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَقَالَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱخْرُجْ", "translit": "ْjgُrْhkٱ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "رَأَيْنَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَnْyَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَكْبَرْنَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَnْrَbْkَaʾ", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَقَطَّعْنَ", "translit": "َnْʿعَّṭَqَw", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَيْدِيَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَقُلْنَ", "translit": "َnْlُqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "حَٰشَ", "translit": "َhsَٰḥ", "root": "حوش"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "بَشَرًا", "translit": "āًrَhsَb", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "مَلَكٌ", "translit": "ٌkَlَm", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "كَرِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِrَk", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "قَالَتْ فَذَٰلِكُنَّ ٱلَّذِى لُمْتُنَّنِى فِيهِۖ وَلَقَدْ رَٰوَدتُّهُۥ عَن نَّفْسِهِۦ فَٱسْتَعْصَمَۖ وَلَئِن لَّمْ يَفْعَلْ مَآ ءَامُرُهُۥ لَيُسْجَنَنَّ وَلَيَكُونًا مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰغِرِينَ ", "translation": "She said, \"That is the one about whom you blamed me. And I certainly sought to seduce him, but he firmly refused; and if he will not do what I order him, he will surely be imprisoned and will be of those debased.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَذَٰلِكُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُkِlَٰhdَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لُمْتُنَّنِى", "translit": "àِnَّnُtْmُl", "root": "لوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَٰوَدتُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّtdَwَٰr", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَٱسْتَعْصَمَ", "translit": "َmَṣْʿعَtْsٱَf", "root": "عصم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَلَئِن", "translit": "nِyʾَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَفْعَلْ", "translit": "ْlَʿعْfَy", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ءَامُرُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُrُmāَء", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَيُسْجَنَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَnَjgْsُyَl", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَلَيَكُونًا", "translit": "āًnwُkَyَlَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰغِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِغَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صغر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "قَالَ رَبِّ ٱلسِّجْنُ أَحَبُّ إِلَىَّ مِمَّا يَدْعُونَنِىٓ إِلَيْهِۖ وَإِلَّا تَصْرِفْ عَنِّى كَيْدَهُنَّ أَصْبُ إِلَيْهِنَّ وَأَكُن مِّنَ ٱلْجَٰهِلِينَ ", "translation": "He said, \"My Lord, prison is more to my liking than that to which they invite me. And if You do not avert from me their plan, I might incline toward them and [thus] be of the ignorant.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنُ", "translit": "ُnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَحَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَḥَaʾ", "root": "حبب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَدْعُونَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَnwُʿعْdَy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَإِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "تَصْرِفْ", "translit": "ْfِrْṣَt", "root": "صرف"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَنِّى", "translit": "àِّnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَيْدَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَصْبُ", "translit": "ُbْṣَaʾ", "root": "صبو"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَأَكُن", "translit": "nُkَaʾَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْجَٰهِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِhَٰjgْlٱ", "root": "جهل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "فَٱسْتَجَابَ لَهُۥ رَبُّهُۥ فَصَرَفَ عَنْهُ كَيْدَهُنَّۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ", "translation": "So his Lord responded to him and averted from him their plan. Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Knowing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱسْتَجَابَ", "translit": "َbāَjgَtْsٱَf", "root": "جوب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَصَرَفَ", "translit": "َfَrَṣَf", "root": "صرف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَيْدَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمِيعُ", "translit": "ُʿعyِmَّslٱ", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِlَʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "ثُمَّ بَدَا لَهُم مِّنۢ بَعْدِ مَا رَأَوُا۟ ٱلْءَايَٰتِ لَيَسْجُنُنَّهُۥ حَتَّىٰ حِينٍ ", "translation": "Then it appeared to them after they had seen the signs[1] that he [i.e., al-ʿAzeez] should surely imprison him for a time.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَدَا", "translit": "āَdَb", "root": "بدو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَأَوُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwَaʾَr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْءَايَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰyāَءْlٱ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَيَسْجُنُنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnُnُjgْsَyَl", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "حِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِḥ", "root": "حين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "وَدَخَلَ مَعَهُ ٱلسِّجْنَ فَتَيَانِۖ قَالَ أَحَدُهُمَآ إِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰنِىٓ أَعْصِرُ خَمْرًاۖ وَقَالَ ٱلْءَاخَرُ إِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰنِىٓ أَحْمِلُ فَوْقَ رَأْسِى خُبْزًا تَأْكُلُ ٱلطَّيْرُ مِنْهُۖ نَبِّئْنَا بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦٓۖ إِنَّا نَرَىٰكَ مِنَ ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "And there entered the prison with him two young men. One of them said, \"Indeed, I have seen myself [in a dream] pressing [grapes for] wine.\" The other said, \"Indeed, I have seen myself carrying upon my head [some] bread, from which the birds were eating. Inform us of its interpretation; indeed, we see you to be of those who do good.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَدَخَلَ", "translit": "َlَhkَdَw", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَعَهُ", "translit": "ُhَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنَ", "translit": "َnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَتَيَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَyَtَf", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَحَدُهُمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmُhُdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَرَىٰنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnٰàَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَعْصِرُ", "translit": "ُrِṣْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عصر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "خَمْرًا", "translit": "āًrْmَhk", "root": "خمر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرُ", "translit": "ُrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَرَىٰنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnٰàَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَحْمِلُ", "translit": "ُlِmْḥَaʾ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَوْقَ", "translit": "َqْwَf", "root": "فوق"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "رَأْسِى", "translit": "àِsْaʾَr", "root": "راس"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "خُبْزًا", "translit": "āًzْbُhk", "root": "خبز"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "تَأْكُلُ", "translit": "ُlُkْaʾَt", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلطَّيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَّṭlٱ", "root": "طير"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مِنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "نَبِّئْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyʾِّbَn", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِlyِwْaʾَtِb", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "نَرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrَn", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "قَالَ لَا يَأْتِيكُمَا طَعَامٌ تُرْزَقَانِهِۦٓ إِلَّا نَبَّأْتُكُمَا بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦ قَبْلَ أَن يَأْتِيَكُمَاۚ ذَٰلِكُمَا مِمَّا عَلَّمَنِى رَبِّىٓۚ إِنِّى تَرَكْتُ مِلَّةَ قَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَهُم بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ هُمْ كَٰفِرُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"You will not receive food that is provided to you except that I will inform you of its interpretation before it comes to you. That is from what my Lord has taught me. Indeed, I have left the religion of a people who do not believe in Allāh, and they, in the Hereafter, are disbelievers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَأْتِيكُمَا", "translit": "āَmُkyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "طَعَامٌ", "translit": "ٌmāَʿعَṭ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تُرْزَقَانِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِnāَqَzْrُt", "root": "رزق"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَبَّأْتُكُمَا", "translit": "āَmُkُtْaʾَّbَn", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlyِwْaʾَtِb", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قَبْلَ", "translit": "َlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَأْتِيَكُمَا", "translit": "āَmُkَyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكُمَا", "translit": "āَmُkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَّمَنِى", "translit": "àِnَmَّlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "تَرَكْتُ", "translit": "ُtْkَrَt", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِلَّةَ", "translit": "َẗَّlِm", "root": "ملل"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "لَّا", "translit": "āَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَهُم", "translit": "mُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱِb", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "كَٰفِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِfَٰk", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "وَٱتَّبَعْتُ مِلَّةَ ءَابَآءِىٓ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ وَإِسْحَٰقَ وَيَعْقُوبَۚ مَا كَانَ لَنَآ أَن نُّشْرِكَ بِٱللَّهِ مِن شَىْءٍۚ ذَٰلِكَ مِن فَضْلِ ٱللَّهِ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلَى ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَشْكُرُونَ ", "translation": "And I have followed the religion of my fathers, Abraham, Isaac and Jacob. And it was not for us to associate anything with Allāh. That is from the favor of Allāh upon us and upon the people, but most of the people are not grateful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱتَّبَعْتُ", "translit": "ُtْʿعَbَّtٱَw", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِلَّةَ", "translit": "َẗَّlِm", "root": "ملل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَابَآءِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِءٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَإِسْحَٰقَ", "translit": "َqَٰḥْsِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَيَعْقُوبَ", "translit": "َbwُqْʿعَyَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "نُّشْرِكَ", "translit": "َkِrْhsُّn", "root": "شرك"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "فَضْلِ", "translit": "ِlْḍَf", "root": "فضل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَعَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "يَشْكُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُkْhsَy", "root": "شكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "يَٰصَىٰحِبَىِ ٱلسِّجْنِ ءَأَرْبَابٌ مُّتَفَرِّقُونَ خَيْرٌ أَمِ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْوَٰحِدُ ٱلْقَهَّارُ ", "translation": "O [my] two companions of prison, are separate lords better or Allāh, the One,[1] the Prevailing?[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰصَىٰحِبَىِ", "translit": "ِàَbِḥٰàَṣَٰy", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنِ", "translit": "ِnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَأَرْبَابٌ", "translit": "ٌbāَbْrَaʾَء", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُّتَفَرِّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِّrَfَtُّm", "root": "فرق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَمِ", "translit": "ِmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْوَٰحِدُ", "translit": "ُdِḥَٰwْlٱ", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْقَهَّارُ", "translit": "ُrāَّhَqْlٱ", "root": "قهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "مَا تَعْبُدُونَ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَسْمَآءً سَمَّيْتُمُوهَآ أَنتُمْ وَءَابَآؤُكُم مَّآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ بِهَا مِن سُلْطَٰنٍۚ إِنِ ٱلْحُكْمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِۚ أَمَرَ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوٓا۟ إِلَّآ إِيَّاهُۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلْقَيِّمُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "You worship not besides Him except [mere] names you have named them,[1] you and your fathers, for which Allāh has sent down no evidence. Legislation is not but for Allāh. He has commanded that you worship not except Him. That is the correct religion, but most of the people do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "دُونِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَسْمَآءً", "translit": "ًءٓāَmْsَaʾ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "سَمَّيْتُمُوهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhwُmُtْyَّmَs", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَءَابَآؤُكُم", "translit": "mُkُwʾٓāَbāَءَw", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَنزَلَ", "translit": "َlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِهَا", "translit": "āَhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "سُلْطَٰنٍ", "translit": "ٍnَٰṭْlُs", "root": "سلط"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "إِنِ", "translit": "ِnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْحُكْمُ", "translit": "ُmْkُḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أَمَرَ", "translit": "َrَmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "إِيَّاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَّyِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينُ", "translit": "ُnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْقَيِّمُ", "translit": "ُmِّyَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "يَٰصَىٰحِبَىِ ٱلسِّجْنِ أَمَّآ أَحَدُكُمَا فَيَسْقِى رَبَّهُۥ خَمْرًاۖ وَأَمَّا ٱلْءَاخَرُ فَيُصْلَبُ فَتَأْكُلُ ٱلطَّيْرُ مِن رَّأْسِهِۦۚ قُضِىَ ٱلْأَمْرُ ٱلَّذِى فِيهِ تَسْتَفْتِيَانِ ", "translation": "O two companions of prison, as for one of you, he will give drink to his master of wine; but as for the other, he will be crucified, and the birds will eat from his head. The matter has been decreed about which you both inquire.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰصَىٰحِبَىِ", "translit": "ِàَbِḥٰàَṣَٰy", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنِ", "translit": "ِnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَحَدُكُمَا", "translit": "āَmُkُdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَيَسْقِى", "translit": "àِqْsَyَf", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خَمْرًا", "translit": "āًrْmَhk", "root": "خمر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرُ", "translit": "ُrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَيُصْلَبُ", "translit": "ُbَlْṣُyَf", "root": "صلب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَتَأْكُلُ", "translit": "ُlُkْaʾَtَf", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلطَّيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَّṭlٱ", "root": "طير"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "رَّأْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْaʾَّr", "root": "راس"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "قُضِىَ", "translit": "َàِḍُq", "root": "قضي"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمْرُ", "translit": "ُrْmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "تَسْتَفْتِيَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَyِtْfَtْsَt", "root": "فتي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "وَقَالَ لِلَّذِى ظَنَّ أَنَّهُۥ نَاجٍ مِّنْهُمَا ٱذْكُرْنِى عِندَ رَبِّكَ فَأَنسَىٰهُ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ ذِكْرَ رَبِّهِۦ فَلَبِثَ فِى ٱلسِّجْنِ بِضْعَ سِنِينَ ", "translation": "And he said to the one whom he knew would go free, \"Mention me before your master.\" But Satan made him forget the mention [to] his master, and he [i.e., Joseph] remained in prison several years.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ظَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَاجٍ", "translit": "ٍjgāَn", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنْهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱذْكُرْنِى", "translit": "àِnْrُkْhdٱ", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عِندَ", "translit": "َdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَأَنسَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَsnَaʾَf", "root": "نسي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰṭْyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ذِكْرَ", "translit": "َrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَبِّهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فَلَبِثَ", "translit": "َhtِbَlَf", "root": "لبث"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنِ", "translit": "ِnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "بِضْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْḍِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "سِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِs", "root": "سنو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلْمَلِكُ إِنِّىٓ أَرَىٰ سَبْعَ بَقَرَٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَأْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَسَبْعَ سُنۢبُلَٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَأُخَرَ يَابِسَٰتٍۖ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْمَلَأُ أَفْتُونِى فِى رُءْيَٰىَ إِن كُنتُمْ لِلرُّءْيَا تَعْبُرُونَ ", "translation": "And [subsequently] the king said, \"Indeed, I have seen [in a dream] seven fat cows being eaten by seven [that were] lean, and seven green spikes [of grain] and others [that were] dry. O eminent ones, explain to me my vision, if you should interpret visions.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَبْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَقَرَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰrَqَb", "root": "بقر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "سِمَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَmِs", "root": "سمن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَأْكُلُهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhُlُkْaʾَy", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "سَبْعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عِجَافٌ", "translit": "ٌfāَjgِʿع", "root": "عجف"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "وَسَبْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْbَsَw", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "سُنۢبُلَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰlُbۢnُs", "root": "سنبل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "خُضْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْḍُhk", "root": "خضر"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَأُخَرَ", "translit": "َrَhkُaʾَw", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يَابِسَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰsِbāَy", "root": "يبس"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَأُ", "translit": "ُaʾَlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملا"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَفْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْfَaʾ", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "رُءْيَٰىَ", "translit": "َàَٰyْءُr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "لِلرُّءْيَا", "translit": "āَyْءُّrlِl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "تَعْبُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 44, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ أَضْغَٰثُ أَحْلَٰمٍۖ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِتَأْوِيلِ ٱلْأَحْلَٰمِ بِعَٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"[It is but] a mixture of false dreams, and we are not learned in the interpretation of dreams.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَضْغَٰثُ", "translit": "ُhtَٰغْḍَaʾ", "root": "ضغث"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَحْلَٰمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَٰlْḥَaʾ", "root": "حلم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِتَأْوِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِwْaʾَtِb", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحْلَٰمِ", "translit": "ِmَٰlْḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حلم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بِعَٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَٰʿعِb", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 45, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِى نَجَا مِنْهُمَا وَٱدَّكَرَ بَعْدَ أُمَّةٍ أَنَا۠ أُنَبِّئُكُم بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦ فَأَرْسِلُونِ ", "translation": "But the one who was freed and remembered after a time said, \"I will inform you of its interpretation, so send me forth.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَجَا", "translit": "āَjgَn", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْهُمَا", "translit": "āَmُhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَٱدَّكَرَ", "translit": "َrَkَّdٱَw", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَعْدَ", "translit": "َdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أُمَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّmُaʾ", "root": "امم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أُنَبِّئُكُم", "translit": "mُkُyʾِّbَnُaʾ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "بِتَأْوِيلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlyِwْaʾَtِb", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَأَرْسِلُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُlِsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 46, "text": "يُوسُفُ أَيُّهَا ٱلصِّدِّيقُ أَفْتِنَا فِى سَبْعِ بَقَرَٰتٍ سِمَانٍ يَأْكُلُهُنَّ سَبْعٌ عِجَافٌ وَسَبْعِ سُنۢبُلَٰتٍ خُضْرٍ وَأُخَرَ يَابِسَٰتٍ لَّعَلِّىٓ أَرْجِعُ إِلَى ٱلنَّاسِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "[He said], \"Joseph, O man of truth, explain to us about seven fat cows eaten by seven [that were] lean, and seven green spikes [of grain] and others [that were] dry - that I may return to the people [i.e., the king and his court]; perhaps they will know [about you].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلصِّدِّيقُ", "translit": "ُqyِّdِّṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَفْتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtْfَaʾ", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبْعِ", "translit": "ِʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَقَرَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰrَqَb", "root": "بقر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سِمَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَmِs", "root": "سمن"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَأْكُلُهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhُlُkْaʾَy", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سَبْعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عِجَافٌ", "translit": "ٌfāَjgِʿع", "root": "عجف"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَسَبْعِ", "translit": "ِʿعْbَsَw", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "سُنۢبُلَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰlُbۢnُs", "root": "سنبل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "خُضْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْḍُhk", "root": "خضر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَأُخَرَ", "translit": "َrَhkُaʾَw", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَابِسَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰsِbāَy", "root": "يبس"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "لَّعَلِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّlَʿعَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَرْجِعُ", "translit": "ُʿعِjgْrَaʾ", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "لَعَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 47, "text": "قَالَ تَزْرَعُونَ سَبْعَ سِنِينَ دَأَبًا فَمَا حَصَدتُّمْ فَذَرُوهُ فِى سُنۢبُلِهِۦٓ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّمَّا تَأْكُلُونَ ", "translation": "[Joseph] said, \"You will plant for seven years consecutively; and what you harvest leave in its spikes, except a little from which you will eat.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَزْرَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَrْzَt", "root": "زرع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَبْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِs", "root": "سنو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "دَأَبًا", "translit": "āًbَaʾَd", "root": "داب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "حَصَدتُّمْ", "translit": "ْmُّtdَṣَḥ", "root": "حصد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَذَرُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُrَhdَf", "root": "وذر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سُنۢبُلِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِlُbۢnُs", "root": "سنبل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَلِيلًا", "translit": "āًlyِlَq", "root": "قلل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِّمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "تَأْكُلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlُkْaʾَt", "root": "اكل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 48, "text": "ثُمَّ يَأْتِى مِنۢ بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ سَبْعٌ شِدَادٌ يَأْكُلْنَ مَا قَدَّمْتُمْ لَهُنَّ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا مِّمَّا تُحْصِنُونَ ", "translation": "Then will come after that seven difficult [years] which will consume what you advanced [i.e., saved] for them, except a little from which you will store.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَأْتِى", "translit": "àِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَبْعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعْbَs", "root": "سبع"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شِدَادٌ", "translit": "ٌdāَdِhs", "root": "شدد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَأْكُلْنَ", "translit": "َnْlُkْaʾَy", "root": "اكل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَدَّمْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْmَّdَq", "root": "قدم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "قَلِيلًا", "translit": "āًlyِlَq", "root": "قلل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِّمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "تُحْصِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِṣْḥُt", "root": "حصن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 49, "text": "ثُمَّ يَأْتِى مِنۢ بَعْدِ ذَٰلِكَ عَامٌ فِيهِ يُغَاثُ ٱلنَّاسُ وَفِيهِ يَعْصِرُونَ ", "translation": "Then will come after that a year in which the people will be given rain and in which they will press [olives and grapes].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَأْتِى", "translit": "àِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَامٌ", "translit": "ٌmāَʿع", "root": "عوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يُغَاثُ", "translit": "ُhtāَغُy", "root": "غيث"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسُ", "translit": "ُsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَفِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِfَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يَعْصِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِṣْʿعَy", "root": "عصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 50, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلْمَلِكُ ٱئْتُونِى بِهِۦۖ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُ ٱلرَّسُولُ قَالَ ٱرْجِعْ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَسْـَٔلْهُ مَا بَالُ ٱلنِّسْوَةِ ٱلَّٰتِى قَطَّعْنَ أَيْدِيَهُنَّۚ إِنَّ رَبِّى بِكَيْدِهِنَّ عَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "And the king said, \"Bring him to me.\" But when the messenger came to him, [Joseph] said, \"Return to your master and ask him what is the case of the women who cut their hands. Indeed, my Lord is Knowing of their plan.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱئْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْyʾٱ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جَآءَهُ", "translit": "ُhَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلرَّسُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُsَّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱرْجِعْ", "translit": "ْʿعِjgْrٱ", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَسْـَٔلْهُ", "translit": "ُhْlَٔـْsَf", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بَالُ", "translit": "ُlāَb", "root": "بول"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلنِّسْوَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَwْsِّnlٱ", "root": "نسو"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلَّٰتِى", "translit": "àِtَّٰlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قَطَّعْنَ", "translit": "َnْʿعَّṭَq", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَيْدِيَهُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُhَyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِكَيْدِهِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِhِdْyَkِb", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 51, "text": "قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ إِذْ رَٰوَدتُّنَّ يُوسُفَ عَن نَّفْسِهِۦۚ قُلْنَ حَٰشَ لِلَّهِ مَا عَلِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ مِن سُوٓءٍۚ قَالَتِ ٱمْرَأَتُ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْـَٰٔنَ حَصْحَصَ ٱلْحَقُّ أَنَا۠ رَٰوَدتُّهُۥ عَن نَّفْسِهِۦ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَمِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "Said [the king to the women], \"What was your condition when you sought to seduce Joseph?\" They said, \"Perfect is Allāh![1] We know about him no evil.\" The wife of al-ʿAzeez said, \"Now the truth has become evident. It was I who sought to seduce him, and indeed, he is of the truthful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَطْبُكُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُkُbْṭَhk", "root": "خطب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَٰوَدتُّنَّ", "translit": "َّnُّtdَwَٰr", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قُلْنَ", "translit": "َnْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حَٰشَ", "translit": "َhsَٰḥ", "root": "حوش"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلِمْنَا", "translit": "āَnْmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "سُوٓءٍ", "translit": "ٍءٓwُs", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قَالَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱمْرَأَتُ", "translit": "ُtَaʾَrْmٱ", "root": "مرا"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزِ", "translit": "ِzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْـَٰٔنَ", "translit": "َnَٰٔـْlٱ", "root": "اون"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "حَصْحَصَ", "translit": "َṣَḥْṣَḥ", "root": "حصحص"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "ٱلْحَقُّ", "translit": "ُّqَḥْlٱ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "رَٰوَدتُّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُّtdَwَٰr", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "نَّفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 52, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ لِيَعْلَمَ أَنِّى لَمْ أَخُنْهُ بِٱلْغَيْبِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهْدِى كَيْدَ ٱلْخَآئِنِينَ ", "translation": "That is so he [i.e., al-ʿAzeez] will know that I did not betray him in [his] absence and that Allāh does not guide the plan of betrayers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِيَعْلَمَ", "translit": "َmَlْʿعَyِl", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنِّى", "translit": "àِّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَخُنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnُhkَaʾ", "root": "خون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱِb", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "يَهْدِى", "translit": "àِdْhَy", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَيْدَ", "translit": "َdْyَk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْخَآئِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِyʾٓāَhkْlٱ", "root": "خون"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 53, "text": "وَمَآ أُبَرِّئُ نَفْسِىٓۚ إِنَّ ٱلنَّفْسَ لَأَمَّارَةٌۢ بِٱلسُّوٓءِ إِلَّا مَا رَحِمَ رَبِّىٓۚ إِنَّ رَبِّى غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ", "translation": "And I do not acquit myself. Indeed, the soul is a persistent enjoiner of evil, except those upon which my Lord has mercy. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving and Merciful.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أُبَرِّئُ", "translit": "ُyʾِّrَbُaʾ", "root": "برا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَفْسِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلنَّفْسَ", "translit": "َsْfَّnlٱ", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَأَمَّارَةٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢẗَrāَّmَaʾَl", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلسُّوٓءِ", "translit": "ِءٓwُّslٱِb", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَحِمَ", "translit": "َmِḥَr", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "غَفُورٌ", "translit": "ٌrwُfَغ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "رَّحِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِḥَّr", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 54, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلْمَلِكُ ٱئْتُونِى بِهِۦٓ أَسْتَخْلِصْهُ لِنَفْسِىۖ فَلَمَّا كَلَّمَهُۥ قَالَ إِنَّكَ ٱلْيَوْمَ لَدَيْنَا مَكِينٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "And the king said, \"Bring him to me; I will appoint him exclusively for myself.\" And when he spoke to him, he said, \"Indeed, you are today established [in position] and trusted.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلِكُ", "translit": "ُkِlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱئْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْyʾٱ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَسْتَخْلِصْهُ", "translit": "ُhْṣِlْhkَtْsَaʾ", "root": "خلص"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِنَفْسِى", "translit": "àِsْfَnِl", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَلَّمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmَّlَk", "root": "كلم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱ", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَدَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مَكِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِkَm", "root": "مكن"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 55, "text": "قَالَ ٱجْعَلْنِى عَلَىٰ خَزَآئِنِ ٱلْأَرْضِۖ إِنِّى حَفِيظٌ عَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "[Joseph] said, \"Appoint me over the storehouses of the land. Indeed, I will be a knowing guardian.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱجْعَلْنِى", "translit": "àِnْlَʿعْjgٱ", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خَزَآئِنِ", "translit": "ِnِyʾٓāَzَhk", "root": "خزن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "حَفِيظٌ", "translit": "ٌẓyِfَḥ", "root": "حفظ"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 56, "text": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ مَكَّنَّا لِيُوسُفَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ يَتَبَوَّأُ مِنْهَا حَيْثُ يَشَآءُۚ نُصِيبُ بِرَحْمَتِنَا مَن نَّشَآءُۖ وَلَا نُضِيعُ أَجْرَ ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "And thus We established Joseph in the land to settle therein wherever he willed. We touch with Our mercy whom We will, and We do not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَكَّنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَّkَm", "root": "مكن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِيُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُyِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَتَبَوَّأُ", "translit": "ُaʾَّwَbَtَy", "root": "بوا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "حَيْثُ", "translit": "ُhtْyَḥ", "root": "حيث"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "نُصِيبُ", "translit": "ُbyِṣُn", "root": "صوب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِرَحْمَتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَmْḥَrِb", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَّشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَّn", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "نُضِيعُ", "translit": "ُʿعyِḍُn", "root": "ضيع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَجْرَ", "translit": "َrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 57, "text": "وَلَأَجْرُ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَكَانُوا۟ يَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "And the reward of the Hereafter is better for those who believed and were fearing Allāh.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَأَجْرُ", "translit": "ُrْjgَaʾَlَw", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لِّلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَكَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَkَw", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 58, "text": "وَجَآءَ إِخْوَةُ يُوسُفَ فَدَخَلُوا۟ عَلَيْهِ فَعَرَفَهُمْ وَهُمْ لَهُۥ مُنكِرُونَ ", "translation": "And the brothers of Joseph came [seeking food], and they entered upon him; and he recognized them, but he was to them unknown.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِخْوَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَwْhkِiʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَدَخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkَdَf", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَعَرَفَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَfَrَʿعَf", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُنكِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِknُm", "root": "نكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 59, "text": "وَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمْ قَالَ ٱئْتُونِى بِأَخٍ لَّكُم مِّنْ أَبِيكُمْۚ أَلَا تَرَوْنَ أَنِّىٓ أُوفِى ٱلْكَيْلَ وَأَنَا۠ خَيْرُ ٱلْمُنزِلِينَ ", "translation": "And when he had furnished them with their supplies, he said, \"Bring me a brother of yours from your father.[1] Do you not see that I give full measure and that I am the best of accommodators?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَهَّزَهُم", "translit": "mُhَzَّhَjg", "root": "جهز"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِجَهَازِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِzāَhَjgِb", "root": "جهز"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱئْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْyʾٱ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِأَخٍ", "translit": "ٍhkَaʾِb", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَبِيكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkyِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَرَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أُوفِى", "translit": "àِfwُaʾ", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلْكَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَkْlٱ", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَأَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "خَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنزِلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlِznُmْlٱ", "root": "نزل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 60, "text": "فَإِن لَّمْ تَأْتُونِى بِهِۦ فَلَا كَيْلَ لَكُمْ عِندِى وَلَا تَقْرَبُونِ ", "translation": "But if you do not bring him to me, no measure will there be [hereafter] for you from me, nor will you approach me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَأْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَk", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عِندِى", "translit": "àِdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "تَقْرَبُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُbَrْqَt", "root": "قرب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 61, "text": "قَالُوا۟ سَنُرَٰوِدُ عَنْهُ أَبَاهُ وَإِنَّا لَفَٰعِلُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"We will attempt to dissuade his father from [keeping] him, and indeed, we will do [it].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَنُرَٰوِدُ", "translit": "ُdِwَٰrُnَs", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَبَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَفَٰعِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِʿعَٰfَl", "root": "فعل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 62, "text": "وَقَالَ لِفِتْيَٰنِهِ ٱجْعَلُوا۟ بِضَٰعَتَهُمْ فِى رِحَالِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَعْرِفُونَهَآ إِذَا ٱنقَلَبُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰٓ أَهْلِهِمْ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُونَ ", "translation": "And [Joseph] said to his servants, \"Put their merchandise[1] into their saddlebags so they might recognize it when they have gone back to their people that perhaps they will [again] return.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِفِتْيَٰنِهِ", "translit": "ِhِnَٰyْtِfِl", "root": "فتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱجْعَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَʿعْjgٱ", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِضَٰعَتَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَtَʿعَٰḍِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رِحَالِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlāَḥِr", "root": "رحل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَعَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَعْرِفُونَهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhَnwُfِrْʿعَy", "root": "عرف"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱنقَلَبُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُbَlَqnٱ", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَهْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَعَلَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَرْجِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِjgْrَy", "root": "رجع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 63, "text": "فَلَمَّا رَجَعُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰٓ أَبِيهِمْ قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَا مُنِعَ مِنَّا ٱلْكَيْلُ فَأَرْسِلْ مَعَنَآ أَخَانَا نَكْتَلْ وَإِنَّا لَهُۥ لَحَٰفِظُونَ ", "translation": "So when they returned to their father, they said, \"O our father, [further] measure has been denied to us, so send with us our brother [that] we will be given measure. And indeed, we will be his guardians.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَجَعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعَjgَr", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَبِيهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhyِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُنِعَ", "translit": "َʿعِnُm", "root": "منع"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْكَيْلُ", "translit": "ُlْyَkْlٱ", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَأَرْسِلْ", "translit": "ْlِsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَعَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَخَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَكْتَلْ", "translit": "ْlَtْkَn", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَحَٰفِظُونَ", "translit": "َnwُẓِfَٰḥَl", "root": "حفظ"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 64, "text": "قَالَ هَلْ ءَامَنُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ إِلَّا كَمَآ أَمِنتُكُمْ عَلَىٰٓ أَخِيهِ مِن قَبْلُۖ فَٱللَّهُ خَيْرٌ حَٰفِظًاۖ وَهُوَ أَرْحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Should I entrust you with him except [under coercion] as I entrusted you with his brother before? But Allāh is the best guardian, and He is the most merciful of the merciful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَمِنتُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُtnِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَf", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "حَٰفِظًا", "translit": "āًẓِfَٰḥ", "root": "حفظ"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَرْحَمُ", "translit": "ُmَḥْrَaʾ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِḥَّٰrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 65, "text": "وَلَمَّا فَتَحُوا۟ مَتَٰعَهُمْ وَجَدُوا۟ بِضَٰعَتَهُمْ رُدَّتْ إِلَيْهِمْۖ قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَا مَا نَبْغِىۖ هَٰذِهِۦ بِضَٰعَتُنَا رُدَّتْ إِلَيْنَاۖ وَنَمِيرُ أَهْلَنَا وَنَحْفَظُ أَخَانَا وَنَزْدَادُ كَيْلَ بَعِيرٍۖ ذَٰلِكَ كَيْلٌ يَسِيرٌ ", "translation": "And when they opened their baggage, they found their merchandise returned to them. They said, \"O our father, what [more] could we desire? This is our merchandise returned to us. And we will obtain supplies [i.e., food] for our family and protect our brother and obtain an increase of a camel's load; that is an easy measurement.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَتَحُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḥَtَf", "root": "فتح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَتَٰعَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَʿعَٰtَm", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَجَدُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُdَjgَw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِضَٰعَتَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَtَʿعَٰḍِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رُدَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّdُr", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "نَبْغِى", "translit": "àِغْbَn", "root": "بغي"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "هَٰذِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِضَٰعَتُنَا", "translit": "āَnُtَʿعَٰḍِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "رُدَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّdُr", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَنَمِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِmَnَw", "root": "مير"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَهْلَنَا", "translit": "āَnَlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَنَحْفَظُ", "translit": "ُẓَfْḥَnَw", "root": "حفظ"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "أَخَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَنَزْدَادُ", "translit": "ُdāَdْzَnَw", "root": "زيد"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "كَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَk", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "بَعِيرٍ", "translit": "ٍryِʿعَb", "root": "بعر"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "كَيْلٌ", "translit": "ٌlْyَk", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "يَسِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِsَy", "root": "يسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 66, "text": "قَالَ لَنْ أُرْسِلَهُۥ مَعَكُمْ حَتَّىٰ تُؤْتُونِ مَوْثِقًا مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ لَتَأْتُنَّنِى بِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن يُحَاطَ بِكُمْۖ فَلَمَّآ ءَاتَوْهُ مَوْثِقَهُمْ قَالَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ مَا نَقُولُ وَكِيلٌ ", "translation": "[Jacob] said, \"Never will I send him with you until you give me a promise [i.e., oath] by Allāh that you will bring him [back] to me, unless you should be surrounded [i.e., overcome by enemies].\" And when they had given their promise, he said, \"Allāh, over what we say, is Entrusted.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَنْ", "translit": "ْnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أُرْسِلَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَlِsْrُaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَعَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تُؤْتُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُtْwʾُt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَوْثِقًا", "translit": "āًqِhtْwَm", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَتَأْتُنَّنِى", "translit": "àِnَّnُtْaʾَtَl", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يُحَاطَ", "translit": "َṭāَḥُy", "root": "حوط"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَلَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ءَاتَوْهُ", "translit": "ُhْwَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مَوْثِقَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَqِhtْwَm", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "نَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَn", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "وَكِيلٌ", "translit": "ٌlyِkَw", "root": "وكل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 67, "text": "وَقَالَ يَٰبَنِىَّ لَا تَدْخُلُوا۟ مِنۢ بَابٍ وَٰحِدٍ وَٱدْخُلُوا۟ مِنْ أَبْوَٰبٍ مُّتَفَرِّقَةٍۖ وَمَآ أُغْنِى عَنكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَىْءٍۖ إِنِ ٱلْحُكْمُ إِلَّا لِلَّهِۖ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُۖ وَعَلَيْهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ ٱلْمُتَوَكِّلُونَ ", "translation": "And he said, \"O my sons, do not enter from one gate but enter from different gates; and I cannot avail you against [the decree of] Allāh at all. The decision is only for Allāh; upon Him I have relied, and upon Him let those who would rely [indeed] rely.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰبَنِىَّ", "translit": "َّàِnَbَٰy", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَدْخُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُhkْdَt", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَb", "root": "بوب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٰحِدٍ", "translit": "ٍdِḥَٰw", "root": "وحد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَٱدْخُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُhkْdٱَw", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَبْوَٰبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَٰwْbَaʾ", "root": "بوب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُّتَفَرِّقَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَqِّrَfَtُّm", "root": "فرق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أُغْنِى", "translit": "àِnْغُaʾ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَنكُم", "translit": "mُknَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "إِنِ", "translit": "ِnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْحُكْمُ", "translit": "ُmْkُḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "تَوَكَّلْتُ", "translit": "ُtْlَّkَwَt", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "وَعَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿعَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ", "translit": "ِlَّkَwَtَyْlَf", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱلْمُتَوَكِّلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِّkَwَtُmْlٱ", "root": "وكل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 68, "text": "وَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا۟ مِنْ حَيْثُ أَمَرَهُمْ أَبُوهُم مَّا كَانَ يُغْنِى عَنْهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن شَىْءٍ إِلَّا حَاجَةً فِى نَفْسِ يَعْقُوبَ قَضَىٰهَاۚ وَإِنَّهُۥ لَذُو عِلْمٍ لِّمَا عَلَّمْنَٰهُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And when they entered from where their father had ordered them, it did not avail them against Allāh at all except [it was] a need [i.e., concern] within the soul of Jacob, which he satisfied. And indeed, he was a possessor of knowledge because of what We had taught him, but most of the people do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkَd", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حَيْثُ", "translit": "ُhtْyَḥ", "root": "حيث"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَمَرَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَrَmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَبُوهُم", "translit": "mُhwُbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُغْنِى", "translit": "àِnْغُy", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَنْهُم", "translit": "mُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "حَاجَةً", "translit": "ًẗَjgāَḥ", "root": "حوج"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "نَفْسِ", "translit": "ِsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يَعْقُوبَ", "translit": "َbwُqْʿعَy", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "قَضَىٰهَا", "translit": "āَhٰàَḍَq", "root": "قضي"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لَذُو", "translit": "wُhdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "عِلْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "لِّمَا", "translit": "āَmِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "عَلَّمْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْmَّlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "أَكْثَرَ", "translit": "َrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "يَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 69, "text": "وَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا۟ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ ءَاوَىٰٓ إِلَيْهِ أَخَاهُۖ قَالَ إِنِّىٓ أَنَا۠ أَخُوكَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "And when they entered upon Joseph, he took his brother to himself; he said, \"Indeed, I am your brother, so do not despair over what they used to do [to me].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkَd", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَاوَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَwāَء", "root": "اوي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَخَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَخُوكَ", "translit": "َkwُhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَبْتَئِسْ", "translit": "ْsِyʾَtْbَt", "root": "باس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 70, "text": "فَلَمَّا جَهَّزَهُم بِجَهَازِهِمْ جَعَلَ ٱلسِّقَايَةَ فِى رَحْلِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ أَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ أَيَّتُهَا ٱلْعِيرُ إِنَّكُمْ لَسَٰرِقُونَ ", "translation": "So when he had furnished them with their supplies, he put the [gold measuring] bowl into the bag of his brother. Then an announcer called out, \"O caravan, indeed you are thieves.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَهَّزَهُم", "translit": "mُhَzَّhَjg", "root": "جهز"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِجَهَازِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِzāَhَjgِb", "root": "جهز"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَعَلَ", "translit": "َlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسِّقَايَةَ", "translit": "َẗَyāَqِّslٱ", "root": "سقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَحْلِ", "translit": "ِlْḥَr", "root": "رحل"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَذَّنَ", "translit": "َnَّhdَaʾ", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُؤَذِّنٌ", "translit": "ٌnِّhdَwʾُm", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَيَّتُهَا", "translit": "āَhُtَّyَaʾ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْعِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عير"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَسَٰرِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِrَٰsَl", "root": "سرق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 71, "text": "قَالُوا۟ وَأَقْبَلُوا۟ عَلَيْهِم مَّاذَا تَفْقِدُونَ ", "translation": "They said while approaching them, \"What is it you are missing?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَأَقْبَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَbْqَaʾَw", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَفْقِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِqْfَt", "root": "فقد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 72, "text": "قَالُوا۟ نَفْقِدُ صُوَاعَ ٱلْمَلِكِ وَلِمَن جَآءَ بِهِۦ حِمْلُ بَعِيرٍ وَأَنَا۠ بِهِۦ زَعِيمٌ ", "translation": "They said, \"We are missing the measure of the king. And for he who produces it is [the reward of] a camel's load, and I am responsible for it.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَفْقِدُ", "translit": "ُdِqْfَn", "root": "فقد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "صُوَاعَ", "translit": "َʿعāَwُṣ", "root": "صوع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلِكِ", "translit": "ِkِlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلِمَن", "translit": "nَmِlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "حِمْلُ", "translit": "ُlْmِḥ", "root": "حمل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَعِيرٍ", "translit": "ٍryِʿعَb", "root": "بعر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "زَعِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِʿعَz", "root": "زعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 73, "text": "قَالُوا۟ تَٱللَّهِ لَقَدْ عَلِمْتُم مَّا جِئْنَا لِنُفْسِدَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا كُنَّا سَٰرِقِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"By Allāh, you have certainly known that we did not come to cause corruption in the land, and we have not been thieves.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلِمْتُم", "translit": "mُtْmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "جِئْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyʾِjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لِنُفْسِدَ", "translit": "َdِsْfُnِl", "root": "فسد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "سَٰرِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِrَٰs", "root": "سرق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 74, "text": "قَالُوا۟ فَمَا جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥٓ إِن كُنتُمْ كَٰذِبِينَ ", "translation": "They [the accusers] said, \"Then what would be its recompense[1] if you should be liars?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhُwʾَٰٓzَjg", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَٰذِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِhdَٰk", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 75, "text": "قَالُوا۟ جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥ مَن وُجِدَ فِى رَحْلِهِۦ فَهُوَ جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِى ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "[The brothers] said, \"Its recompense is that he in whose bag it is found - he [himself] will be its recompense.[1] Thus do we recompense the wrongdoers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُwʾَٰٓzَjg", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وُجِدَ", "translit": "َdِjgُw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَحْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْḥَr", "root": "رحل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "جَزَٰٓؤُهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhُwʾَٰٓzَjg", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "نَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَn", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 76, "text": "فَبَدَأَ بِأَوْعِيَتِهِمْ قَبْلَ وِعَآءِ أَخِيهِ ثُمَّ ٱسْتَخْرَجَهَا مِن وِعَآءِ أَخِيهِۚ كَذَٰلِكَ كِدْنَا لِيُوسُفَۖ مَا كَانَ لِيَأْخُذَ أَخَاهُ فِى دِينِ ٱلْمَلِكِ إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ ٱللَّهُۚ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجَٰتٍ مَّن نَّشَآءُۗ وَفَوْقَ كُلِّ ذِى عِلْمٍ عَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "So he began [the search] with their bags before the bag of his brother; then he extracted it from the bag of his brother. Thus did We plan for Joseph. He could not have taken his brother within the religion [i.e., law] of the king except that Allāh willed. We raise in degrees whom We will, but over every possessor of knowledge is one [more] knowing.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَبَدَأَ", "translit": "َaʾَdَbَf", "root": "بدا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَوْعِيَتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtَyِʿعْwَaʾِb", "root": "وعي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "قَبْلَ", "translit": "َlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وِعَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَʿعِw", "root": "وعي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱسْتَخْرَجَهَا", "translit": "āَhَjgَrْhkَtْsٱ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وِعَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَʿعِw", "root": "وعي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كِدْنَا", "translit": "āَnْdِk", "root": "كيد"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لِيُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُyِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لِيَأْخُذَ", "translit": "َhdُhkْaʾَyِl", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَخَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "دِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِd", "root": "دين"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلِكِ", "translit": "ِkِlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "إِلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يَشَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "نَرْفَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَfْrَn", "root": "رفع"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "دَرَجَٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَٰjgَrَd", "root": "درج"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "مَّن", "translit": "nَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "نَّشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَّn", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "وَفَوْقَ", "translit": "َqْwَfَw", "root": "فوق"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "ذِى", "translit": "àِhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "عِلْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 77, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ إِن يَسْرِقْ فَقَدْ سَرَقَ أَخٌ لَّهُۥ مِن قَبْلُۚ فَأَسَرَّهَا يُوسُفُ فِى نَفْسِهِۦ وَلَمْ يُبْدِهَا لَهُمْۚ قَالَ أَنتُمْ شَرٌّ مَّكَانًاۖ وَٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَصِفُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"If he steals - a brother of his has stolen before.\" But Joseph kept it within himself and did not reveal it to them.[1] He said, \"You are worse in position, and Allāh is most knowing of what you describe.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَسْرِقْ", "translit": "ْqِrْsَy", "root": "سرق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَرَقَ", "translit": "َqَrَs", "root": "سرق"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَخٌ", "translit": "ٌhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَأَسَرَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّrَsَaʾَf", "root": "سرر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَفْسِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِsْfَn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُبْدِهَا", "translit": "āَhِdْbُy", "root": "بدو"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "شَرٌّ", "translit": "ٌّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مَّكَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَkَّm", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "تَصِفُونَ", "translit": "َnwُfِṣَt", "root": "وصف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 78, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْعَزِيزُ إِنَّ لَهُۥٓ أَبًا شَيْخًا كَبِيرًا فَخُذْ أَحَدَنَا مَكَانَهُۥٓۖ إِنَّا نَرَىٰكَ مِنَ ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"O ʿAzeez,[1] indeed he has a father [who is] an old man, so take one of us in place of him. Indeed, we see you as a doer of good.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَبًا", "translit": "āًbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شَيْخًا", "translit": "āًhkْyَhs", "root": "شيخ"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَبِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِbَk", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَخُذْ", "translit": "ْhdُhkَf", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَحَدَنَا", "translit": "āَnَdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَكَانَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَnāَkَm", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrَn", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 79, "text": "قَالَ مَعَاذَ ٱللَّهِ أَن نَّأْخُذَ إِلَّا مَن وَجَدْنَا مَتَٰعَنَا عِندَهُۥٓ إِنَّآ إِذًا لَّظَٰلِمُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"[I seek] the refuge of Allāh [to prevent] that we take except him with whom we found our possession. Indeed, we would then be unjust.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَعَاذَ", "translit": "َhdāَʿعَm", "root": "عوذ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَّأْخُذَ", "translit": "َhdُhkْaʾَّn", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَجَدْنَا", "translit": "āَnْdَjgَw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَتَٰعَنَا", "translit": "āَnَʿعَٰtَm", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عِندَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَdnِʿع", "root": "عند"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِذًا", "translit": "āًhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَّظَٰلِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِlَٰẓَّl", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 80, "text": "فَلَمَّا ٱسْتَيْـَٔسُوا۟ مِنْهُ خَلَصُوا۟ نَجِيًّاۖ قَالَ كَبِيرُهُمْ أَلَمْ تَعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّ أَبَاكُمْ قَدْ أَخَذَ عَلَيْكُم مَّوْثِقًا مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَمِن قَبْلُ مَا فَرَّطتُمْ فِى يُوسُفَۖ فَلَنْ أَبْرَحَ ٱلْأَرْضَ حَتَّىٰ يَأْذَنَ لِىٓ أَبِىٓ أَوْ يَحْكُمَ ٱللَّهُ لِىۖ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ ٱلْحَٰكِمِينَ ", "translation": "So when they had despaired of him, they secluded themselves in private consultation. The eldest of them said, \"Do you not know that your father has taken upon you an oath by Allāh and [that] before you failed in [your duty to] Joseph? So I will never leave [this] land until my father permits me or Allāh decides for me,[1] and He is the best of judges.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱسْتَيْـَٔسُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُsَٔـْyَtْsٱ", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خَلَصُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُṣَlَhk", "root": "خلص"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نَجِيًّا", "translit": "āًّyِjgَn", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَبِيرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُryِbَk", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَبَاكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkāَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَخَذَ", "translit": "َhdَhkَaʾ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُم", "translit": "mُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مَّوْثِقًا", "translit": "āًqِhtْwَّm", "root": "وثق"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "وَمِن", "translit": "nِmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "فَرَّطتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtṭَّrَf", "root": "فرط"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "فَلَنْ", "translit": "ْnَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "أَبْرَحَ", "translit": "َḥَrْbَaʾ", "root": "برح"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضَ", "translit": "َḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "يَأْذَنَ", "translit": "َnَhdْaʾَy", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "لِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "أَبِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "يَحْكُمَ", "translit": "َmُkْḥَy", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "خَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "ٱلْحَٰكِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِkَٰḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 81, "text": "ٱرْجِعُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰٓ أَبِيكُمْ فَقُولُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَآ إِنَّ ٱبْنَكَ سَرَقَ وَمَا شَهِدْنَآ إِلَّا بِمَا عَلِمْنَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِلْغَيْبِ حَٰفِظِينَ ", "translation": "Return to your father and say, 'O our father, indeed your son has stolen, and we did not testify except to what we knew. And we were not witnesses of the unseen.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱرْجِعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعِjgْrٱ", "root": "رجع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَبِيكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkyِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَقُولُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlwُqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱبْنَكَ", "translit": "َkَnْbٱ", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "سَرَقَ", "translit": "َqَrَs", "root": "سرق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "شَهِدْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْdِhَhs", "root": "شهد"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلِمْنَا", "translit": "āَnْmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "لِلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlِl", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "حَٰفِظِينَ", "translit": "َnyِẓِfَٰḥ", "root": "حفظ"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 82, "text": "وَسْـَٔلِ ٱلْقَرْيَةَ ٱلَّتِى كُنَّا فِيهَا وَٱلْعِيرَ ٱلَّتِىٓ أَقْبَلْنَا فِيهَاۖ وَإِنَّا لَصَٰدِقُونَ ", "translation": "And ask the city in which we were and the caravan in which we came - and indeed, we are truthful.'\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَسْـَٔلِ", "translit": "ِlَٔـْsَw", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْقَرْيَةَ", "translit": "َẗَyْrَqْlٱ", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَٱلْعِيرَ", "translit": "َryِʿعْlٱَw", "root": "عير"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَقْبَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَbْqَaʾ", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "لَصَٰدِقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqِdَٰṣَl", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 83, "text": "قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًاۖ فَصَبْرٌ جَمِيلٌۖ عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَأْتِيَنِى بِهِمْ جَمِيعًاۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ ", "translation": "[Jacob] said, \"Rather, your souls have enticed you to something, so patience is most fitting. Perhaps Allāh will bring them to me all together. Indeed, it is He who is the Knowing, the Wise.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَوَّلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَّwَs", "root": "سول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنفُسُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُsُfnَaʾ", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَمْرًا", "translit": "āًrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَصَبْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْbَṣَf", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "جَمِيلٌ", "translit": "ٌlyِmَjg", "root": "جمل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَسَى", "translit": "àَsَʿع", "root": "عسي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "يَأْتِيَنِى", "translit": "àِnَyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "بِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "جَمِيعًا", "translit": "āًʿعyِmَjg", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِlَʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 84, "text": "وَتَوَلَّىٰ عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يَٰٓأَسَفَىٰ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ وَٱبْيَضَّتْ عَيْنَاهُ مِنَ ٱلْحُزْنِ فَهُوَ كَظِيمٌ ", "translation": "And he turned away from them and said, \"Oh, my sorrow over Joseph,\" and his eyes became white[1] from grief, for he was [of that] a suppressor.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَوَلَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّlَwَtَw", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَنْهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَسَفَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَfَsَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "اسف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَٱبْيَضَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّḍَyْbٱَw", "root": "بيض"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَيْنَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَnْyَʿع", "root": "عين"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلْحُزْنِ", "translit": "ِnْzُḥْlٱ", "root": "حزن"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَظِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِẓَk", "root": "كظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 85, "text": "قَالُوا۟ تَٱللَّهِ تَفْتَؤُا۟ تَذْكُرُ يُوسُفَ حَتَّىٰ تَكُونَ حَرَضًا أَوْ تَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْهَٰلِكِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"By Allāh, you will not cease remembering Joseph until you become fatally ill or become of those who perish.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَفْتَؤُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwʾَtْfَt", "root": "فتا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَذْكُرُ", "translit": "ُrُkْhdَt", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "حَرَضًا", "translit": "āًḍَrَḥ", "root": "حرض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "تَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْهَٰلِكِينَ", "translit": "َnyِkِlَٰhْlٱ", "root": "هلك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 86, "text": "قَالَ إِنَّمَآ أَشْكُوا۟ بَثِّى وَحُزْنِىٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَأَعْلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"I only complain of my suffering and my grief to Allāh, and I know from Allāh that which you do not know.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَشْكُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُkْhsَaʾ", "root": "شكو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَثِّى", "translit": "àِّhtَb", "root": "بثث"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَحُزْنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnْzُḥَw", "root": "حزن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 87, "text": "يَٰبَنِىَّ ٱذْهَبُوا۟ فَتَحَسَّسُوا۟ مِن يُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ وَلَا تَا۟يْـَٔسُوا۟ مِن رَّوْحِ ٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَا يَا۟يْـَٔسُ مِن رَّوْحِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلْقَوْمُ ٱلْكَٰفِرُونَ ", "translation": "O my sons, go and find out about Joseph and his brother and despair not of relief from Allāh. Indeed, no one despairs of relief from Allāh except the disbelieving people.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰبَنِىَّ", "translit": "َّàِnَbَٰy", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱذْهَبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَhْhdٱ", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَتَحَسَّسُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُsَّsَḥَtَf", "root": "حسس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَأَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾَw", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَا۟يْـَٔسُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُsَٔـْy۟āَt", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَّوْحِ", "translit": "ِḥْwَّr", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَا۟يْـَٔسُ", "translit": "ُsَٔـْy۟āَy", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "رَّوْحِ", "translit": "ِḥْwَّr", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 88, "text": "فَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا۟ عَلَيْهِ قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْعَزِيزُ مَسَّنَا وَأَهْلَنَا ٱلضُّرُّ وَجِئْنَا بِبِضَٰعَةٍ مُّزْجَىٰةٍ فَأَوْفِ لَنَا ٱلْكَيْلَ وَتَصَدَّقْ عَلَيْنَآۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَجْزِى ٱلْمُتَصَدِّقِينَ ", "translation": "So when they entered upon him [i.e., Joseph], they said, \"O ʿAzeez, adversity has touched us and our family, and we have come with goods poor in quality, but give us full measure and be charitable to us. Indeed, Allāh rewards the charitable.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkَd", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَسَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّsَm", "root": "مسس"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَأَهْلَنَا", "translit": "āَnَlْhَaʾَw", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلضُّرُّ", "translit": "ُّrُّḍlٱ", "root": "ضرر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَجِئْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyʾِjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِبِضَٰعَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَʿعَٰḍِbِb", "root": "بضع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مُّزْجَىٰةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗٰàَjgْzُّm", "root": "زجو"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فَأَوْفِ", "translit": "ِfْwَaʾَf", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْكَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَkْlٱ", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "وَتَصَدَّقْ", "translit": "ْqَّdَṣَtَw", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "يَجْزِى", "translit": "àِzْjgَy", "root": "جزي"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "ٱلْمُتَصَدِّقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِّdَṣَtُmْlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 89, "text": "قَالَ هَلْ عَلِمْتُم مَّا فَعَلْتُم بِيُوسُفَ وَأَخِيهِ إِذْ أَنتُمْ جَٰهِلُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Do you know what you did with Joseph and his brother when you were ignorant?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلِمْتُم", "translit": "mُtْmِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَعَلْتُم", "translit": "mُtْlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِيُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُyِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَأَخِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِhkَaʾَw", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "جَٰهِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِhَٰjg", "root": "جهل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 90, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ أَءِنَّكَ لَأَنتَ يُوسُفُۖ قَالَ أَنَا۠ يُوسُفُ وَهَٰذَآ أَخِىۖ قَدْ مَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْنَآۖ إِنَّهُۥ مَن يَتَّقِ وَيَصْبِرْ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"Are you indeed Joseph?\" He said, \"I am Joseph, and this is my brother. Allāh has certainly favored us. Indeed, he who fears Allāh and is patient, then indeed, Allāh does not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَءِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِءَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَأَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يُوسُفُ", "translit": "ُfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَهَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَخِى", "translit": "àِhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَm", "root": "منن"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَتَّقِ", "translit": "ِqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَيَصْبِرْ", "translit": "ْrِbْṣَyَw", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "فَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "يُضِيعُ", "translit": "ُʿعyِḍُy", "root": "ضيع"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "أَجْرَ", "translit": "َrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "ٱلْمُحْسِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِsْḥُmْlٱ", "root": "حسن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 91, "text": "قَالُوا۟ تَٱللَّهِ لَقَدْ ءَاثَرَكَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْنَا وَإِن كُنَّا لَخَٰطِـِٔينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"By Allāh, certainly has Allāh preferred you over us, and indeed, we have been sinners.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَاثَرَكَ", "translit": "َkَrَhtāَء", "root": "اثر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَخَٰطِـِٔينَ", "translit": "َnyِٔـِṭَٰhkَl", "root": "خطا"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 92, "text": "قَالَ لَا تَثْرِيبَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْيَوْمَۖ يَغْفِرُ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمْۖ وَهُوَ أَرْحَمُ ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ ", "translation": "He said, \"No blame will there be upon you today. May Allāh forgive you; and He is the most merciful of the merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَثْرِيبَ", "translit": "َbyِrْhtَt", "root": "ثرب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْيَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَyْlٱ", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَغْفِرُ", "translit": "ُrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَرْحَمُ", "translit": "ُmَḥْrَaʾ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِḥَّٰrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 93, "text": "ٱذْهَبُوا۟ بِقَمِيصِى هَٰذَا فَأَلْقُوهُ عَلَىٰ وَجْهِ أَبِى يَأْتِ بَصِيرًا وَأْتُونِى بِأَهْلِكُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ", "translation": "Take this, my shirt, and cast it over the face of my father; he will become seeing. And bring me your family, all together.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱذْهَبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَhْhdٱ", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِقَمِيصِى", "translit": "àِṣyِmَqِb", "root": "قمص"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَأَلْقُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُqْlَaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَجْهِ", "translit": "ِhْjgَw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَبِى", "translit": "àِbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَأْتِ", "translit": "ِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَصِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِṣَb", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَأْتُونِى", "translit": "àِnwُtْaʾَw", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بِأَهْلِكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkِlْhَaʾِb", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَجْمَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 94, "text": "وَلَمَّا فَصَلَتِ ٱلْعِيرُ قَالَ أَبُوهُمْ إِنِّى لَأَجِدُ رِيحَ يُوسُفَۖ لَوْلَآ أَن تُفَنِّدُونِ ", "translation": "And when the caravan departed [from Egypt], their father said,[1] \"Indeed, I find the smell of Joseph [and would say that he was alive] if you did not think me weakened in mind.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَصَلَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlَṣَf", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِʿعْlٱ", "root": "عير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَبُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَأَجِدُ", "translit": "ُdِjgَaʾَl", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "رِيحَ", "translit": "َḥyِr", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَوْلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "تُفَنِّدُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُdِّnَfُt", "root": "فند"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 95, "text": "قَالُوا۟ تَٱللَّهِ إِنَّكَ لَفِى ضَلَٰلِكَ ٱلْقَدِيمِ ", "translation": "They said, \"By Allāh, indeed you are in your [same] old error.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 96, "text": "فَلَمَّآ أَن جَآءَ ٱلْبَشِيرُ أَلْقَىٰهُ عَلَىٰ وَجْهِهِۦ فَٱرْتَدَّ بَصِيرًاۖ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ إِنِّىٓ أَعْلَمُ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And when the bearer of good tidings[1] arrived, he cast it over his face, and he returned [once again] seeing. He said, \"Did I not tell you that I know from Allāh that which you do not know?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَشِيرُ", "translit": "ُryِhsَbْlٱ", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَلْقَىٰهُ", "translit": "ُhٰàَqْlَaʾ", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَجْهِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِhْjgَw", "root": "وجه"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَٱرْتَدَّ", "translit": "َّdَtْrٱَf", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بَصِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِṣَb", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَقُل", "translit": "lُqَaʾ", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 97, "text": "قَالُوا۟ يَٰٓأَبَانَا ٱسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا خَٰطِـِٔينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"O our father, ask for us forgiveness of our sins; indeed, we have been sinners.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَانَا", "translit": "āَnāَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱسْتَغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغَtْsٱ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذُنُوبَنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَbwُnُhd", "root": "ذنب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "خَٰطِـِٔينَ", "translit": "َnyِٔـِṭَٰhk", "root": "خطا"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 98, "text": "قَالَ سَوْفَ أَسْتَغْفِرُ لَكُمْ رَبِّىٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلْغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "He said, \"I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَs", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَسْتَغْفِرُ", "translit": "ُrِfْغَtْsَaʾ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْغَفُورُ", "translit": "ُrwُfَغْlٱ", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 99, "text": "فَلَمَّا دَخَلُوا۟ عَلَىٰ يُوسُفَ ءَاوَىٰٓ إِلَيْهِ أَبَوَيْهِ وَقَالَ ٱدْخُلُوا۟ مِصْرَ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ ءَامِنِينَ ", "translation": "And when they entered upon Joseph, he took his parents to himself [i.e., embraced them] and said, \"Enter Egypt, Allāh willing, safe [and secure].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَخَلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlَhkَd", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُوسُفَ", "translit": "َfُswُy", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَاوَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَwāَء", "root": "اوي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَبَوَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَwَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱدْخُلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlُhkْdٱ", "root": "دخل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِصْرَ", "translit": "َrْṣِm", "root": "مصر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "شَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ءَامِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmāَء", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 100, "text": "وَرَفَعَ أَبَوَيْهِ عَلَى ٱلْعَرْشِ وَخَرُّوا۟ لَهُۥ سُجَّدًاۖ وَقَالَ يَٰٓأَبَتِ هَٰذَا تَأْوِيلُ رُءْيَٰىَ مِن قَبْلُ قَدْ جَعَلَهَا رَبِّى حَقًّاۖ وَقَدْ أَحْسَنَ بِىٓ إِذْ أَخْرَجَنِى مِنَ ٱلسِّجْنِ وَجَآءَ بِكُم مِّنَ ٱلْبَدْوِ مِنۢ بَعْدِ أَن نَّزَغَ ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ بَيْنِى وَبَيْنَ إِخْوَتِىٓۚ إِنَّ رَبِّى لَطِيفٌ لِّمَا يَشَآءُۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ٱلْحَكِيمُ ", "translation": "And he raised his parents upon the throne, and they bowed to him in prostration.[1] And he said, \"O my father, this is the explanation of my vision of before. My Lord has made it reality. And He was certainly good to me when He took me out of prison and brought you [here] from bedouin life after Satan had induced [estrangement] between me and my brothers. Indeed, my Lord is Subtle[2] in what He wills. Indeed, it is He who is the Knowing, the Wise.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَرَفَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَfَrَw", "root": "رفع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَبَوَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَwَbَaʾ", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَرْشِ", "translit": "ِhsْrَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عرش"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَخَرُّوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُّrَhkَw", "root": "خرر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "سُجَّدًا", "translit": "āًdَّjgُs", "root": "سجد"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَبَتِ", "translit": "ِtَbَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "تَأْوِيلُ", "translit": "ُlyِwْaʾَt", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "رُءْيَٰىَ", "translit": "َàَٰyْءُr", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "قَبْلُ", "translit": "ُlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "جَعَلَهَا", "translit": "āَhَlَʿعَjg", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "حَقًّا", "translit": "āًّqَḥ", "root": "حقق"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "وَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "أَحْسَنَ", "translit": "َnَsْḥَaʾ", "root": "حسن"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "أَخْرَجَنِى", "translit": "àِnَjgَrْhkَaʾ", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "ٱلسِّجْنِ", "translit": "ِnْjgِّslٱ", "root": "سجن"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "وَجَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjgَw", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "بِكُم", "translit": "mُkِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "ٱلْبَدْوِ", "translit": "ِwْdَbْlٱ", "root": "بدو"}, {"id": 30, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 31, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 32, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 33, "arabic": "نَّزَغَ", "translit": "َغَzَّn", "root": "نزغ"}, {"id": 34, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰṭْyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}, {"id": 35, "arabic": "بَيْنِى", "translit": "àِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 36, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 37, "arabic": "إِخْوَتِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِtَwْhkِiʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 38, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 39, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 40, "arabic": "لَطِيفٌ", "translit": "ٌfyِṭَl", "root": "لطف"}, {"id": 41, "arabic": "لِّمَا", "translit": "āَmِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 42, "arabic": "يَشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَy", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 43, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 44, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 45, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِlَʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 46, "arabic": "ٱلْحَكِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِkَḥْlٱ", "root": "حكم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 101, "text": "رَبِّ قَدْ ءَاتَيْتَنِى مِنَ ٱلْمُلْكِ وَعَلَّمْتَنِى مِن تَأْوِيلِ ٱلْأَحَادِيثِۚ فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ أَنتَ وَلِىِّۦ فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلْءَاخِرَةِۖ تَوَفَّنِى مُسْلِمًا وَأَلْحِقْنِى بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "My Lord, You have given me [something] of sovereignty and taught me of the interpretation of dreams. Creator of the heavens and earth, You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter. Cause me to die a Muslim and join me with the righteous.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَاتَيْتَنِى", "translit": "àِnَtْyَtāَء", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُلْكِ", "translit": "ِkْlُmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَعَلَّمْتَنِى", "translit": "àِnَtْmَّlَʿعَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَأْوِيلِ", "translit": "ِlyِwْaʾَt", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْأَحَادِيثِ", "translit": "ِhtyِdāَḥَaʾْlٱ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "فَاطِرَ", "translit": "َrِṭāَf", "root": "فطر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلِىِّۦ", "translit": "ۦِّàِlَw", "root": "ولي"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ٱلدُّنْيَا", "translit": "āَyْnُّdlٱ", "root": "دنو"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱَw", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "تَوَفَّنِى", "translit": "àِnَّfَwَt", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "مُسْلِمًا", "translit": "āًmِlْsُm", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَأَلْحِقْنِى", "translit": "àِnْqِḥْlَaʾَw", "root": "لحق"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱِb", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 102, "text": "ذَٰلِكَ مِنْ أَنۢبَآءِ ٱلْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيْكَۖ وَمَا كُنتَ لَدَيْهِمْ إِذْ أَجْمَعُوٓا۟ أَمْرَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَمْكُرُونَ ", "translation": "That is from the news of the unseen which We reveal, [O Muḥammad], to you. And you were not with them when they put together their plan while they conspired.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنۢبَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَbۢnَaʾ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَيْبِ", "translit": "ِbْyَغْlٱ", "root": "غيب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نُوحِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِḥwُn", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَيْكَ", "translit": "َkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَدَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَdَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "أَجْمَعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَمْرَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَمْكُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُkْmَy", "root": "مكر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 103, "text": "وَمَآ أَكْثَرُ ٱلنَّاسِ وَلَوْ حَرَصْتَ بِمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And most of the people, although you strive [for it], are not believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُ", "translit": "ُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَرَصْتَ", "translit": "َtْṣَrَḥ", "root": "حرص"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmِb", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 104, "text": "وَمَا تَسْـَٔلُهُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۚ إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And you do not ask of them for it any payment. It is not except a reminder to the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَسْـَٔلُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُlَٔـْsَt", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ذِكْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlِّl", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 105, "text": "وَكَأَيِّن مِّنْ ءَايَةٍ فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ يَمُرُّونَ عَلَيْهَا وَهُمْ عَنْهَا مُعْرِضُونَ ", "translation": "And how many a sign within the heavens and earth do they pass over while they, therefrom, are turning away.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكَأَيِّن", "translit": "nِّyَaʾَkَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَايَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَمُرُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّrُmَy", "root": "مرر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَلَيْهَا", "translit": "āَhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَنْهَا", "translit": "āَhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُعْرِضُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḍِrْʿعُm", "root": "عرض"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 106, "text": "وَمَا يُؤْمِنُ أَكْثَرُهُم بِٱللَّهِ إِلَّا وَهُم مُّشْرِكُونَ ", "translation": "And most of them believe not in Allāh except while they associate others with Him.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُ", "translit": "ُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱِb", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَهُم", "translit": "mُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُّشْرِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِrْhsُّm", "root": "شرك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 107, "text": "أَفَأَمِنُوٓا۟ أَن تَأْتِيَهُمْ غَٰشِيَةٌ مِّنْ عَذَابِ ٱللَّهِ أَوْ تَأْتِيَهُمُ ٱلسَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ", "translation": "Then do they feel secure that there will not come to them an overwhelming [aspect] of the punishment of Allāh or that the Hour will not come upon them suddenly while they do not perceive?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَأَمِنُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُnِmَaʾَfَaʾ", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَأْتِيَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَyِtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "غَٰشِيَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَyِhsَٰغ", "root": "غشو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَذَابِ", "translit": "ِbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَأْتِيَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَyِtْaʾَt", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلسَّاعَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَʿعāَّslٱ", "root": "سوع"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَغْتَةً", "translit": "ًẗَtْغَb", "root": "بغت"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "يَشْعُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُʿعْhsَy", "root": "شعر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 108, "text": "قُلْ هَٰذِهِۦ سَبِيلِىٓ أَدْعُوٓا۟ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۚ عَلَىٰ بَصِيرَةٍ أَنَا۠ وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَنِىۖ وَسُبْحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ ", "translation": "Say, \"This is my way; I invite to Allāh with insight, I and those who follow me. And exalted is Allāh; and I am not of those who associate others with Him.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قُلْ", "translit": "ْlُq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَبِيلِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِlyِbَs", "root": "سبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَدْعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعْdَaʾ", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَصِيرَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَryِṣَb", "root": "بصر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "وَمَنِ", "translit": "ِnَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعَنِى", "translit": "àِnَʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَسُبْحَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰḥْbُsَw", "root": "سبح"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ", "translit": "َnyِkِrْhsُmْlٱ", "root": "شرك"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 109, "text": "وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَا مِن قَبْلِكَ إِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوحِىٓ إِلَيْهِم مِّنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْقُرَىٰٓۗ أَفَلَمْ يَسِيرُوا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ فَيَنظُرُوا۟ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْۗ وَلَدَارُ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوْا۟ۗ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ ", "translation": "And We sent not before you [as messengers] except men to whom We revealed from among the people of cities. So have they[1] not traveled through the earth and observed how was the end of those before them? And the home of the Hereafter is best for those who fear Allāh; then will you not reason?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسَلْنَا", "translit": "āَnْlَsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَبْلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رِجَالًا", "translit": "āًlāَjgِr", "root": "رجل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نُّوحِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِḥwُّn", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَهْلِ", "translit": "ِlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَrُqْlٱ", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "أَفَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "يَسِيرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُryِsَy", "root": "سير"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "فَيَنظُرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrُẓnَyَf", "root": "نظر"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "كَيْفَ", "translit": "َfْyَk", "root": "كيف"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "عَٰقِبَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَbِqَٰʿع", "root": "عقب"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "قَبْلِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "وَلَدَارُ", "translit": "ُrāَdَlَw", "root": "دور"}, {"id": 24, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 25, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 26, "arabic": "لِّلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 27, "arabic": "ٱتَّقَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَqَّtٱ", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 28, "arabic": "أَفَلَا", "translit": "āَlَfَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 29, "arabic": "تَعْقِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِqْʿعَt", "root": "عقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 110, "text": "حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا ٱسْتَيْـَٔسَ ٱلرُّسُلُ وَظَنُّوٓا۟ أَنَّهُمْ قَدْ كُذِبُوا۟ جَآءَهُمْ نَصْرُنَا فَنُجِّىَ مَن نَّشَآءُۖ وَلَا يُرَدُّ بَأْسُنَا عَنِ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "[They continued] until, when the messengers despaired and were certain that they had been denied, there came to them Our victory, and whoever We willed was saved. And Our punishment cannot be repelled from the people who are criminals.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱسْتَيْـَٔسَ", "translit": "َsَٔـْyَtْsٱ", "root": "ياس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلرُّسُلُ", "translit": "ُlُsُّrlٱ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَظَنُّوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُّnَẓَw", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "قَدْ", "translit": "ْdَq", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُذِبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbِhdُk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "جَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "نَصْرُنَا", "translit": "āَnُrْṣَn", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فَنُجِّىَ", "translit": "َàِّjgُnَf", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "نَّشَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَhsَّn", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "يُرَدُّ", "translit": "ُّdَrُy", "root": "ردد"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "بَأْسُنَا", "translit": "āَnُsْaʾَb", "root": "باس"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 111, "text": "لَقَدْ كَانَ فِى قَصَصِهِمْ عِبْرَةٌ لِّأُو۟لِى ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِۗ مَا كَانَ حَدِيثًا يُفْتَرَىٰ وَلَٰكِن تَصْدِيقَ ٱلَّذِى بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيلَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ ", "translation": "There was certainly in their stories a lesson for those of understanding. Never was it [i.e., the Qur’ān] a narration invented, but a confirmation of what was before it and a detailed explanation of all things and guidance and mercy for a people who believe.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَصَصِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِṣَṣَq", "root": "قصص"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عِبْرَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَrْbِʿع", "root": "عبر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِّأُو۟لِى", "translit": "àِl۟wُaʾِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَلْبَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰbْlَaʾْlٱ", "root": "لبب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "حَدِيثًا", "translit": "āًhtyِdَḥ", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "يُفْتَرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrَtْfُy", "root": "فري"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "وَلَٰكِن", "translit": "nِkَٰlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "تَصْدِيقَ", "translit": "َqyِdْṣَt", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "بَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "يَدَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَتَفْصِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِṣْfَtَw", "root": "فصل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "شَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhs", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَهُدًى", "translit": "àًdُhَw", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "وَرَحْمَةً", "translit": "ًẗَmْḥَrَw", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 22, "arabic": "لِّقَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَqِّl", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 23, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "الآثار قال ابن لقمان الحكيم لأبيه يا أبت أي الخصال من الإنسان خير قال الدين قال فإذا كانت اثنتين قال الدين والمال قال فإذا كانت ثلاثا قال الدين والمال والحياء قال فإذا كانت أربعا قال الدين والمال والحياء وحسن الخلق قال فإذا كانت خمسا قال الدين والمال والحياء وحسن الخلق والسخاء قال فإذا كانت ستا قال يا بني إذا اجتمعت فيه الخمس خصال فهو نقي تقي والله ولي ومن الشيطان يري وقال الحسن من ساء خلقه عذب نفسه وقال أنس بن مالك إن العبد ليبلغ بحسن خلقه أعلى درجة في الجنة وهو غير عابد ويبلغ", "english": "The Book of Etiquette — and in it [are reports] — and from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \"The Messenger of God — peace and blessings be upon him — was the most beautiful of people in face and the best of them in character.\" (1) And from Abū Masʿūd al-Badrī, who said: \"The Messenger of God — peace and blessings be upon him — used to say in his supplication: 'O God, just as You have made beautiful my creation (khalqī), so make beautiful my character (khuluqī).'\" (2) And from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar — may God be pleased with them both — who said: \"The Messenger of God — peace and blessings be upon him — used to supplicate frequently, saying: 'O God, I ask You for [Page V03P050] soundness, well-being, and good character.'\" (3)", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "section_title_ar": "Section 614", "section_title_en": "The Book of Etiquette (Kitāb al-Ādāb) — Section 614: On Good Character (Ḥusn al-Khulq)", "section_index": 614, "anchors": "- Root: خلق (Kh-L-Q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is \"to measure, proportion, or fashion precisely\" — as the leather-worker measures and cuts hide, or the tailor measures cloth before cutting. Also denotes smoothness (ṣakhrah khalqāʾ: a smooth rock) and worn-out garment (thawb khaliq).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخلق أصله: التقدير المستقيم\" — its origin is \"straight/right measure.\" Used for bringing something into being from nothing (ibdāʿ) without prior model, as in {«He created the heavens and the earth»} (al-Anʿām 6:1), and for bringing something forth from another thing, as in {«He created you from a single soul»} (al-Nisāʾ 4:1). When applied to human character (khuluq), it denotes the inward constitution and disposition — the \"measure\" or \"form\" of the soul.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"خلق الخراز الأديم\" — the leather-worker measured the hide; \"خلق الله الخلق\" — God brought creation into being upon a measure necessitated by wisdom. Metaphorical (majāz): \"وله خلق حسن\" — he has beautiful character, i.e., the inward form of the soul measured upon praiseworthy traits. The term khuluq (character) is a metaphorical extension of khalq (creation/form), referring to the soul's stable constitution just as khalq refers to the body's outward form.\n- Root: حسن (Ḥ-S-N)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Beauty, goodness, excellence — both in outward appearance and inward quality.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الحسن: عبارة عن كل مبهج مرغوب فيه\" — goodness/beauty is an expression of everything delightful and desirable. It is of three kinds: what is deemed good by the intellect, by desire (hawā), and by the senses. \"الحسنة\" (a good deed) is everything that brings joy through a blessing reaching a person.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"أنظر إلى محاسن وجهه\" — look at the beauties of his face (physical beauty). Metaphorical: \"فلان لا يحسن شيئا\" — so-and-so does not do anything well (competence); \"قيمة المرء ما يحسن\" — a man's worth is what he does well. When coupled with khuluq (character), ḥusn al-khuluq denotes the beauty of the soul's inward form — its praiseworthy measure and proportion.\n- Root: حدث (Ḥ-D-Th)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Newness, origination, occurrence. \"الحديث\" — speech that is new/recently originated.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الحدوث: كون الشيء بعد أن لم يكن\" — origination is a thing's coming to be after it was not. \"المحدث: ما أوجد بعد أن لم يكن\" — the originated is what is brought into existence after non-existence. In ḥadīth terminology, it refers to the transmitted sayings of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — reports that convey his words and deeds.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"هو حدث من الأحداث\" — he is young (recent in age). Metaphorical: \"صاروا أحاديث\" — they became subjects of talk. In the context of this section, the term \"ḥadīth\" (pl. aḥādīth) refers to the prophetic traditions being cited as evidence for the virtue of good character.\n- Root: قال (Q-W-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To say, to speak, to utter. In scholarly context, \"qāla\" (he said) introduces transmitted statements — whether prophetic, companion, or scholar sayings.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"قال\" is the verb of direct speech, used to transmit authoritative statements. In this section, it introduces the chain of transmission for prophetic ḥadīths and the sayings of the Companions and early scholars (āthār).\n- Sibawayh Rule: Prepositional Interposition and Apposition (al-ʿAṭf wa al-Badl) — The text employs extensive appositional structures (badl) and coordinated attributions (ʿaṭf bayān) to identify the sources of transmitted reports, e.g., \"أخرجه الخرايطي في مكارم الأخلاق بإسناد ضعيف\" — the verb \"akhrajahu\" (he recorded it) governs a chain of transmitters and works, each in apposition to the other, requiring precise tracking of who recorded what from whom.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Insight"}], "8": [{"arabic": "حسد إخوة يوسف عليه السلام وعبر عما في قلوبهم بقوله تعالى {إذ قالوا ليوسف وأخوه أحب إلى أبينا منا ونحن عصبة إن أبانا لفي ضلال مبين اقتلوا يوسف أو اطرحوه أرضا يخل لكم وجه أبيكم} فلما كرهوا حب أبيهم له وساءهم ذلك وأحبوا زواله عنه غيبوه عنه وقال تعالى {ولا يجدون في صدورهم حاجة مما أوتوا} أي لا تضيق صدورهم به ولا يغتمون فأثنى عليهم بعدم الحسد وقال تعالى في معرض الإنكار {أم يحسدون الناس على ما آتاهم الله من فضله} وقال تعالى {كان الناس أمة واحدة} إلى قوله {إلا الذين أوتوه من بعد ما جاءتهم البينات بغيا بينهم} قيل في التفسير حسدا وقال تعالى {وما تفرقوا إل", "english": "The Prophet ﷺ said: «إن المؤمن يغبط والمنافق يحسد» — \"The believer aspires emulously, and the hypocrite envies.\"", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 720", "section_title_en": "On the Reality of Envy (Ḥasad) and Its Degrees — Section 720", "section_index": 720, "anchors": "- Root: نعم (n-ʿ-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of \"bounty, benefaction, grace\" — that state of goodness and well-being bestowed.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النعمة: الحالة الحسنة\" — bounty is the excellent state/condition; it is the genus term applying to both little and much, as in {«وإن تعدوا نعمة الله لا تحصوها»} [Ibrahim: 34].\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"جلت نعمة الله ونعماؤه\" — bounty as actual bestowed good. Metaphorical (majāz): \"خفت نعامتهم\" — departure/removal, relevant to the envier's wish for the bounty's removal.\n- Root: حسد (ḥ-s-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Envy — the desire for removal of another's good.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الحسد: تمني زوال نعمة من مستحق لها\" — envy is wishing the removal of bounty from one who deserves it, sometimes accompanied by striving to effect its removal. Cited: «المؤمن يغبط والمنافق يحسد».\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"حسده على نعمة الله\" — envying someone for God's bounty. \"إن الحسد يأكل الجسد\" — envy consumes the body.\n- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self; also value, preciousness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): النفس: الروح — the soul/spirit; also الذات (essence/self).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس ومنفس\" — a precious thing. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه أي دمه\" — poured out his self, i.e., his blood. From this root derives المنافسة (emulative competition) — the striving for precious things.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Specification) — The definition of ḥasad is given as a restricted predication (ḥadd), delimiting its essential meaning: \"كراهة النعمة وحب زوالها عن المنعم عليه\" — the hatred of bounty and love of its removal from the one upon whom it is bestowed. This is a formal definition (ḥadd), not merely a lexical gloss.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "13": [{"arabic": "لا قال لقولك لأخوته أخاف أن يأكله الذئب وأنتم عنه غافلون لم خفت عليه الذئب ولم ترجني ولم نظرت إلى غفلة أخوته ولم تنظر إلى حفظي له وتدري لم رددته عليك قال لا قال لأنك رجوتني وقلت {عسى الله أن يأتيني بهم جميعا} وبما قلت اذهبو فتحسسوا من يوسف وأخيه ولا تيأسوا وكذلك لما قال يوسف لصاحب الملك {اذكرني عند ربك} قال الله تعالى {فأنساه الشيطان ذكر ربه فلبث في السجن بضع سنين} وأمثال هذه الحكايات لا تنحصر ولم يرد بها القرآن والأخبار ورود الأسمار بل الغرض بها الاعتبار والاستبصار لتعلم أن الأنبياء عليهم السلام لم يتجا", "english": "The second type [of narratives that stir the heart toward repentance] concerns the stories of the prophets and the righteous predecessors, and what befell them of calamities by reason of their sins. For this is intensely impactful and manifestly beneficial upon the hearts of creation—such as the state of Adam (peace be upon him) in his disobedience and what he encountered of expulsion from Paradise. It is even narrated that when he ate from the tree, the [heavenly] garments (al-ḥulal) flew off his body and his nakedness became exposed. Then the crown and the diadem felt shame before his face to remain lifted above him, so Gabriel (peace be upon him) came to him, took the crown from his head, and loosened the diadem from his brow. And it was proclaimed from above the Throne: \"Descend from My proximity, for none who disobeys Me dwells near Me.\" He said: Then Adam turned to Eve weeping and said: \"This is the first ill-omen of disobedience—it has driven us from the proximity of the Beloved.\"", "book_title": "Fear and Hope", "section_title_ar": "Section 946", "section_title_en": "The Second Type: Narratives of the Prophets and Righteous Predecessors Concerning the Calamities That Befell Them Due to Their Sins", "section_index": 946, "anchors": "- Root: ن ب أ (n-b-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To inform, to announce with importance; the core sense of conveying news of significant import.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological usage, 'naba'' (نبأ) denotes divine communication of unseen realities—here, God's informing of events carrying moral and spiritual weight.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) for direct announcement; metaphorical (Majaz) when used of the heart being 'informed' through reflection (i'tibar).\n- Root: ذ ن ب (dh-n-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The tail of an animal; by extension, that which follows or trails behind—hence, a sin as the consequence that trails a soul.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الذنب في الأصل: الأخذ بذنب الشيء\" — sin is fundamentally 'seizing the tail of a thing,' i.e., pursuing a wrongful act that drags one into its wake; used for minor offenses (sagha'ir) of prophets versus major ones (kaba'ir) of others.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the physical tail. Metaphorical: \"هو من الأذناب\" — one who trails behind; here, the prophets' sins are 'tails'—swiftly punished in this world to spare them the hereafter.\n- Root: ع ج ل (ʿ-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Haste, swiftness; to expedite.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Haste in divine punishment ('uujila bil-'uqubah) signifies mercy for the elect—cleansing them before the afterlife.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: speed of action. Metaphorical: God's 'hastening' of retribution as a mark of honor, contrasted with the respite (imhal) granted to the wretched.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Applied to \"إنما نطيعك إذا أطعنت الله\" (We only obey you when you obey God), where 'innama' restricts obedience to a conditional state, and to \"إن هذا أمر كان من السماء\" where 'inna' provides emphatic predication of divine decree.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Fear and Hope'", "badge": "Insight"}], "17": [{"arabic": "الله تعالى وما أنت بمؤمن لنا أي بمصدق والإسلام عبارة عن التسليم والاستسلام بالإذعان والانقياد وترك التمرد والإباء والعناد وللتصديق محل خاص وهو القلب واللسان ترجمان وأما التسليم فإنه عام في القلب واللسان والجوارح فإن كل تصديق بالقلب فهو تسليم وترك الإباء والجحود وكذلك الاعتراف باللسان وكذلك الطاعة والانقياد بالجوارح فموجب اللغة أن الإسلام أعم والإيمان أخص فكان الإيمان عبارة عن أشرف أجزاء الإسلام فإذن كل تصديق تسليم وليس كل تسليم تصديقا البحث الثاني عن إطلاق الشرع والحق", "english": "The truth in this matter is that faith (iman) is an expression for assent (tasdiq). God, exalted be He, has said: {وَمَا أَنتَ بِمُؤْمِنٍ لِّنَا} [And you are not one to believe us] (Quran 12:17) — that is, not one to assent to us. And Islam is an expression for surrender (taslim) and self-abandonment (istislam) through acquiescence (idhan) and compliance (inqiyad), and the abandonment of recalcitrance, refusal, obstinacy, and stubbornness.", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "section_title_ar": "Section 98", "section_title_en": "On Whether Islam and Faith (Iman) Are Identical or Distinct", "section_index": 98, "anchors": "- Root: أمن (amana)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes safety, security, and freedom from fear; the isti'man form yields 'belief' as an act of granting credence and trust.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإيمان هو التصديق\" — Faith (iman) is fundamentally assent (tasdiq), a conviction of the heart, not a mere verbal profession.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage ties iman to tasdiq (verification/assent); metaphorical extension applies it to outward compliance only in a derived sense.\n- Root: سلم (salima)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes soundness, safety, and freedom from defect; the istislam form yields 'submission' as an act of yielding and surrendering.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإسلام عبارة عن التسليم والاستسلام\" — Islam is surrender (taslim) and self-abandonment (istislam) through compliance and obedience.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage encompasses outward acts of the limbs; metaphorical (Majaz) usage can extend to inward assent, but the primary domain is the external.\n- Root: صدق (sadaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes truthfulness and veracity in speech and report.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الصدق والكذب أصلهما في القول\" — Truth and falsehood originate in speech; tasdiq is the act of affirming a report as true.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is in verbal confirmation; metaphorical extension applies to 'true in resolve' or 'true in attack,' i.e., confirming through action.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Interposition (باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور) — Governing the permissible separation between a governing word and its governed prepositional phrase, relevant here for parsing the conditional and contrastive structures in the theological arguments.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "20": [{"arabic": "وبالإضافة إلى العوض عنه رغبة فيه وحبا ولذلك قال الله تعالى وشروه بثمن بخس دراهم معدودة وكانوا فيه من الزاهدين معناه باعوه فقد يطلق الشراء بمعنى البيع ووصف أخوة يوسف بالزهد فيه إذ طمعوا أن يخلو لهم وجه أبيهم وكان ذلك عندهم أحب إليهم من يوسف فباعوه طمعا في العوض فإذن كل من باع الدنيا بالآخرة فهو زاهد في الدنيا وكل من باع الآخرة بالدنيا فهو أيضا زاهد ولكن في الآخرة ولكن العادة جارية بتخصيص اسم الزهد بمن يزهد في الدنيا كما خصص اسم الإلحاد بمن يميل إلى الباطل خاصة وإن كان هو للميل في وضع اللسان ولما كان الزهد رغبة عن محبوب بالجملة لم يتصور إلا بالعدول إلى شيء هو", "english": "Know that asceticism in this world (al-zuhd fī al-dunyā) is a noble station (maqām sharīf) among the stations of the wayfarers (al-sālikīn). This station is composed of knowledge (ʿilm), a state (ḥāl), and action (ʿamal), just like all other stations — for all the gates of faith, as the predecessors (al-salaf) said, reduce to a creedal affirmation (ʿaqd), a utterance (qawl), and an action (ʿamal). It is as though utterance, due to its outward manifestation, was made to stand in the place of the state (ḥāl), since through it the inner state becomes manifest. Otherwise, utterance is not intended for its own sake; if it does not issue from a state, it is called \"submission\" (islām) and is not called \"faith\" (īmān). Knowledge is the cause that produces the state, running in the manner of a fruit-bearing tree, while action runs from the state in the manner of the fruit itself. So let us mention the state together with both of its two extremities — knowledge and action.", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 1087", "section_title_en": "On Asceticism (Al-Zuhd) — Its Reality, Conditions, and Degrees", "section_index": 1087, "anchors": "- Root: زهد (Z-H-D)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning: scarcity, smallness, and abstemiousness; also estimation (kharṣ) of fruit.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الزهيد: الشيء القليل، والزاهد في الشيء: الراغب عنه والراضي منه بالزهيد\" — the ascetic is one who turns away from a thing, content with little instead of it.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"زهد في الشيء: رغب عنه\" (to turn one's desire away from something). Metaphorical (Majaz): \"رجل زهيد: قليل الخير\" — applied to one of little worth; \"واد زهيد\" — a valley that takes little water. The term is conventionally restricted to renouncing the permissible (mubāḥāt), not the forbidden.\n- Root: رغب (R-GH-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes spaciousness and amplitude; \"رغب الشيء: اتسع\" (the thing became wide).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"أصل الرغبة: السعة في الشيء... والرغبة والرغب والرغبى: السعة في الإرادة\" — desire is an expansion of the will toward something; \"رغب عنه\" implies turning desire away (the very definition of zuhd).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"هو راغب فيه وراغب عنه\" — one can be desirous of a thing or averse to it. Metaphorical: \"واد رغيب: كثير الأخذ للماء\" — a valley that takes much water, contrasting with \"واد زهيد\" (one that takes little). Thus, zuhd and raghbah are relative terms defined by their objects.\n- Root: دنا (D-N-W)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الدنو: القرب بالذات، أو بالحكم\" — nearness in essence or by judgment; used for place, time, and rank. The \"nearer\" (adnā) life is the worldly life, contrasted with the \"farther\" (ākhirah), which is superior and more enduring.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The term \"zāhid\" (ascetic) is not applied absolutely but is restricted by convention (istiṣlāḥ) to specific objects of renunciation (worldly goods), just as \"mulḥid\" (heretic) is restricted to one who inclines to falsehood, though the root meaning is broader. This governs the author's analysis of how names are conventionally specified.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "21": [{"arabic": "الدرجات قال الله عز وجل {وكذلك مكنا ليوسف في الأرض} وأيوب عليه السلام بعد المحنة العظيمة مكن قال الله تعالى وآتيناه أهله ومثلهم معهم الآية فهذا الكلام من الشافعي رحمه الله يدل على تبحره في أسرار القرآن واطلاعه على مقامات السائرين إلى الله تعالى من الأنبياء والأولياء وكل ذلك من علوم الآخرة وقيل للشافعي رحمه الله متى يكون الرجل عالما قال إذا تحقق في علم الدين فعلمه وتعرض لسائر العلوم فنظر فيما فاته فعند ذلك يكون عالما فإنه قيل لجالينوس إنك تأمر للداء الواحد بالأدوية الكثيرة المجمعة فقال إنما المقصود م", "english": "And al-Shafi'i, may God Most High have mercy upon him, said: \"If you fear for your deed the blight of self-admiration (al-ʿujb), then consider: whose pleasure do you seek? Toward what reward do you yearn? From what punishment do you flee? What well-being do you thank? And what affliction do you recall? For if you reflect upon even one of these five qualities, your deed will appear small in your eyes.\" Observe how he mentioned the reality of ostentation and the remedy for self-admiration—both being among the gravest maladies of the heart.", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "section_title_ar": "Section 21", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 21: The Sciences of the Hereafter and the Signs of Sincere Intention in Knowledge", "section_index": 21, "anchors": "- Root: مكن (m-k-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of establishing, empowering, and granting firm footing in a place or station.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"المكان عند أهل اللغة: الموضع الحاوي للشيء\" — the place that encompasses a thing; theological nuance: divine empowerment (tamkīn) as a station granted after trial.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"مكنته من الشيء وأمكنته منه، فتمكن منه واستمكن\" — physical enabling. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"الناس على مكناتهم: على مقارهم\" — people upon their settled abodes/stations; here, the spiritual station of the prophets after tribulation.\n- Root: محن (m-ḥ-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Testing, refining, and proving; a worn garment (mamḥūn) that has been stretched and expanded by use.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"المحن والامتحان نحو الابتلاء\" — trial and testing akin to affliction; Quranic: {فامتحنوهن} (Al-Mumtahanah: 10) — the testing of hearts for sincerity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"وقع في محنة ومحن\" — falling into trial. Metaphorical: \"محن الأديم: مدده حتى وسعه\" — stretching hide until it widens; thus {امتحن الله قلوبهم} — God expands and purifies the heart through trial.\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge as the apprehension of a thing's reality; the mark (ʿalam) by which one is guided.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the perception of a thing in its true reality; two types: apprehension of essence, and judgment of existence or negation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"ما علمت بخبرك: ما شعرت به\" — to be aware. Metaphorical: \"خفيت معالم الطريق\" — the traces of the path that guide the seeker; here, the signs (ʿalāmāt) of sincere intention.\n- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Turning, overturning, and transforming a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart as that which is constantly turned and transformed; the seat of spiritual perception.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — physical overturning. Metaphorical: \"قلب التاجر السلعة\" — the merchant scrutinizing his goods; \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور\" — one who turns matters over; here, the heart's gaze upon its own intentions.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to confine a predicate to a single subject, as in \"إنما المقصود منها واحد\" (the intended aim is but one), emphasizing exclusive focus.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}], "23": [{"arabic": "فقالت له التي هو في بيتها لقد أقمأتك إذ ردت عليك هديتك (5) أي أذلتك واستصغرتك فقال صلى الله عليه وسلم أنتن أهون على الله أن تقمئنني ثم غضب عليهن كلهن شهرا إلى أن عاد إليهن العاشر في آداب الجماع ويستحب أن يبدأ باسم الله تعالى ويقرأ قل هو الله أحد أولا ويكبر ويهلل ويقول بسم الله العلي العظيم اللهم اجعلها ذرية طيبة إن كنت قدرت أن تخرج ذلك من صلبي وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم لو أن أحدكم إذا أتى أهله قال اللهم جنبني الشيطان وجنب الشيطان ما رزقتنا فإن كان بينهما ولد لم يضره PageV02", "english": "I say: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, has said: «من كان له امرأتان فمال إلى إحداهما دون الأخرى» — \"Whoever has two wives and inclines toward one of them to the exclusion of the other\" — and in another wording: «ولم يعدل بينهما جاء يوم القيامة وأحد شقيه مائل» — \"and does not act equitably between them, he shall come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides leaning.\"", "book_title": "Etiquette of Marriage", "section_title_ar": "Section 305", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Book on the Etiquette of Marriage: Section 305 (On Justice Between Co-Wives, Nushuz, and the Etiquette of Intercourse)", "section_index": 305, "anchors": "- Root: عدل (ʿadl)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is \"to be equal, to balance, to straighten\" — the root denotes equity and even-handedness in distribution.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological usage, ʿadl is the mean of justice, opposed to jawr (tyranny) — it is the act of placing things in their proper stations.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage pertains to measurable distribution (ʿatāʾ, mabīt); metaphorical (Majāz) usage extends to that which is not under voluntary control, such as love (maḥabbah) and inclination of the heart.\n- Root: نشز (nushūz)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes \"rising up\" or \"elevation\"; in marital context it signifies a rising of one spouse against the other in discord or recalcitrance.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Nushūz is the rebellion of one spouse against the bond of obedience and harmony, a moral elevation against the other.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is the physical rising from a place; metaphorical usage is the spiritual/moral rising in defiance.\n- Root: وقع (waqʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes \"falling\" or \"occurrence\"; in the marital context, it is a euphemism for sexual intercourse.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The term is used in the Quran for the \"falling\" of an event; here it is a euphemistic transfer (naql) for coitus.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is physical falling; metaphorical usage is the act of intercourse, as in the hadith \"لا يقعن أحدكم على امرأته\" (Let none of you fall upon his wife like a beast).\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The particle innamā restricts the predicate to the subject alone, as in the hadith \"إنما عليه العدل في العطاء والمبيت\" (Upon him is only justice in expenditure and overnight stays), confining the obligation to what is within human capacity.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Etiquette of Marriage'", "badge": "Du'a"}], "24": [{"arabic": "وهم بها لولا أن رأى برهان ربه} وعنه أيضا ما هو أعجب من هذا وذلك أنه خرج من المدينة حاجا ومعه رفيق له حتى نزلا بالأبواء فقام رفيقه وأخذ السفرة وانطلق إلى السوق ليبتاع شيئا وجلس سليمان في الخيمة وكان من أجمل الناس وجها وأورعهم فبصرت به أعرابية من قلة الجبل وانحدرت إليه حتى وقفت بين يديه وعليها البرقع والقفازان فأسفرت عن وجه لها كأنه فلقة قمر وقالت أهنئني فظن أنها تريد طعاما فقام إلى فضلة السفرة ليعطيها فقالت لست أريد هذا إنما أريد ما يكون من الرجل إلى أهله فقال جهزك إلى إبليس", "english": "...which one is ashamed of and fears to plunge into. And the abstention of most people from its requirements is either due to incapacity, or fear, or shame, or concern for preserving one's body — and in none of these is there any reward, for that is merely preferring one share of one's worldly desires over another share. Yes — from divine protection (al-ʿiṣmah) is that one is not able [to sin]; so in these obstacles there is a benefit, namely the repulsion of sin. For whoever abandons fornication, its sin is repelled from him by whatever cause his abandonment occurred. Rather, the virtue and abundant reward lie in abandoning it out of fear of God — may He be exalted — while possessing the ability, with the removal of obstacles, the facilitation of means, and especially at the height of genuine desire. And this is the station of the veracious (al-ṣiddīqīn). For this reason, the Prophet — peace be upon him — said: \"Whoever loves passionately, then remains chaste, then conceals [his love], then dies — he dies a martyr.\"(1)", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 654", "section_title_en": "The Book of Breaking the Two Desires — Section 654: On Chastity, Guarding the Gaze, and the Virtue of Restraining Desire", "section_index": 654, "anchors": "- **Root: ع ف ف** (ʿaffa)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: Core meaning of abstaining from what is unlawful, refraining, and remaining chaste; al-ʿafāf is the state of one who abstains from forbidden things.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: Theological nuance — ʿiffah (chastity) is a virtue of the soul that restrains the appetitive faculty from pursuing what is not permissible; it is a station of the ṣiddīqūn (veracious ones).\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal (ḥaqīqah) — physical abstention from unlawful acts; Metaphorical (majāz) — the heart's abstention from coveting what God has forbidden, which is the higher reality of chastity.\n\n- **Root: غ ب ق** (ghabaqa)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: The evening drink (al-ghabūq) — the milking or drink given at nightfall; contrasted with al-ṣabūḥ (the morning drink).\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In the hadith of the three men in the cave, the term marks the temporal precision of filial devotion — serving parents before any other claim, even at the boundary of night.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the evening milking; the narrative use in the hadith is literal, denoting the exact act of service delayed out of reverence.\n\n- **Root: ه م م** (hamma)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To intend, to resolve upon a matter; al-hamm is the initial stirring of intention before full determination.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In Q. 12:24 {«وَلَقَدْ هَمَّتْ بِهِ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوْلَا أَنْ رَأَى بُرْهَانَ رَبِّهِ»} — \"And certainly she desired him, and he would have desired her, had it not been that he saw the proof of his Lord\" — the term distinguishes between a passing inclination (hamm) and a settled resolve; Yūsuf's hamm was repelled by divine proof, while Zulaykhā's was consummated in action.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the inward movement of intention; the rhetorical force lies in the contrast between the two hamm-s, one punished and one pardoned.\n\n- **Root: ن ظ ر** (naẓara)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To look, to gaze; al-naẓar is the act of sight, whether physical or intellectual.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: The gaze (naẓar) is the gateway to desire; the Quranic phrase {«يَعْلَمُ خَائِنَةَ الْأَعْيُنِ»} — \"He knows the treachery of the eyes\" (Q. 40:19) — indicates that the look which steals toward the forbidden is itself an act of betrayal recorded by God.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the first glance that occurs unintentionally; Metaphorical — the second glance is the \"treachery of the eyes,\" for it is a deliberate return to what the first glance stumbled upon by accident.\n\n- **Root: ر و د** (rāwada)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To seek, to desire, to solicit; murāwadah is the act of soliciting someone for an unlawful purpose.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In the Yūsuf narrative, murāwadah denotes the persistent solicitation toward sin; the term carries the weight of repeated, deliberate pursuit.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the physical act of solicitation; the narrative contexts in this section use the term literally for the woman's pursuit of the young man.\n\n- **Sibawayh Rule**: **Bāb al-ḥaṣr wa-l-taqyīd bi-innamā** (Restriction and Focused Predication with innamā)\n  * The particle innamā restricts and confines the predicate to the subject alone, negating all else. In the woman's statement \"innamā urīdu mā yakūnu min al-rajuli ilā ahlihī\" — \"I only desire what comes from a man to his wife\" — the restriction (ḥaṣr) intensifies the gravity of the solicitation, making the young man's resistance all the more virtuous.\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Hadith"}, {"arabic": "يوسف الذي هممت وأنت سليمان الذي لم تهم أشار إلى قوله تعالى {ولقد همت به وهم بها لولا أن رأى برهان ربه} وعنه أيضا ما هو أعجب من هذا وذلك أنه خرج من المدينة حاجا ومعه رفيق له حتى نزلا بالأبواء فقام رفيقه وأخذ السفرة وانطلق إلى السوق ليبتاع شيئا وجلس سليمان في الخيمة وكان من أجمل الناس وجها وأورعهم فبصرت به أعرابية من قلة الجبل وانحدرت إليه حتى وقفت بين يديه وعليها البرقع والقفازان فأسفرت عن وجه لها كأنه فلقة قمر وقالت أهنئني فظن أنها تريد طعاما فقام إلى فضلة السفرة ليعطيها فقالت لست أريد هذا إنما أريد ما يكون من الرجل إلى أهله فقال جهزك إلى إبل", "english": "...which one is ashamed of and fears to plunge into. And the abstention of most people from its requirements is either due to incapacity, or fear, or shame, or concern for preserving one's body — and in none of these is there any reward, for that is merely preferring one share of one's worldly desires over another share. Yes — from divine protection (al-ʿiṣmah) is that one is not able [to sin]; so in these obstacles there is a benefit, namely the repulsion of sin. For whoever abandons fornication, its sin is repelled from him by whatever cause his abandonment occurred. Rather, the virtue and abundant reward lie in abandoning it out of fear of God — may He be exalted — while possessing the ability, with the removal of obstacles, the facilitation of means, and especially at the height of genuine desire. And this is the station of the veracious (al-ṣiddīqīn). For this reason, the Prophet — peace be upon him — said: \"Whoever loves passionately, then remains chaste, then conceals [his love], then dies — he dies a martyr.\"(1)", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "section_title_ar": "Section 654", "section_title_en": "The Book of Breaking the Two Desires — Section 654: On Chastity, Guarding the Gaze, and the Virtue of Restraining Desire", "section_index": 654, "anchors": "- **Root: ع ف ف** (ʿaffa)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: Core meaning of abstaining from what is unlawful, refraining, and remaining chaste; al-ʿafāf is the state of one who abstains from forbidden things.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: Theological nuance — ʿiffah (chastity) is a virtue of the soul that restrains the appetitive faculty from pursuing what is not permissible; it is a station of the ṣiddīqūn (veracious ones).\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal (ḥaqīqah) — physical abstention from unlawful acts; Metaphorical (majāz) — the heart's abstention from coveting what God has forbidden, which is the higher reality of chastity.\n\n- **Root: غ ب ق** (ghabaqa)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: The evening drink (al-ghabūq) — the milking or drink given at nightfall; contrasted with al-ṣabūḥ (the morning drink).\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In the hadith of the three men in the cave, the term marks the temporal precision of filial devotion — serving parents before any other claim, even at the boundary of night.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the evening milking; the narrative use in the hadith is literal, denoting the exact act of service delayed out of reverence.\n\n- **Root: ه م م** (hamma)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To intend, to resolve upon a matter; al-hamm is the initial stirring of intention before full determination.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In Q. 12:24 {«وَلَقَدْ هَمَّتْ بِهِ وَهَمَّ بِهَا لَوْلَا أَنْ رَأَى بُرْهَانَ رَبِّهِ»} — \"And certainly she desired him, and he would have desired her, had it not been that he saw the proof of his Lord\" — the term distinguishes between a passing inclination (hamm) and a settled resolve; Yūsuf's hamm was repelled by divine proof, while Zulaykhā's was consummated in action.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the inward movement of intention; the rhetorical force lies in the contrast between the two hamm-s, one punished and one pardoned.\n\n- **Root: ن ظ ر** (naẓara)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To look, to gaze; al-naẓar is the act of sight, whether physical or intellectual.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: The gaze (naẓar) is the gateway to desire; the Quranic phrase {«يَعْلَمُ خَائِنَةَ الْأَعْيُنِ»} — \"He knows the treachery of the eyes\" (Q. 40:19) — indicates that the look which steals toward the forbidden is itself an act of betrayal recorded by God.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the first glance that occurs unintentionally; Metaphorical — the second glance is the \"treachery of the eyes,\" for it is a deliberate return to what the first glance stumbled upon by accident.\n\n- **Root: ر و د** (rāwada)\n  * **Lisan / Ayn**: To seek, to desire, to solicit; murāwadah is the act of soliciting someone for an unlawful purpose.\n  * **Al-Raghib (Mufradat)**: In the Yūsuf narrative, murāwadah denotes the persistent solicitation toward sin; the term carries the weight of repeated, deliberate pursuit.\n  * **Al-Zamakhshari (Asas)**: Literal — the physical act of solicitation; the narrative contexts in this section use the term literally for the woman's pursuit of the young man.\n\n- **Sibawayh Rule**: **Bāb al-ḥaṣr wa-l-taqyīd bi-innamā** (Restriction and Focused Predication with innamā)\n  * The particle innamā restricts and confines the predicate to the subject alone, negating all else. In the woman's statement \"innamā urīdu mā yakūnu min al-rajuli ilā ahlihī\" — \"I only desire what comes from a man to his wife\" — the restriction (ḥaṣr) intensifies the gravity of the solicitation, making the young man's resistance all the more virtuous.\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "25": [{"arabic": "فقال تعالى وألفيا سيدها لدى الباب فإذا انقلب السيد مسخرا فقد بدل نعمة الله كفرا ونفس المرأة على مثال نفسك إن أرسلت عنانها قليلا جمحت بك طويلا وإن أرخيت عذارها فترا جذبتك ذراعا وإن كبحتها وشددت يدك عليها في محل الشدة ملكتها قال الشافعي رضي الله عنه ثلاثة إن أكرمتهم أهانوك وإن أهنتهم أكرموك المرأة والخادم والنبطي أراد به إن محضت الإكرام ولم تمزج غلظك بلينك وفظاظتك برفقك وكانت نساء العرب يعلمن بناتهن اختبار الأزواج وكانت المرأة تقول لابنتها اختبري زوجك قبل الإقدام والجراء", "english": "The first point of etiquette is the wedding feast (walīmah), and it is recommended (mustaḥabbah). Anas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw upon ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, may God be pleased with him, a trace of yellow dye, so he said: {«What is this?»} He replied: \"I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold.\" He said: \"May God bless you. Hold a wedding feast, even if with a single sheep.\" {«...»} And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, held a wedding feast for Ṣafiyyah with dates and sawīq (barley porridge). {«...»} And he, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The food of the first day is an obligation (ḥaqq), the food of the second day is a Sunnah, and the food of the third day is for show (sumʿah); and whoever seeks to be heard, God will make his deeds heard.\" {«...»} None raised this hadith except Ziyād ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and it is anomalous (gharīb). It is recommended to offer congratulations to him, and the one who enters upon the husband should say: \"May God bless you and shower blessings upon you, and may He bring you both together in goodness.\" {«...»} Abū Hurayrah, may God be pleased with him, reported that he, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded this. It is also recommended to make the marriage public (iẓhār al-nikāḥ). He, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the drum and the voice.\" {«...»} The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Announce this marriage, hold it in the mosques, and beat drums for it.\" {«...»} And on the authority of al-Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and entered on the morning of my wedding night, and he sat upon my bedding, and we had young girls with us who were beating their drums and lamenting those of my forefathers who had been killed—until one of them said: \"And among us is a Prophet who knows what will be tomorrow.\" He said to her: \"Stop this, and say what you were saying before.\" {«...»}", "book_title": "Etiquette of Marriage", "section_title_ar": "Section 303", "section_title_en": "On What is Incumbent Upon the Husband and What is Incumbent Upon the Wife", "section_index": 303, "anchors": "- Root: و ل م (w-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The core meaning pertains to the wedding feast (walīmah), derived from the concept of gathering and union.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological usage, it signifies the communal meal marking the consummation of a marriage contract, a recommended act of public gratitude.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage denotes the specific feast; metaphorical (Majaz) extension applies to any act of publicizing a joyous occasion.\n- Root: ع ش ر (ʿ- sh-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes association, companionship, and intimacy; the tenth (ʿasharah) of a thing is related, but the primary social sense is cohabitation and mutual dealing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the Quranic context of {وَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ}, it signifies a sustained, equitable mode of social intercourse grounded in moral rectitude, not mere physical proximity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is the act of living together; metaphorical (Majaz) usage elevates it to a standard of ethical conduct (maʿrūf) that defines the marital bond.\n- Root: ق س م (q-s-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root indicates division, apportionment, and distribution; in the marital context, it refers to the equitable division of time among co-wives.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theologically, it is tied to justice (ʿadl) as a divine attribute; for the husband, it is a legal obligation to maintain fairness in material and temporal allotments.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is the physical act of dividing; metaphorical (Majaz) usage applies to the moral duty of impartiality in affection and provision.\n- Root: غ ي ر (gh-y-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root conveys alteration and change, but in the moral register, it denotes protective jealousy (ghayrah), a state of aversion to the violation of honor.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In Kalam, ghayrah is a praiseworthy emotion when aligned with divine law—jealousy for the sanctity of the family—and blameworthy when it stems from unjust suspicion (sūʾ al-ẓann).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage is the emotional state; metaphorical (Majaz) usage is attributed to God (al-Ghayyār) as a figure for His prohibition of indecencies, distinguishing human passion from divine will.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to isolate specific obligations (e.g., \"the third is that he should increase...\") and to distinguish categories of jealousy and pride, ensuring precise legal and moral demarcation.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Marriage'", "badge": "Insight"}], "31": [{"arabic": "الله تعالى عن صواحبات يوسف عليه السلام بقوله ما هذا بشرا إن هذا إلا ملك كريم ومن صرف همته إلى اتباع اللذات البدنية يأكل كما تأكل الأنعام فقد انحط إلى حضيض أفق البهائم فيصير إما غمرا كثور وإما شرها كخنزير وإما ضربا ككلب أو سنور أو حقودا كجمل أو متكبرا كنمر أو ذا روغان كثعلب أو يجمع ذلك كله كشيطان مريد وما من عضو من الأعضاء ولا حاسة من الحواس إلا ويمكن الاستعانة به على طريق الوصول إلى الله تعالى كما سيأتي بيان طرف منه في كتاب الشكر فمن استعمله فيه فقد فاز ومن عدل عنه فقد خسر وخاب وجملة السعادة في ذلك أن يجعل لقاء الله تعالى", "english": "Know that just as the rational person does not know the necessary sciences (al-ʿulūm al-ḍarūriyyah) nor what distinguishes the state of the rational one from what he has acquired of the theoretical sciences, so too does the rational person not know what Allah has opened for His friends (awliyāʾ) and His prophets of the prerogatives of His gentleness (luṭf) and mercy. Whatever mercy Allah opens to people, none can withhold it. This mercy is dispensed by the decree of bounty and generosity from Allah, Glorified and Exalted, not grudged to anyone. But it only appears in hearts that expose themselves to the wafts of the mercy of Allah, Exalted — as he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"Indeed, your Lord has, in the days of your time, wafts of mercy — so expose yourselves to them.\" (1) Hadith: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \"Long has been the yearning of the righteous for My meeting\" — the hadith. I found no source for it except that the author of al-Firdaws transmitted it from the hadith of Abū al-Dardāʾ, and his son did not mention for it in the Musnad of al-Firdaws an isnād.", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "section_title_ar": "Section 579", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 579: The Human's Distinguishing Property is Knowledge and Wisdom; The Heart as the Seat of the King", "section_index": 579, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of turning over, revolving, and transformation from one state to another; the heart as that which is constantly turning and fluctuating.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The heart (qalb) is so named for its constant turning (taqallub) between states; it is the seat of perception and understanding, the faculty by which one grasps realities.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: turning a thing over. Metaphorical: the heart as the seat of understanding and the center of the human kingdom, that which governs and directs the faculties.\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge, perception, and certainty; the mark or trace by which a thing is known.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Knowledge is the apprehension of a thing as it truly is; it is the distinguishing property of the human being and the purpose of his creation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: knowing. Metaphorical: the light by which the heart perceives realities, the noblest of which is knowledge of God.\n- Root: ملك (m-l-k)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Possession, sovereignty, and dominion; a king who rules over a domain.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The king is one who possesses authority and commands; the heart is the king of the human body, ruling over its faculties.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: a king. Metaphorical: the heart as the sovereign of the human kingdom, with the faculties as its subjects, messengers, and servants.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب التشبيه والتمثيل (The Chapter of Simile and Analogy) — The use of extended analogies (tamthīl) to clarify abstract realities through concrete images, where the comparison is drawn between the relations of parts, not merely individual attributes.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}], "38": [{"arabic": "الجميل بجماله وعجب الغني بغناه لأن كل ذلك من فضل الله وإنما هو محل لفيضان فضل الله تعالى وجوده والمحل أيضا من فضله وجوده فإن قلت لا يمكنني أن أجهل أعمالي وإني أنا عملتها فإني أنتظر عليها ثوابا ولولا أنها عملي لما انتظرت ثوابا فإن كانت الأعمال مخلوقة لله على سبيل الاختراع فمن أين لي الثواب وإن كانت الأعمال مني وبقدرته فكيف لا أعجب بها فاعلم أن جوابك من وجهين أحدهما هو صريح الحق والآخر فيه مسامحة أما صريح الحق فهو أنك وقدرتك وإرادتك وحركتك وجميع ذلك من خلق الله واختراعه فما عملت إذ عملت وما صليت إذ ص", "english": "...and you were not pleased with it. Then He gave you a servant, and you became pleased with it, saying: \"He only gave me a servant because I am a horse-owner; as for another, he has no horse.\" So it is said: He is the One who gave you the horse — there is no difference between His giving you the horse and the servant together, or His giving you one after the other. Since all of it is from Him, it behooves you to admire His bounty and favor, not yourself.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Delusion", "section_title_ar": "Section 878", "section_title_en": "On the Vanity of Self-Admiration in Acts of Worship — The True Source of Grace and the Illusion of Personal Agency", "section_index": 878, "anchors": "- Root: عجب (ʿajiba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Astonishment, wonder, and self-amazement; the state of being struck by something marvelous.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Self-admiration (ʿujb) is blameworthy when directed at one's own acts, as it implies a false attribution of agency to the self rather than to God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: wonder at a thing's beauty or rarity. Metaphorical: wonder at oneself, which is a delusion when all causes proceed from another.\n- Root: خلق (khalaqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To measure, fashion, and originate; creation as divine act of bringing into being.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Creation (khalq) is the origination of a thing from nothing without prior model, or the bringing forth of one thing from another by divine decree.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: shaping and proportioning. Metaphorical: God's absolute origination of all acts, attributes, and agents — exclusive to Him.\n- Root: قدر (qadara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Power, capacity, and measure; the ability to bring about an act.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Divine power (qudrah) is the negation of incapacity; human power is a created instrument, not an independent source of effect.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: ability over a specific thing. Metaphorical: the key (miftāḥ) to action, which is entirely in God's hand.\n- Root: قلب (qalaba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn, overturn, or transform; the heart as the seat of volition and understanding.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The heart (qalb) is the locus of knowledge and will; its turning is directed by God alone.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical turning. Metaphorical: the heart's inclination and the divine disposal of its states.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Restriction and Focused Predication (باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما) — The particle \"innamā\" restricts the predicate to the subject alone, used here to expose the fallacy of self-attribution in the hypothetical objection.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Condemnation of Delusion'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "50": [{"arabic": "عين الشهود الذي يضاهي حاله حال النسوة اللاتي قطعن أيديهن في مشاهدة جمال يوسف عليه السلام حتى دهشن وسقط إحساسهن وعن مثل هذه الحالة تعبر الصوفية بأنه قد فنى عن نفسه ومهما فنى عن نفسه فهو عن غيره أفنى فكأنه فنى عن كل شيء إلا عن الواحد المشهود وفنى أيضا عن الشهود فإن القلب أيضا إذا التفت إلى الشهود وإلى نفسه بأنه مشاهد فقد غفل عن المشهود فالمستهتر بالمرئي لا التفات له في حال استغراقه إلى رؤيته ولا إلى عينه التي بها رؤيته ولا إلى قلبه الذي به لذته فالسكران لا خبر له من سكره والمتلذذ لا خبر له من التذاذه وإنم", "english": "**The second meaning** — that he descends it upon himself with respect to God Most High. For when he reflects, his knowledge is ignorance, since {«ما قدروا الله حق قدره»} (They did not measure God with His true measure) [Al-Anʿām 6:91]; and his obedience is ostentation (riyāʾ), since he does not {«يتقي الله حق تقاته»} (fear God as He deserves to be feared) [Āl ʿImrān 3:102]; and his love is defective, since he does not abandon any of his lusts in his love [of God]. And whoever God desires good for, He shows him the faults of his own soul, so he sees the confirmation of this verse in himself, even if he is upon a [high] rank in relation to the heedless. For this reason, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"I do not enumerate praise upon You; You are as You have praised Yourself.\" (2) And he, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"I indeed seek God's forgiveness seventy times in the day and the night.\" (3) His seeking forgiveness was only for states that are degrees [of closeness] in relation to what is beyond them, even though they are closeness in relation to what precedes them. For there is no closeness except that behind it remains a closeness that has no end, since the path of journeying to God Most High is without termination, and reaching the utmost limits of closeness is impossible.", "book_title": "Audition and Ecstasy", "section_title_ar": "Section 505", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 505: On the Hidden Maladies of Praise and Blame (Continued)", "section_index": 505, "anchors": "- Root: سرر (s-r-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The concealed essence of a thing; that which is hidden from perception, whether good or evil.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-sirr (secret) is that which is concealed in the heart, and its plural asrār denotes the innermost hidden realities of the soul's states.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah) for what is veiled from the senses; metaphorical (majāz) for the hidden motives and subtle deceptions of the self.\n- Root: عيب (ʿ-ī-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: A defect, blemish, or imperfection; to find fault with something, exposing its deficiency.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the theological context, ʿayb denotes moral and spiritual deficiency that distances the servant from God, often concealed by self-deception.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical blemish; metaphorical for moral faults that the soul conceals from itself.\n- Root: شهد (sh-h-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To witness, to be present; shuhūd is presence with the eye or the heart.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الشهود والشهادة: الحضور مع المشاهدة، إما بالبصر، أو بالبصيرة\" — witnessing is presence with observation, either by the eye or by inner insight (basīrah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical presence; metaphorical for the heart's absorption in contemplation of the Divine, where the witness is annihilated in the witnessed.\n- Root: فني (f-n-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To perish, to cease; fanāʾ is the passing away of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In the Sufi lexicon, fanāʾ ʿan al-nafs is the passing away of self-awareness, not ontological annihilation, but the cessation of attending to oneself.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Metaphorical (majāz) for the extinction of sensory and self-referential perception in the state of total absorption.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction and Specification) — The particle إنما restricts predication, and the construction \"فكأنه فنى عن كل شيء إلا عن الواحد المشهود\" employs exception (istithnāʾ) to affirm total annihilation save the One Witnessed, a syntactic structure that emphasizes exclusive focus.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Audition and Ecstasy'", "badge": "Insight"}], "53": [{"arabic": "قال الله تعالى إخبارا عن يوسف عليه السلام أو امرأة العزيز {وما أبرئ نفسي إن النفس لأمارة بالسوء} وقد يجوز أن يقال المراد بالأمارة بالسوء هي النفس بالمعنى الأول فإذن النفس بالمعنى الأول مذمومة غاية الذم وبالمعنى الثاني محمودة لأنها نفس الإنسان أي ذاته وحقيقته العالمة بالله تعالى وسائر المعلومات اللفظ الرابع العقل وهو أيضا مشترك لمعان مختلفة ذكرناها في كتاب العلم والمتعلق بغرضنا من جملتها معنيان أحدهما أنه قد يطلق ويراد به العلم بحقائق الأمور فيكون عبارة عن صفة العلم الذي محله القلب والثاني أنه قد يطلق ويراد به المدرك للعلوم فيكون هو الق", "english": "The second meaning [of nafs] is the subtle reality (al-laṭīfah) which we have mentioned — that which is truly the human being. It is the soul of man and his very essence (dhāt), but it is described by different attributes according to the variation of its states. When it settles under the command [of God] and the agitation caused by the opposition of the passions departs from it, it is called the tranquil soul (al-nafs al-muṭma'innah). God Most High said concerning its like: {«يَا أَيَّتُهَا النَّفْسُ الْمُطْمَئِنَّةُ ارْجِعِي إِلَىٰ رَبِّكِ رَاضِيَةً مَّرْضِيَّةً»} — \"O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, well-pleased and well-pleasing.\" But the soul in the first meaning cannot be conceived to return to God Most High, for it is banished far from God and is of the party of Satan.", "book_title": "Disciplining the Soul", "section_title_ar": "Section 574", "section_title_en": "The Comprehensive Principle of Blameworthy Traits and the True Nature of the Soul, Spirit, and Intellect", "section_index": 574, "anchors": "- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, breath; that which animates and individuates a being\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-nafs denotes the rūḥ (spirit) in certain Quranic usages, but also the very dhāt (essence/self) of a thing—as in {«وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ»} where \"His Self\" means His Essence, not a separate entity\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes the blood of life (\"nafs sā'ilah\" — flowing blood); metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to the inner self, the eye of envy, and the puerperal woman\n- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn over, to flip, to transform from one state to another\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Taqlīb is the constant turning and disposition of a thing from one state to another; the heart is so named because of its perpetual fluctuation of states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: turning a thing over, inverting it; Metaphorical: the heart as the seat of understanding and discernment—\"قلب المعلم الصبيان\" (the teacher turns the boys [toward their homes]) extends to directing the intellect\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge, perception, discernment; the mark or sign by which something is known\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): ʿIlm is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality (idrāk al-shay' bi-ḥaqīqatihi)—two kinds: (1) apprehension of the essence of a thing, (2) judgment upon a thing affirming or denying something of it\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to know, to be aware of; also used for the landmarks (aʿlām) and traces by which one is guided on the path\n- Root: انس ('-n-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To perceive, to become familiar with, to find comfort in\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The ins (human) is so called for his sociability and perceptive nature, contrasted with the jinn (from tajannun — hiddenness)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to find comfort and familiarity with someone; Metaphorical: \"ibn urns\" — the intimate companion, the special confidant\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The rule governing the permissibility of interposing elements between a governing word and its governed prepositional phrase, relevant here for parsing the grammatical relationships in complex attributive constructions distinguishing the various referents of the terms under discussion.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Disciplining the Soul'", "badge": "Insight"}], "55": [{"arabic": "الله عليه وسلم فيما أخبر عنه الرب تعالى اجعلني على خزائن الأرض إني حفيظ عليم فإنه طلب المنزلة في قلبه بكونه حفيظا عليما وكان", "english": "If you say: \"His seeking of rank and status in the heart of his teacher, his servant, his companion, and his sovereign — and of anyone with whom his affair is tied — is it permissible absolutely, however it may be? Or is it permissible up to a specific limit, in a specific manner?\" — I say: This is sought in three modes: two modes are permissible and one mode is prohibited.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Status and Ostentation", "section_title_ar": "Section 801", "section_title_en": "Exposition of What is Praiseworthy in the Love of Status (Jāh) and What is Blameworthy", "section_index": 801, "anchors": "- Root: ج-و-ه (J-W-H)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is \"face\" or \"countenance\"; al-jāh (الجاه) denotes \"standing, dignity, rank, or status\" — the weight one carries in the eyes of others.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-jāh is that which grants a person eminence and consideration among people; it is a relational quality subsisting in the hearts of others, not an intrinsic property of the self.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"وجاهة\" = honor/respect. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"فلان له جاه\" = he possesses influence and intercessory power; the term is transferred from the physical face (which faces people) to the social standing by which one \"faces\" others with authority.\n- Root: م-ل-ك (M-L-K)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To possess, to have dominion over something; to grasp and control.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الملك: possession and disposal over a thing.\" When applied to hearts, it signifies the capacity to direct and dispose over the affections and wills of others.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: ownership of property. Metaphorical: \"ملكت قلبه\" — one has taken possession of another's heart, i.e., gained mastery over their inclination.\n- Root: ق-ل-ب (Q-L-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; also \"to turn over, to flip, to transform.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The heart is so named because of its constant turning (تقلب) between states; it is the seat of perception and intention.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the physical organ. Metaphorical: the locus of understanding, will, and affection — \"فلان في قلبي محل\" = he holds a station in my heart.\n- Root: ن-ز-ل (N-Z-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"To descend, to alight, to settle.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النزول: انحطاط من علو\" — descent from a height; also \"to settle in a place.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical descent. Metaphorical: \"نزل فلان من قلبي منزلة\" — he has taken up a station in my heart; the heart is conceived as a dwelling-place in which persons \"alight\" at varying degrees of honor.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين المبتدأ والخبر (Interposition between Subject and Predicate) — The periodic structure \"مهما عرفت أن...\" (Whenever you know that...) establishes a conditional frame governing the entire ensuing argument, requiring the translator to preserve the logical subordination across long sentences without fragmenting the author's unified reasoning.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of Status and Ostentation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "56": [{"arabic": "فإذن جميع أقطار ملكوت السموات والأرض ميدان العارف يتبوأ منه حيث يشاء من غير حاجة إلى أن يتحرك إليها بجسمه وشخصه فهو من مطالعة جمال الملكوت في جنة عرضها السموات والأرض وكل عارف فله مثلها من غير أن يضيق بعضهم على بعض أصلا إلا أنهم يتفاوتون في سعة منتزهاتهم بقدر تفاوتهم في اتساع نظرهم", "english": "And just as the pleasure of leadership and honor is the most dominant of pleasures over the one who has surpassed the deficiency of childhood and imbecility, so too the pleasure of knowing Allah Most High, contemplating the beauty of the Presence of Lordship, and gazing upon the secrets of divine matters is more pleasurable than leadership — which is itself the highest of the pleasures that dominate creation. The utmost expression of it is to say: {«فَلَا تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ مِنْ قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ»} — \"No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort of the eyes\" — and that He has prepared for them {«مَا لَا عَيْنٌ رَأَتْ وَلَا أُذُنٌ سَمِعَتْ وَلَا خَطَرَ عَلَى قَلْبِ بَشَرٍ»} — \"what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any human being.\"", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "section_title_ar": "Section 1159", "section_title_en": "Exposition that the Most Sublime and Highest of Pleasures is Knowledge of Allah Most High and the Contemplation of His Noble Countenance, and that No Other Pleasure Can Be Conceived to Outweigh It Save for One Who Has Been Deprived of This Very Pleasure", "section_index": 1159, "anchors": "- Root: لذذ (Ladhdh)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core sensory delight, sweetness, and gratification experienced through the faculties.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Pleasure (al-ladhdhah) as the perception of what is agreeable and harmonious with one's nature; its highest form is intellectual and spiritual, not merely corporeal.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) for sensory delights; Metaphorical (Majaz) extension to intellectual and spiritual joys, such as dominance (al-ghalabah) and knowledge (al-ʿilm).\n- Root: عرف (ʿArf)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To know by tracing effects and signs; cognizance through reflection.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Maʿrifah is the perception of a thing through reflection and contemplation of its trace; it is more specific than ʿilm and is the mode by which creatures know Allah—through His effects, not His essence.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal sense of recognition; here applied to the highest theological act of contemplative knowledge of the Divine.\n- Root: غلب (Ghalab)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To overcome, conquer, or dominate.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Ghalabah is qahr (compelling subjugation); victory of one over another.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical conquest; Metaphorical: the pleasure of intellectual and spiritual supremacy (riyāsah) over others.\n- Root: صور (Ṣūr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Form, shape, image.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Two types of form: sensible (perceived by the senses) and intelligible (perceived by the intellect alone); the latter is the higher, pertaining to spiritual realities.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical form; Metaphorical: inclination and turning of the heart toward a beloved object.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Focused Predication (al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā) — Used to delimit the exclusive superiority of divine knowledge over all other pleasures, and to structure conditional contrasts (law khuyyira... fa-in) for logical demonstration.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الدرجات قال الله عز وجل {وكذلك مكنا ليوسف في الأرض} وأيوب عليه السلام بعد المحنة العظيمة مكن قال الله تعالى وآتيناه أهله ومثلهم معهم الآية فهذا الكلام من الشافعي رحمه الله يدل على تبحره في أسرار القرآن واطلاعه على مقامات السائرين إلى الله تعالى من الأنبياء والأولياء وكل ذلك من علوم الآخرة وقيل للشافعي رحمه الله متى يكون الرجل عالما قال إذا تحقق في علم الدين فعلمه وتعرض لسائر العلوم فنظر فيما فاته فعند ذلك يكون عالما فإنه قيل لجالينوس إنك تأمر للداء الواحد بالأدوية الكثيرة المجمعة فقال إنما المقصود م", "english": "And al-Shafi'i, may God Most High have mercy upon him, said: \"If you fear for your deed the blight of self-admiration (al-ʿujb), then consider: whose pleasure do you seek? Toward what reward do you yearn? From what punishment do you flee? What well-being do you thank? And what affliction do you recall? For if you reflect upon even one of these five qualities, your deed will appear small in your eyes.\" Observe how he mentioned the reality of ostentation and the remedy for self-admiration—both being among the gravest maladies of the heart.", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "section_title_ar": "Section 21", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 21: The Sciences of the Hereafter and the Signs of Sincere Intention in Knowledge", "section_index": 21, "anchors": "- Root: مكن (m-k-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of establishing, empowering, and granting firm footing in a place or station.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"المكان عند أهل اللغة: الموضع الحاوي للشيء\" — the place that encompasses a thing; theological nuance: divine empowerment (tamkīn) as a station granted after trial.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"مكنته من الشيء وأمكنته منه، فتمكن منه واستمكن\" — physical enabling. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"الناس على مكناتهم: على مقارهم\" — people upon their settled abodes/stations; here, the spiritual station of the prophets after tribulation.\n- Root: محن (m-ḥ-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Testing, refining, and proving; a worn garment (mamḥūn) that has been stretched and expanded by use.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"المحن والامتحان نحو الابتلاء\" — trial and testing akin to affliction; Quranic: {فامتحنوهن} (Al-Mumtahanah: 10) — the testing of hearts for sincerity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"وقع في محنة ومحن\" — falling into trial. Metaphorical: \"محن الأديم: مدده حتى وسعه\" — stretching hide until it widens; thus {امتحن الله قلوبهم} — God expands and purifies the heart through trial.\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge as the apprehension of a thing's reality; the mark (ʿalam) by which one is guided.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العلم: إدراك الشيء بحقيقته\" — knowledge is the perception of a thing in its true reality; two types: apprehension of essence, and judgment of existence or negation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"ما علمت بخبرك: ما شعرت به\" — to be aware. Metaphorical: \"خفيت معالم الطريق\" — the traces of the path that guide the seeker; here, the signs (ʿalāmāt) of sincere intention.\n- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Turning, overturning, and transforming a thing from one state to another.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — the heart as that which is constantly turned and transformed; the seat of spiritual perception.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — physical overturning. Metaphorical: \"قلب التاجر السلعة\" — the merchant scrutinizing his goods; \"رجل قلب حول: يقلب الأمور\" — one who turns matters over; here, the heart's gaze upon its own intentions.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to confine a predicate to a single subject, as in \"إنما المقصود منها واحد\" (the intended aim is but one), emphasizing exclusive focus.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}], "67": [{"arabic": "الأقربين} فقال يا عباس ويا صفية عمي النبي ويا فاطمة بنت محمد إني لست أغني عنكم من الله شيئا إن لي عملي ولكم عملكم (3) وقد قال عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه لا يقيم أمر الناس إلا حصيف العقل أريب العقد لا يطلع منه على عورة ولا يخاف منه على حرة ولا تأخذه في الله لومة لائم وقال الأمراء أربعة فأمير قوي ظلف نفسه وعماله فذلك كالمجاهد في سبيل الله يد الله باسطة عليه بالرحمة وأمير فيه ضعف ظلف نفسه وأرتع عماله لضعفه فهو على شفا هلاك إلا أن يرحمه الله وأمير ظلف عماله وأرتع نفسه فذلك الحطمة الذي قال فيه رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم شر الرع", "english": "He turned to al-Shaʿbī and said: \"O Abā ʿAmr! I am the trustee of the Commander of the Faithful over Iraq and his governor over it, and a man commanded to obedience. I have been tried with the subjects, and their right has become incumbent upon me. So I love to preserve them and to attend to what sets them right, along with sincere counsel (naṣīḥah) to them. And reports may reach me about a band of people from the regions concerning a matter, and I find myself severe against them therein, so I withhold a portion of their stipends and place it in the treasury (bayt al-māl), with the intention in myself that I shall return it to them. Then it reaches the Commander of the Faithful that I have withheld it in that manner, so he writes to me that I must not return it. I cannot then countermand his order, nor can I execute his letter [against my better judgment]. I am but a man commanded to obedience. Is there any liability upon me in this, and in similar matters, where the intention is as I have described?\"", "book_title": "Enjoining Good and Forbidding Evil", "section_title_ar": "Section 553", "section_title_en": "The Upright Scholars Before the Tyrannical Rulers — Counsel and Fearless Truth-Telling", "section_index": 553, "anchors": "- Root: نصح (naṣaḥa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is sincerity, faithfulness, and pure counsel free from deceit; the root denotes the act of seeking the welfare of another with complete integrity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological context, naṣīḥah is the obligation of the sincere advisor to guide the ruler toward divine truth, even at personal peril, as it is a form of worship (ʿibādah) and a trust (amānah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage denotes pure honey (ʿasal naṣīḥ) free from admixture; metaphorical (majāz) usage applies to counsel that is untainted by flattery or self-interest.\n- Root: سلط (sulṭ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Denotes authority, power, and dominion; the ruler (sulṭān) is one who has been given sway over affairs.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In Kalam, sulṭān is a trial (ibtilāʾ) and a trust (amānah) from God, whose exercise demands justice (ʿadl) and whose neglect invites divine wrath.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage refers to physical power or a governing authority; metaphorical usage extends to the authority of proof (sulṭān al-burhān) that compels assent.\n- Root: عظ (waʿaẓa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes admonition, exhortation, and reminding of consequences; it implies softening the heart through remembrance of God and the Hereafter.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological terms, ʿiẓah is the act of turning the soul away from transgression through a blend of fear (tarhīb) and hope (targhīb), grounded in revealed truth.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is the verbal admonition; metaphorical usage is the admonition of circumstance (ʿiẓah al-ḥāl) when events themselves teach a lesson.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Focused Predication (bāb al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd bi-innamā) — Governing the emphasis of exclusive predication in statements of counsel, such as \"No obedience to a creature in disobedience of the Creator,\" where the restriction (ḥaṣr) is achieved through negation and exception (nafy wa istithnāʾ).", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Enjoining Good and Forbidding Evil'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فإن قلت فقد قال صلى الله عليه وسلم بعد قوله لفاطمة وصفية إني لا أغني عنكما من الله شيئا إلا أن لكم رحما سأبلها ببلالها (1) حديث أترجو سليم شفاعتي ولا ترجوها بنو عبد المطلب أخرجه الطبراني في الأوسط من حديث عبد الله بن جعفر وفيه أصيرم بن حوشب عن إسحاق بن واصل وكلاهما ضعيف جدا فذلك يدل على أنه سيخصص قرابته بالشفاعة فاعلم أن كل مسلم فهو منتظر شفاعة رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم والنسيب أيضا جدير بأن يرجوها لكن بشرط أن يتقي الله أن يغضب عليه فإنه إن يغضب عليه فلا يأذن لأحد في شفاعته لأن الذنوب منقسمة إلى ما يوجب المقت فلا يؤذن في ال", "english": "If you say: \"He, peace and blessings be upon him, said after his words to Fāṭimah and Ṣafiyyah: 'I cannot avail you against God in anything, except that you have a tie of kinship which I will moisten with its moisture'\" — a ḥadīth [reported as]: \"Do you hope for my intercession, while the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib do not hope for it?\" — narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ from the narration of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, and in it is Uṣayrim ibn Ḥawshab from Isḥāq ibn Wāṣil, and both are extremely weak — so that indicates that he will single out his relatives for intercession.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Pride and Conceit", "section_title_ar": "Section 882", "section_title_en": "Section 882 — On the Limits of Intercession, the Vices of Pride in Lineage, Numbers, Wealth, and Opinion, and Their Treatment", "section_index": 882, "anchors": "- Root: شفع (Sh-F-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is pairing or joining; intercession (shafā'ah) is the joining of one's plea to another's cause.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Intercession is the seeking of benefit for another; its acceptance is contingent upon divine permission and good pleasure, as restricted by the Qur'anic qualifiers.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah) is the act of making a number even (from watr, odd); metaphorical (majāz) is the mediator's plea before authority.\n- Root: عجب (ʿ-J-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Astonishment arising from an unknown cause; self-admiration (ʿujb) is a blameworthy state of being pleased with oneself.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العجب والتعجب: حالة تعرض للإنسان عند الجهل بسبب الشيء\" — a state that overtakes a person due to ignorance of the cause; hence, it is impossible regarding God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: a wondrous thing; metaphorical: the one who performs marvels (taʿjābah). Self-admiration is the root of every error and innovation.\n- Root: رأي (R-'-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Opinion, view, or judgment formed through reflection.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ra'y is the considered opinion that may err or hit the mark; it is blameworthy when it becomes an object of ʿujb (self-admiration).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: sight/vision; metaphorical: intellectual insight. The ḥadīth \"إعجاب كل ذي رأي برأيه\" (the admiration of every man of opinion for his own view) is cited as a sign of the age's corruption.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction and Qualification) — The conditional clauses (in-sharṭ) governing intercession, e.g., {إلا لمن ارتضى} and {إلا بإذنه}, impose necessary restrictions that negate any absolute reliance on intercession.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Condemnation of Pride and Conceit'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "76": [{"arabic": "كذا كذا فقال أصبت وأخطأت وفوق كل ذي علم عليم واستدرك ابن مسعود على أبي موسى الأشعري رضي الله عنهما فقال أبو موسى لا تسألوني عن شيء وهذا الحبر بين أظهركم وذلك لما سئل أبو موسى عن رجل قاتل في سبيل الله فقتل فقال هو في الجنة وكان أمير الكوفة فقام ابن مسعود فقال أعده على الأمير فلعله لم يفهم فأعادوا عليه فأعاد الجواب فقال ابن مسعود وأنا أقول إن قتل فأصاب الحق فهو في الجنة فقال أبو موسى الحق ما قال وهكذا يكون إنصاف طلب الحق ولو ذكر مثل هذا الآن لأقل فقيه لأنكره واستبعده وقال لا يحتاج إلى أن يقال", "english": "The fourth [etiquette]: that he should not dispute except over a matter that has actually occurred, or that is likely to occur in most cases. For the Companions (may God be pleased with them) did not consult one another except over newly arising incidents or what was likely to occur, such as the laws of inheritance (farāʾiḍ). And we do not see the disputants concerning themselves with critiquing questions that are of general affliction (ʿumūm al-balawā) in issuing verdicts about them; rather, they seek out the \"drum-beat\" questions (ṭubūliyyāt)—those that make noise—so that the field of argumentation widens in them, however the matter may be. PageV01P043", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "section_title_ar": "Section 37", "section_title_en": "Section 37 — On the Etiquette of Disputation and the Pursuit of Truth", "section_index": 37, "anchors": "- Root: نظر (naẓara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of gazing, examining, and deliberating with the eye of the intellect.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance of speculative reflection (naẓar) as the means to attain knowledge of the unseen and the divine.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) denotes physical sight; metaphorical (majāz) denotes intellectual consideration and weighing of evidence.\n- Root: حق (ḥaqqa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes firmness, reality, and that which is established and undeniable.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance of truth (ḥaqq) as the eternal reality of God and His commands, opposed to falsehood (bāṭil).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal denotes the opposite of falsehood; metaphorical denotes the due right and the correct ruling in a given case.\n- Root: خصم (khaṣama)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes the act of contending, disputing, and overcoming in argument.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance of the adversary (khaṣm) in debate, whose refutation is sought for the sake of truth, not vanity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal denotes the opponent in a legal contest; metaphorical denotes the one who contends against the truth with fallacious reasoning.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Focused Predication (al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd bi-innamā) — Governing the exclusive emphasis on truth-seeking over partisan victory, as in the phrase \"the object is truth alone.\"", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "ولا تقولن لشيء إني فاعل ذلك غدا إلا أن يشاء الله ثم لم يقتصر على ذلك فيما لا يشك فيه بل قال تعالى لتدخلن المسجد الحرام إن شاء الله آمنين محلقين رءؤسكم ومقصرين وكان الله سبحانه عالما بأنهم يدخلون لا محالة وأنه شاءه ولكن المقصود تعليمه ذلك فتأدب رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم في ما كان يخبر عنه معلوما كان أو مشكوكا حتى قال صلى الله عليه وسلم لما دخل المقابر السلام عليكم دار قوم مؤمنين وإنا إن شاء الله بكم لاحقون (1) واللحوق بهم غير مشكوك فيه ولكن مقتضى الأدب ذكر الله تعالى وربط الأمور به وهذه الصيغ", "english": "If you say: \"What is the meaning of the Salaf's statement, 'I am a believer, if God wills' — given that the exception (istithnā') implies doubt, and doubt in faith is unbelief? Yet they all refrained from giving an unqualified answer affirming faith and were cautious about it.\"", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 102", "section_title_en": "On the Meaning of the Salaf's Statement \"I am a Believer, If God Wills\" — Section 102", "section_index": 102, "anchors": "- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, the soul; that which is breathed; the innermost reality of a person.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): النفس is used for the rūḥ (spirit), for the dhāt (essence/self), and for the seat of intention and knowledge. When one says \"he knows in himself (nafsihi) that he is a believer,\" it denotes certitude residing in the very core of one's being, not a corporeal faculty.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage refers to the soul's reflexive self-awareness; metaphorical (majāz) usage extends to \"blood\" (dam) or \"the eye\" (ʿayn) of envy. Here, \"in himself\" (fī nafsihi) is literal self-knowledge, not mere outward profession.\n- Root: وجه (w-j-h)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Face, countenance; the foremost part; a mode, aspect, or direction.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The face is the most noble apparent part of a thing; hence it is used for the \"aspect\" or \"manner\" (wajh) of an affair. \"Four aspects\" (wujūh) means four distinct modes of interpretation or rational grounds.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the face of a person or object. Metaphorical: \"the face of the matter\" (wajh al-amr) — its most salient and honorable dimension. Here, the \"aspects\" are hermeneutical angles, not physical parts.\n- Root: ايم (a-y-m)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The unmarried state (aym); one who has no spouse. Not applicable here directly, but the root's semantic field of \"being alone/without attachment\" contrasts with īmān's root (a-m-n) — security and trust — which is the operative term in this text.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Not directly relevant; the operative root is أمن (a-m-n), meaning security from fear, and by extension, faith (īmān) as the state of being secure in God's truth.\n- Root: كان (k-w-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be, to exist; the copula of predication.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Kāna denotes existence and becoming; in theological usage, it grounds the distinction between what is (mawjūd) and what is merely asserted. The question \"Are you a believer?\" (a-mu'min anta?) uses kāna implicitly to ask about actual, present state — not future contingency.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: existence. Metaphorical: the \"being-so\" of a predicate. The istithnā' (exception) with \"in shā' Allāh\" suspends the copula's certainty, shifting from assertive existence to contingent hope.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الاستثناء والتعليق بالمشيئة (The Chapter of Exception and Suspension by the Divine Will) — When an exception clause (istithnā') follows a positive assertion, it grammatically suspends the universality or certainty of the predication. In theological discourse, this suspension may be semantic (doubt) or pragmatic (deference, etiquette, or self-deprecation), and Sibawayh's parsing of conditional suspension (taʿlīq) shows that the apodosis need not be negated — only its absolute, unqualified force is tempered.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Insight"}], "82": [{"arabic": "وقوله تعالى واسئل القرية التي كنا فيها والعير التي أقبلنا فيها أي أهل العير فالأهل فيهما محذوف مضمر وقوله عز وجل ثقلت في السموات والأرض معناه خفيت على أهل السموات والأرض والشيء إذا خفي ثقل فأبدل اللفظ به وأقيم في مقام على وأضمر الأهل وحذف وقوله تعالى وتجعلون رزقكم أنكم تكذبون أي شكر رزقكم وقوله عز وجل وآتنا ما وعدتنا على رسلك أي على ألسنة رسلك فحذف ألسنة وقوله تعالى إنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر أراد القرآن وما سبق له ذكر وقال عز وجل حتى توارت الحجاب أراد الشمس وما سبق لها ذكر وقوله تعالى والذين اتخذوا من", "english": "I say: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about the means of deliverance from these trials, and he said: \"The Book of Allah — act by what is in it, for it is that which delivers one from them.\" The questioner repeated this three times, and he (peace be upon him) said three times: \"Learn the Book of Allah, Mighty and Glorious, and act by what is in it, for in it is deliverance.\"", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 233", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Etiquette of Recitation — Section 233: On Understanding the Meanings of the Qur'an and the Limits of Interpretation", "section_index": 233, "anchors": "- Root: ف-ه-م (f-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن\" — comprehension as an inherent faculty by which one ascertains meanings\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الفهم: هيئة للإنسان بها يتحقق معاني ما يحسن... وأفهمته: إذا قلت له حتى تصوره\" — comprehension is a cognitive disposition; distinction between understanding (fahm) and making understood (ifhām)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"تقول: من لم يؤت من سوء الفهم أتى من سوء الإفهام\" — literal usage; failure of understanding often stems from failure of communication\n- Root: ف-س-ر (f-s-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"وكل شيء يعرف به تفسير الشيء ومعناه، فهو تَفْسِرَتُه\" — that by which a thing's meaning is made known\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التفسير قد يقال فيما يختص بمفردات الألفاظ وغريبها، وفيما يختص بالتأويل\" — tafsīr concerns lexical surface; taʾwīl concerns deeper meaning\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"هذا كلام يحتاج إلى فسر وتفسير\" — literal: exposition of what is obscure\n- Root: و-ج-ل (w-j-l)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the sensing of fear; used of hearts trembling at divine mention\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"لو واجلت فلانا لوجلته: لغلبته في الوجل\" — literal sense of fear; metaphorical extension to overpowering in fear\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — the particle innamā restricts predication, essential for parsing the Prophet's saying \"innamā al-aʿmālu bi-l-niyyāt\" and analogous restrictive formulations in the ḥadīth cited herein", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "87": [{"arabic": "قبل أن يقنطوا فيهلكوا فإنه لا ييأس من روح الله إلا القوم الكافرون قال فما تم كلامه حتى ارتفعت السماء مثل الجبال", "english": "And Ibn al-Mubārak said: \"I arrived in Medina in a year of severe drought, and the people went out to pray for rain (istisqāʾ). I went out with them, when a black youth approached, wearing two pieces of sackcloth — he had wrapped one around his waist and cast the other over his shoulder. He sat beside me, and I heard him say: 'O Allah, the faces have worn out before You due to the abundance of sins and the evils of deeds. And You have withheld from us the rain of the sky to discipline Your servants by that. So I ask You — O Forbearing One, Possessor of Clemency, O He from Whom His servants know nothing but the Beautiful — to give them drink, this very hour, this very hour.' He kept saying 'this very hour, this very hour' until the sky became clothed with clouds, and the rain came from every direction.\"", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 243", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 243: On the States of the Scholar with Tyrannical Rulers (Continued)", "section_index": 243, "anchors": "- Root: ج و ع (j-w-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of hunger/emptiness of the belly; the opposite of fullness (shabaʿ).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used both literally (hunger of the stomach) and metaphorically (spiritual want or deprivation).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) for bodily hunger; metaphorical (majāz) for the soul's yearning or deprivation.\n- Root: س ه ر (s-h-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Wakefulness, sleeplessness; the opposite of sleep (nawm).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological usage, wakefulness of the heart in vigilance (murāqabah) and devotion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical sleeplessness; metaphorical for the heart's alertness in worship, as in the verse cited.\n- Root: خ ل ق (kh-l-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To create, to measure, to fashion; also to wear out (as in a garment).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Creation (ījād) from nothing; also the wearing out of faces through prolonged exposure — here, the \"wearing out\" of faces before Allah due to sins.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for fashioning; metaphorical for the state of being worn/exhausted (as in the supplication \"akhlaqat al-wujūh\" — the faces have worn out).\n- Root: غ و ث (gh-w-th)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To come to the aid of one in distress; succor, relief (ghiyāth).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Divine succor in times of calamity; the response to a cry for help (istighāthah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for responding to a call for aid; metaphorical for sending rain as divine relief.\n- Root: ق ن ط (q-n-ṭ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To despair, to lose hope; the opposite of hope (rajāʾ).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Despair of Allah's mercy — a characteristic of the disbelievers, as in the Quranic verse cited.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for hopelessness; metaphorical for the spiritual ruin that follows from abandoning trust in Allah.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Interposition (al-Faṣl bayna al-Jār wa al-Majrūr) — The separation between the preposition and its object for rhetorical emphasis, as in the supplications where the vocative and oath constructions are interposed for heightened urgency.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Insight"}], "90": [{"arabic": "فتح الباب والله لا يضيع أجر المحسنين وإن تك حسنة يضاعفها ويؤت من لدنه أجرا عظيما المقام الثاني في دفع العارض منه في أثناء العبادة وذلك لا بد من تعلمه أيضا فإن من جاهد نفسه وقلع مغارس الرياء من قلبه بالقناعة وقطع الطمع وإسقاط نفسه من أعين المخلوقين واستحقار مدح المخلوقين وذمهم فالشيطان لا يتركه في أثناء العبادات بل يعارضه بخطرات الرياء ولا تنقطع عنه نزعاته وهوى النفس وميلها لا ينمحي بالكلية فلا بد وأن يتشمر لدفع ما يعرض من خاطر الرياء وخواطر الرياء ثلاثة قد تخطر دفعة واحدة كالخاطر ال", "english": "So when the harm and injury of these causes is firmly settled in his heart, his desire [for them] slackens, and his heart turns toward God. For the intelligent person does not covet that whose harm is abundant and whose benefit is scant. It suffices him that if people knew what is in his inner self—the intent of ostentation (riyā') and the display of sincerity—they would abhor him. And God will surely expose his secret until He makes him odious to the people and makes them know that he is a show-off, abhorrent to God. Had he been sincere to God, God would have unveiled his sincerity to them, made him beloved to them, subjected them to him, and loosened their tongues in praise and commendation of him—even though there is no perfection in their praise, nor deficiency in their blame. As the poet of Banī Tamīm said: \"My praise is an adornment, and my blame is a disgrace.\" The Messenger of God (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \"You have lied—that belongs to God, there is no deity but Him.\" // [Hadith: A poet of Banī Tamīm said, \"My praise is an adornment, and my blame is a disgrace.\" He (the Prophet) said: \"You have lied—that belongs to God.\" Ahmad narrated it from the hadith of al-Aqra' ibn Ḥābis—who was the speaker of that verse, excluding the phrase \"You have lied\"—and its narrators are trustworthy, except that I do not know of Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān having heard [directly] from al-Aqra'. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it from the hadith of al-Barā' and deemed it sound (ḥasan), with the wording: \"A man said, 'Indeed, my praise...'\"]", "book_title": "Condemnation of Status and Ostentation", "section_title_ar": "Section 827", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 827: The Second Station: Repelling the Accidental Promptings of Ostentation During Worship", "section_index": 827, "anchors": "- Root: كذب (kadhaba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning: falsehood, lying, saying what is contrary to reality; also used for \"to declare someone a liar.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological context, kadhb is the antithesis of sidq (truthfulness); it is a moral and epistemic vice, often linked to hypocrisy (nifāq) and false claims.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqīqah): to report what did not occur. Metaphorical (majāz): attributing to God what is unworthy of Him, as in the Prophet's rebuke of the poet's self-praise.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Predicate Emphasis (Bāb al-Tawkīd) — The Prophet's reply \"كَذَبْتَ\" (You have lied) functions as an emphatic categorical refutation, structured as a nominal sentence with implied subject, establishing a permanent verdict rather than a transient rebuke.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of Status and Ostentation'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "الصبر والتقوى صيرا العبيد ملوكا فقال يوسف كما أخبر الله تعالى عنه {إنه من يتق ويصبر فإن الله لا يضيع أجر المحسنين} وقال الجنيد أرقت ليلة فقمت إلى وردي فلم أجد الحلاوة التي كنت أجدها فأردت أن أنام فلم أقدر فجلست فلم أطق الجلوس فخرجت فإذا رجل ملتف في عباءة مطروح على الطريق فلما أحس بي قال يا أبا القاسم إلى الساعة فقلت يا سيدي من غير موعد قال بلى سألت الله عز وجل إن يحرك لي قلبك فقلت قد فعل فما حاجتك قال فمتى يصير داء النفس دواءها فقلت إذا خالفت النفس هواها فأقبل على نفسه فقال اسمعي فقد أجبتك بهذا سبع مرات فأبيت أن تسمعيه إلا من الجنيدها قد سمعتيه ث", "english": "But if you are incapable of that, then it behooves you not to let slip the affirmation of truth (taṣdīq) and faith (īmān) by way of receptive acceptance (talqqī) and emulation (taqlīd) of one who deserves to be emulated. For faith has a degree, just as knowledge has a degree; and knowledge is attained after faith, and it lies beyond it. God, the Exalted, said: {«يرفع الله الذين آمنوا منكم والذين أوتوا العلم درجات»} — \"God will raise those who have believed among you and those who have been given knowledge, by degrees.\" So whoever affirms as true that opposing the desires (mukhālafat al-shahawāt) is the road to God, the Mighty and Majestic, yet has not been apprised of its cause and its secret — he is among those who believe. And when he is apprised of what we have mentioned concerning the helpers of the desires, he is among those who have been given knowledge. And to both has God promised the goodly reward.", "book_title": "Breaking the Two Desires", "section_title_ar": "Section 627", "section_title_en": "Section 627 — The Path of Opposition to the Desires: On the Consensus of the Scholars that There Is No Road to the Happiness of the Hereafter Save through Restraining the Soul from Caprice", "section_index": 627, "anchors": "- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, spirit; that which breathes; the animating principle; also blood, and the \"evil eye\" (nafs sā'ilah)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): النفس: الروح — the soul as the spiritual reality; in the verse {«ويحذركم الله نفسه»} it denotes the very Essence (al-dhāt); the soul is that which must be disciplined and opposed in its caprice (hawā)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the self that desires and inclines; Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه\" — he poured out his blood/life; the soul as the internal adversary that must be fought (jihād al-nafs)\n- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; to turn over, to transform, to fluctuate; the heart as that which is constantly turning between states\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه — the heart is so named because of its constant turning and fluctuation between conditions; the seat of spiritual perception and disease\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to turn something over; Metaphorical: the heart as the organ of spiritual understanding that can be veiled (maḥjūbah) from God by attachment to desires\n- Root: دنا (d-n-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be near, proximity; the world (al-dunyā) as that which is nearer/lower\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الدنو: القرب بالذات أو بالحكم — proximity by essence or by judgment; the world as the nearer realm that veils from the distant (al-ākhirah)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: closeness; Metaphorical: the lower world as that which is \"near\" and thus preoccupies the heart from what is higher\n- Root: أكل (a-k-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To eat, consume; also to possess and enjoy\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Eating as the most fundamental desire; the restriction of food (qillat al-ṭa'ām) as the first pillar of spiritual discipline (riyāḍah)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: consumption of food; Metaphorical: \"أكل الشهوات\" — the devouring of desires as that which veils the intellect from God\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The periodic sentence structure in which the author interposes explanatory clauses between the subject and its predicate, as in \"فإنه لو تمتع بشيء منه أنس به وألفه\" where the conditional clause governs the entire following apodosis, requiring careful tracking of the protasis-apodosis relationship through extended digressions.\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Breaking the Two Desires'", "badge": "Insight"}], "92": [{"arabic": "عليه وسلم أقول كما قال يوسف {لا تثريب عليكم اليوم يغفر الله لكم وهو أرحم} {الراحمين} (1) قال فخرجوا كأنما نشروا من القبور فدخلوا في الإسلام وعن سهيل بن عمرو قال لما قدم رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم مكة وضع يديه على باب الكعبة والناس حوله فقال لا إله إلا الله وحده لا شريك له صدق وعده ونصر عبده وهزم الأحزاب وحده {ثم قال} يا معشر قريش ما تقولون وما تظنون قال قلت يا رسول الله نقول خيرا ونظن خيرا أخ كريم وابن عم رحيم وقد قدرت فقال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أقول كما قال أخي يوسف {لا تثريب عليكم اليوم يغفر الله لكم}", "english": "Know that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said, as related by Anas (may God be pleased with him) in a tradition transmitted by Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Ḥanafī as a suspended (mursal) report: \"When God—mighty and majestic—gathers the creatures on the Day of Resurrection, a herald will call out from beneath the Throne with three calls: 'O company of monotheists! Verily God has pardoned you, so let some of you pardon others.'\" This was transmitted by Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muqrī in his book *al-Tabṣirah wa al-Tadhkirah* with the wording: \"A herald will call out from the innermost depths of the Throne on the Day of Resurrection: 'O community of Muḥammad! Verily God Most High says: Whatever was due to Me from you, I have bestowed it upon you as a gift. But the claims of one another remain—so forgive one another mutually, and enter Paradise through My mercy.'\" Its chain of transmission is weak. Al-Ṭabarānī related it in *al-Awsaṭ* with the wording: \"A herald will call out: 'O people of the Gathering! Mutually acknowledge the wrongs among yourselves, and your reward is upon Me.'\" And he related from the ḥadīth of Umm Hāniʾ: \"A herald will call out: 'O people of monotheism! Let some of you pardon others, and the reward is upon Me.'\"", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "section_title_ar": "Section 714", "section_title_en": "The Book of Pardon (Kitāb al-ʿAfw) — Section 714", "section_index": 714, "anchors": "- Root: ع ف و (ʿ-f-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"عفا: ترك الذنب وأعرض عنه؛ والعفو: التجاوز عن الذنب، وأصله المحو والطمس\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"العفو: التجافي عن الذنب، وهو أبلغ من الغفران لأنه يقتضي ترك المؤاخذة مع زوال أثر الذنب\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: عفا عن ذنبه: تجاوز عنه. Metaphorical: عفا الأثر: درَس وامّحى — فالعفو محو الذنب كأنه لم يكن\"\n- Root: ث ل ب (th-l-b) — as in \"لا تثريب\"\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الثرب: الشحم الرقيق الذي يغشى الكرش؛ والتثريب: التعيير والتوبيخ على الذنب\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"التثريب: أشد اللوم والتعنيف، ومنه قوله تعالى {لا تثريب عليكم اليوم} أي لا تعيير ولا توبيخ\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: ثرّبه: وبّخه وعيّره. Metaphorical: لا تثريب: إزالة أثر الذنب بالكلية كإزالة الشحم الرقيق\"\n- Root: م ظ ل م (ẓ-l-m)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"المظلمة: حق الغير الذي ظُلم صاحبه فيه، وجمعها مظالم\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: ظلمه: نقصه حقه. Metaphorical: المظالم: الحقوق التي غُصبت، وتناكُر المظالم: معرفة كل واحد مظلمته ليتحلل منها\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of interposing elements between the preposition and its object when the meaning remains clear, as in \"من تحت العرش\" where the spatial specification follows the prepositional phrase.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "لا تثريب عليكم اليوم يغفر الله لكم وهو أرحم الراحمين يعرض للحكم بالعفو عن أصحابه قال الحكم فأنا أقول لا تثريب عليكم اليوم ولو لم أجد إلا ثوبي هذا لواريتكم تحته وكتب ابن المقفع إلى صديق له يسأله العفو عن بعض إخوانه فلان هارب من زلته إلى عفوك لائذ منك بك واعلم أنه لن يزداد الذنب عظما إلا ازداد العفو فضلا وأتى عبد الملك بن مروان بأسارى ابن الأشعث فقال لرجاء بن حيوة ما ترى قال إن الله تعالى قد أعطاك ما تحب من الظفر فأعط الله ما يحب من العفو فعفا عنهم وروي أن زياد أخذ رجلا من الخوارج فأفلت منه فأخذ أخا له فقال ل", "english": "A man was brought to Hishām concerning whom word had reached him. When he was made to stand before him, he began to speak in his own defense. Hishām said to him: You speak as well? The man said: O Commander of the Faithful, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: {«يَوْمَ تَأْتِي كُلُّ نَفْسٍ تُجَادِلُ عَنْ نَفْسِهَا»} — \"The Day when every soul will come disputing on its own behalf.\" Shall we dispute before Allah the Exalted, and not speak a word before you? Hishām said: Yes, woe to you — speak.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "section_title_ar": "Section 715", "section_title_en": "** Section 715 — On the Virtue of Forbearance (al-Ḥilm) and Gentleness (al-Rifq)", "section_index": 715, "anchors": "**\n\n- **Root: عفو (ʿ-F-W)**\n  - *Lisan / Ayn:* Al-ʿAfw is the effacing and obliteration of the trace of a thing; to pardon is to efface the trace of the offense entirely.\n  - *Al-Raghib (Mufradat):* Al-ʿAfw is the erasure of the sin such that no consequence remains — it is the highest form of forgiveness, surpassing al-ghufrān which veils but does not necessarily efface.\n  - *Al-Zamakhshari (Asas):* Literal: \"عفا الأثر\" — the trace was effaced. Metaphorical: pardon as the effacing of the offense's consequence, as in \"عفا عن ذنبه.\"\n\n- **Root: حلم (Ḥ-L-M)**\n  - *Lisan / Ayn:* Al-Ḥilm is forbearance, clemency, and the restraint of the soul from agitation upon provocation.\n  - *Al-Raghib (Mufradat):* Al-Ḥilm is the soul's composure and its withholding from haste; it is a virtue opposed to al-ṭaysh (levity) and al-jahl (foolishness) — not ignorance, but the deliberate restraint of passion.\n  - *Al-Zamakhshari (Asas):* Literal: dreams (aḥlām) share the root — the state of being unmoved. Metaphorical: the forbearing man (ḥalīm) whose soul does not stir toward vengeance when provoked.\n\n- **Root: رفق (R-F-Q)**\n  - *Lisan / Ayn:* Al-Rifq is gentleness, lenity, and the opposite of violence (al-ʿunf).\n  - *Al-Raghib (Mufradat):* Al-Rifq is the disposition toward ease and gentleness in all affairs; it is praised by the Law and is a quality of the prophets.\n  - *Al-Zamakhshari (Asas):* Literal: \"رفق به\" — he was gentle with him. Metaphorical: gentleness in conduct as a mode of spiritual excellence.\n\n- **Root: صفح (Ṣ-F-Ḥ)**\n  - *Lisan / Ayn:* Al-Ṣafḥ is turning away from an offense and meeting it with a generous countenance; from ṣafḥah (cheek/face) — to turn one's face away from the wrong.\n  - *Al-Raghib (Mufradat):* Al-Ṣafḥ is the overlooking of the offense combined with graciousness — it is more than mere pardon, for it includes magnanimity (al-Ifḍāl).\n  - *Al-Zamakhshari (Asas):* Literal: \"صفح عنه\" — he turned his face away from him. Metaphorical: to turn away from requital and instead bestow favor.\n\n- **Sibawayh Rule:** *Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā* (Restriction & Focused Predication) — \"إنما أعطى ما أعطى بأربع خصال\" employs innamā to restrict the cause of the gift to four qualities, and \"ليس الحليم من ظلم فحلم حتى إذا قدر انتقم\" uses laysa to negate the predicate entirely before affirming the true definition.\n\n---\n\n**", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Insight"}], "96": [{"arabic": "ما أحب أن يجعل حسابي إلى أبوي لأني اعلم أن الله تعالى أرحم بي منهما وقال بعض السلف المؤمن إذا عصى الله تعالى ستره عن أبصار الملائكة كيلا تراه فتشهد عليه وكتب محمد بن صعب إلى أسود بن سالم بخطه إن العبد إذا كان مسرفا فاعلى نفسه فرفع يديه يدعو ويقول يا رب حجبت الملائكة صوته وكذا الثانية والثالثة حتى إذا قال الرابعة يا ربي قاله الله تعالى حتى متى تحجبون عني صوت عبدي قد علم عبدي أنه ليس له رب يغفر له الذنوب غيري أشهدكم إني قد غفرت له وقال إبراهيم بن أدهم رحمة الله عليه خلا لي الط", "english": "In the report (khabar): \"Were you not to sin, God would create a creation who would sin, and He would forgive them.\" (1) In another wording: \"He would take you away and bring a creation who would sin, and He would forgive them — verily, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\" And in the report: \"Were you not to sin, I would fear for you what is worse than sins.\" It was said: \"And what is that?\" He said: \"Self-amazement (al-ʿujb).\" (2)", "book_title": "Fear and Hope", "section_title_ar": "Section 1034", "section_title_en": "The Completion of the Matter — On the Preacher's Gentleness in Employing Reports of Fear and Hope", "section_index": 1034, "anchors": "- Root: لطف (luṭf)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Gentleness, subtlety, kindness in approach; to be gracious and delicate in manner.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Divine gentleness (luṭf) as an attribute of God's subtle providence; here, the preacher's emulation of prophetic gentleness in spiritual counsel.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) — physical softness; metaphorical (majāz) — refinement of speech and manner suited to the spiritual state of the listener.\n- Root: رجا (rajā')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Hope, expectation of good; the opposite of despair (ya's).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Hope in God's mercy as a theological virtue balancing fear (khawf); the state of the believer who relies on divine generosity over personal merit.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — anticipation of a future good; metaphorical — the soul's reliance on God's pardon despite sin.\n- Root: عجب (ʿajab)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Self-amazement, vanity, wonder at oneself.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Spiritual pride (ʿujb) — a hidden sin worse than overt transgression, as it nullifies deeds.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — astonishment; metaphorical — the heart's complacency in its own obedience, leading to ruin.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction and Specification) — The conditional and exceptive structures (law lā... la-khalaqa, illā an yataghammadani) govern the precise scope of divine mercy and human agency.", "content_type": "fiqh", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the inner and outer dimensions of worship, from 'Fear and Hope'", "badge": "Worship"}], "98": [{"arabic": "له من يسألني فأعطيه من يستغفرني فأغفر له (6) وقيل إن يعقوب صلى الله عليه وسلم إنما قال سوف أستغفر لكم ربي ليدعو في وقت السحر فقيل إنه قام في وقت السحر يدعو وأولاده يؤمنون خلفه فأوحى الله عز وجل إني قد غفرت لهم وجعلتهم أنبياء الثاني أن يغتنم الأحوال الشريفة قال أبو هريرة رضي الله عنه إن أبواب السماء تفتح عند زحف الصفوف في سبيل الله تعالى وعند نزول الغيث وعند إقامة الصلوات المكتوبة فاغتنموا الدعاء فيها وقال مجاهد إن الصلاة جعلت في خير الساعات فعليكم بالدعاء خلف الصلوات وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم الدعاء بين الأذان والإقامة لا يرد (7) وقال صل", "english": "Allah the Exalted has said: {«وَإِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ أُجِيبُ دَعْوَةَ الدَّاعِ إِذَا دَعَانِ فَلْيَسْتَجِيبُوا لِي»} (And when My servants ask you concerning Me — indeed I am near. I respond to the invocation of the supplicant when he calls upon Me. So let them respond to Me — Qurʾan 2:186). And He the Exalted said: {«ادْعُوا رَبَّكُمْ تَضَرُّعًا وَخُفْيَةً إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِينَ»} (Call upon your Lord in humility and privately; indeed, He does not like transgressors — Qurʾan 7:55). And He the Exalted said: {«وَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُونِي أَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدْخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ»} (And your Lord said: Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell humiliated — Qurʾan 40:60). And He, Glorified and Exalted, said: {«قُلِ ادْعُوا اللَّهَ أَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمَنَ أَيًّا مَا تَدْعُوا فَلَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَى»} (Say: Call upon Allah or call upon the Most Merciful. Whichever [name] you call — to Him belong the Most Beautiful Names — Qurʾan 17:110).", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 241", "section_title_en": "The Book of Invocation — Section 241: The Second Chapter on the Etiquette of Supplication (Duʿāʾ), Its Virtue, the Virtue of Certain Transmitted Supplications, the Virtue of Seeking Forgiveness (Istighfār), and Invoking Blessings upon the Messenger of Allah (Peace Be Upon Him)", "section_index": 241, "anchors": "- Root: دعو (Daʿā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الدعاء: الرغبة إلى الله تعالى، والاستعانة به. وأصل الدعو: الإقبال على الشيء بالرغبة والطلب. والدعوة: الكلمة التي يدعو بها. والمدعوّ: الذي يجيب. والداعي: الفاعل. واستدعاه: طلب منه الدعاء.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الدعاء: الرغبة إلى الله تعالى في قضاء الحاجة، وهو ضربان: دعاء عبادة، ودعاء مسألة. فدعاء العبادة: هو التوجه إلى الله تعالى بالطاعة والإخلاص، ودعاء المسألة: هو طلب الحاجة. قال تعالى: {وقال ربكم ادعوني أستجب لكم} — فجعل الدعاء عبادة، إذ قال: {إن الذين يستكبرون عن عبادتي} فعطف العبادة على الدعاء، فدلّ على أنهما واحد.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"دعوته دعواً ودعاءً: ناديته وصحت به. ودعا الله: ابتهل إليه بالسؤال. ودعا الرجل: استنصره. ودعا الناقة: استدبرها.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"الدعاء في العبادة: استعارة من دعاء المسألة، لأن العابد كأنه يسأل الله الثواب والقبول. ومنه قوله تعالى: {إن الذين يستكبرون عن عبادتي} — أي عن دعائي، فسمّى العبادة دعاءً.\"\n\n- Root: سحر (Saḥara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"السحر: طرف الحلقوم والرئة. وقيل: السحر: آخر الليل عند الصبح. والسحور: الأكل في السحر. والسحرة: السحر الأخير من الليل.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"السحر يقال على معان: الأول: الخداع وتخييلات لا حقيقة لها... والثاني: وقت السحر، وهو آخر الليل، سمي بذلك لأنه وقت يكون فيه تنفس الصعداء واسترواح من ظلمة الليل، أو لأنه وقت خفاء الناس وسكون الأصوات.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"لقيته سحراً وسحرة وبالسحر وفي أعلى السحرين وهما سحر مع الصبح وسحر قبله.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"السحر في قوله تعالى: {وبالأسحار هم يستغفرون} — هو الوقت الأخير من الليل، وهو أشرف الأوقات للدعاء، لأنه وقت غفلة الناس وخلوة القلب.\"\n\n- Root: عرف (ʿArafa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"العرف: الطيب. والمعرفة: العلم بالشيء على وجه التدبر. وعرفة: جبل بمكة، سمي بذلك لأن الناس يتعارفون فيه، أو لأن جبريل عليه السلام عرّف إبراهيم المناسك فيه.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"عرفة: اسم للموقف الذي يقف فيه الحجاج، سمي بذلك لأن آدم وحواء تعارفا فيه بعد الهبوط، وقيل: لأن جبريل عرّف إبراهيم المناسك فيه.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"يوم عرفة: اليوم التاسع من ذي الحجة، وهو يوم الموقف.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"عرفة في قولهم: يوم عرفة — اسم للموقف، سمي بذلك لتعارف الناس فيه، أو لتعريف جبريل إبراهيم المناسك.\"\n\n- Root: غفر (Ghafara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"المغفرة: ستر الذنب والتجاوز عنه. والغفر: الستر. والمغفر: ما يستر الرأس في الحرب. والغفور: الكثير المغفرة.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الغفران: ستر الذنب والتجاوز عنه، وأصله من الغفر وهو الستر. قال تعالى: {وإن تغفر لهم فإنك أنت العزيز الحكيم}. والاستغفار: طلب المغفرة، وهو ضربان: استغفار باللسان، واستغفار بالقلب واللسان معاً، وهو النافع.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"غفرت الذنب غفراً ومغفرة: سترته وتجاوزت عنه. واستغفرت الله: طلبت مغفرته.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"الاستغفار باللسان مع الإصرار: استعارة للكذب، لأن المستغفر الحقيقي هو التائب المقلع عن الذنب.\"\n\n- Root: صلو (Ṣalā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الصلاة: الدعاء، وقيل: العبادة، وقيل: الرحمة من الله، والاستغفار من الملائكة. والصلاة من الله: الرحمة، ومن الملائكة: الاستغفار، ومن المؤمنين: الدعاء.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الصلاة في الأصل: الدعاء، قال تعالى: {صلوا عليه وسلموا تسليماً} — أي ادعوا له. ثم غلب استعمالها في العبادة المخصوصة، والصلاة من الله: الرحمة، ومن الملائكة: الاستغفار.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Haqiqah/Literal): \"الصلاة: الدعاء. ومنه قوله تعالى: {وصل عليهم إن صلاتك سكن لهم} — أي ادع لهم.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas - Majaz/Metaphorical): \"الصلاة على النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم: استعارة للدعاء له بالرحمة والتعظيم، لأن أصل الصلاة الدعاء.\"\n\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication)\n  * Governing Rule: \"إنما\" تفيد الحصر والقصر، فإذا قيل: \"إن الدعاء هو العبادة\" — فالمبتدأ والخبر معرفتان، والجملة تفيد الحصر والتأكيد. وإذا قيل: \"الدعاء مخ العبادة\" — فالإسناد فيه تشبيه بليغ، حيث شبه الدعاء بالمخ الذي هو لبّ العظم وجوهره، فالدعاء هو اللبّ والجوهر الحقيقي للعبادة.\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "أنفسهم لا تقنطوا من رحمة الله إن الله يغفر الذنوب جميعا إنه هو الغفور الرحيم وأنيبوا إلى ربكم أمرهم بالإنابة وقال تعالى وإني لغفار لمن تاب وآمن وعمل صالحا ثم اهتدى فإذا توقع المغفرة مع التوبة فهو راج وإن توقع المغفرة مع الإصرار فهو مغرور كما أن من ضاق عليه وقت الجمعة وهو في السوق فخطر له أن يسعى إلى الجمعة فقال له الشيطان إنك لا تدرك الجمعة فأقم على موضعك فكذب الشيطان ومر يعدو وهو يرجو أن يدرك الجمعة فهو راج وإن استمر على التجارة وأخذ يرجو تأخير الإمام للصلاة لأجله إلى وسط الوقت أو لأجل غيره أو لسبب من الأسباب التي لا يعر", "english": "Every soul shall taste what it has earned. And {«وَأَنَّ كُلَّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ»} — \"And that every soul is a pledge for what it has earned.\" So what has deluded you concerning God, after you have heard and comprehended? They will say: \"Had we but listened or reasoned, we would not be among the companions of the Blaze.\" Thus they will confess their sin. So away with the companions of the Blaze!", "book_title": "Fear and Hope", "section_title_ar": "Section 890", "section_title_en": "The Anatomy of Hope (Rajā') and Delusion (Ghurūr): A Kalamic Dissection of the Soul's Two States", "section_index": 890, "anchors": "- Root: نفس (Nafs)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, or spirit; that which desires proximity and discourse; the locus of breath and life.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Nafs denotes the rūḥ (spirit) and, in divine attribution, the very Dhāt (Essence) of God—as in {«وَيُحَذِّرُكُمُ اللَّهُ نَفْسَهُ»}—entailing no real multiplicity despite grammatical annexation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah) usage refers to the living, breathing self; metaphorical (Majaz) usage extends to \"blood\" (nafs sā'ilah) and the \"evil eye\" (nafs as 'ayn). Here, it signifies the moral agent bearing responsibility.\n- Root: توب (Tawb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Return, repentance; the act of turning back from error.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Tawbah is abandoning the sin in the most excellent manner—the third and highest form of excuse (after denial and pretext). In Sacred Law: forsaking the sin due to its ugliness, remorse for the past, resolve against recurrence, and restitution of what can be restored.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"The servant repents to God from his sin; God turns in mercy to the servant.\" The reciprocal dynamic—God's acceptance (tawbah) meeting the servant's return (inābah)—is operative in this text.\n- Root: ذنب (Dhanb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The tail of an animal; what trails behind; by extension, a fault or crime as the \"consequence\" one drags after oneself.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In origin, \"taking hold of a thing's tail\"—i.e., seizing the outcome. Sin is that which trails the soul and binds it as a pledge (rahīnah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Metaphorical: \"He is among the tails (adhnāb) of the people\"—the laggards. The sinner is one who follows his lower tail, and the verse {«كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ»} makes the soul a hostage to its own trailing deeds.\n- Root: غفر (Ghafr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To cover, shield, or protect; the Ghifār tribe's name; a helmet (mighfar) that shields the head.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ghufrān from God is His shielding the servant from the touch of chastisement—a protective covering, not mere erasure. It may also mean outward forbearance.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"O God, forgive (ghufrānan)!\"—a covering over the stain. Metaphorical: Zuhayr's beasts \"did not forgive\" their negligence—i.e., did not shield the offspring from destruction. Hope of forgiveness without repentance is thus not ghufrān but ghurūr (delusion).\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين العامل والمعمول (Interposition between Operator and Operand) — The periodic structure of verses like {«إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا»} delays the predicate to heighten rhetorical impact; the conditional \"if you say... know that\" (fa-in qulta... fa-'lam) governs the entire dialectical sequence, requiring the apodosis to resolve the protasis with logical necessity.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Fear and Hope'", "badge": "Insight"}], "100": [{"arabic": "الشيطان ينزغ بينهم وقال مخبرا عن يوسف من بعد إن نزغ الشيطان بيني وبين إخوتي ويقال ما تواخى اثنان في الله فتفرق بينهما إلا بذنب يرتكبه أحدهما وكان بشر يقول إذا قصر العبد في طاعة الله سلبه الله من يؤنسه وذلك لأن الإخوان مسلاة للهموم وعون على الدين ولذلك قال ابن المبارك ألذ الأشياء مجالسة الإخوان والانقلاب إلى كفاية والمودة الدائمة هي التي تكون في الله وما يكون لغرض يزول بزوال ذلك الغرض ومن ثمرات المودة في الله أن لا تكون مع حسد في دين ودنيا وكيف يحسده وكل ما هو لأخيه فإليه ترجع فائدته وبه وصف الله تعالى المحبين في الله تعالى فقال", "english": "I say: The meaning of loyalty (al-wafāʾ) is steadfastness upon love and its continuation until death — with him, and after death with his children and his friends. For love is sought only for the Hereafter; if it is severed before death, the deed is rendered void and the striving is lost. For this reason, he ﷺ said concerning the seven whom God will shade in His shade: «ورجلان تحابا في الله اجتمعا على ذلك وتفرقا عليه» — \"And two men who loved each other for God's sake, gathering upon that and parting upon that.\"", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 427", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 427: On the Meaning of Loyalty (al-Wafāʾ) and Its Fruits", "section_index": 427, "anchors": "- Root: وفي (W-F-Y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Complete fulfillment, perfect performance of a covenant; to be true to one's bond.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Loyalty (wafāʾ) is the completion of a promise (ʿahd) and its preservation against dissolution; its opposite is betrayal (ghadr) and severance (qaṭīʿah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"وفى بعهده\" — he fulfilled his pact completely. Metaphorical: \"وفى الكيل\" — he gave full measure; loyalty in love is the full measure of brotherhood, for it is the perfection of the covenant of affection.\n- Root: حبب (Ḥ-B-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core love, affection, steadfast amity.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): True love (maḥabbah) in the theological sense is the inclination of the heart toward what pleases the Beloved; when it is \"for God\" (fī Allāh), it is purely spiritual and enduring, not subject to the vicissitudes of worldly aims.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"حبه يحبه حبا\" — he loved him. Metaphorical: \"تحابا في الله\" — they loved each other for God's sake, i.e., their love is bound by the divine bond, not by transient causes.\n- Root: نزغ (N-Z-GH)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To incite, to provoke, to instigate discord.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Nazgh\" is the insinuation of corruption and the stirring of strife by Satan; it is the subtle injection of rancor between two hearts united in good.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"نزغ بينهم\" — he stirred up trouble between them. Metaphorical: Satan's \"nazgh\" is his secret whispering that ignites the fire of separation after the coolness of affection.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Specification) — The conditional and restrictive particles (innamā, law, idhā) govern the periodic structure, binding the protasis of loyalty's test to its apodosis of reward or loss.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "101": [{"arabic": "مسلمين أنت ولي في الدنيا والآخرة توفني مسلما وألحقني بالصالحين أنت ولينا فاغفر لنا وارحمنا وأنت خير الغافرين واكتب لنا في هذه الدنيا حسنة وفي الآخرة إنا هدنا إليك ربنا عليك توكلنا وإليك أنبنا وإليك المصير ربنا لا تجعلنا فتنة للقوم الظالمين ربنا لا تجعلنا فتنة للذين كفروا واغفر لنا ربنا إنك أنت العزيز الحكيم ربنا اغفر لنا ذنوبنا وإسرافنا في أمرنا وثبت أقدامنا وانصرنا على القوم الكافرين ربنا اغفر لنا ولإخواننا الذين سبقونا بالإيمان ولا تجعل في قلوبنا غلا للذين آمنوا ربنا إنك رؤوف رحيم ربنا آتنا من لدنك", "english": "And employ me in righteous deeds which You will accept from me. (1) O God, I ask You for pardon, well-being, good certainty, and soundness in this world and the next. (2) O You Whom sins do not harm and from Whom forgiveness does not diminish anything — grant me that which will not harm You, and give me that which will not diminish You. Our Lord, pour upon us patience and cause us to die as Muslims. You are our Protector in this world and the next; cause me to die as a Muslim and join me with the righteous. You are our Protector, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the Best of forgivers. And write for us good in this world and in the Hereafter — indeed, we have turned to You in repentance. Our Lord, upon You we rely, to You we turn in repentance, and to You is the final return. Our Lord, make us not a trial for the wrongdoing people. Our Lord, make us not a trial for those who disbelieve, and forgive us, our Lord — indeed, You are the Mighty, the Wise. Our Lord, forgive us our sins and our excesses in our affairs, make firm our feet, and grant us victory over the disbelieving people. Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith, and place not in our hearts any rancor toward those who believe — our Lord, indeed You are Kind, Merciful. Our Lord, grant us from Yourself mercy and prepare for us from our affair right guidance. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the chastisement of the Fire. Our Lord, indeed we have heard a caller calling to faith — to His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {«إنك لا تخلف الميعاد»} [آل عمران/ 194] — Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err. Our Lord, to the end of the surah. (3) My Lord, forgive me and my parents, and have mercy upon them as they raised me when I was small; and forgive the believing men and the believing women, and the Muslim men and the Muslim women, the living among them and the dead. (4) My Lord, forgive, have mercy, and overlook what You know — and You are the Most Exalted, the Most Generous, the Best of the merciful, and the Best of the forgivers. And indeed, to God we belong and to Him we return; and there is no might and no power except through God, the Exalted, the Magnificent; and God suffices us, and He is the Best Disposer of affairs. And may God send blessings upon Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets, and upon his family and his companions, and grant them abundant peace. (5)", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 252", "section_title_en": "Section 252 — Supplications for Morning and Evening: Comprehensive Prayers of the Prophet (ﷺ)", "section_index": 252, "anchors": "- Root: لهم (l-h-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of swallowing/ingesting (iltihām); from this derives the sense of something being cast directly into the innermost recess of the heart (al-rawʿ).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإلهام: إلقاء الشيء في الروع\" — ilhām is the casting of a thing into the innermost consciousness, specifically from God or the higher assembly (al-malaʾ al-aʿlā). It is that which the Prophet (ﷺ) called \"the touch of the angel\" (limat al-malak) and \"the breath of the Holy Spirit in my innermost heart\" (nafth rūḥ al-qudus fī rawʿī).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"ألهمه الله الخير: ألقاه في روعه\" — God inspired him with good: He cast it into his innermost consciousness. Metaphorical (majāz): A horse that \"swallows the ground\" (yaltaḥimu al-arḍ) in swiftness; thus ilhām is the swift, direct ingress of divine guidance into the soul without intermediary effort.\n- Root: حمد (ḥ-m-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes praise arising from recognition of voluntary excellence and beneficence; al-ḥamd is commendation of the beloved for their attributes and acts of goodness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Praise (ḥamd) is the acknowledgment of beneficence (niʿmah) with reverence and love; it is distinguished from mere thanks (shukr) in that it is directed to the essence and attributes of the praised one, not solely to the benefit received.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"أحمد الله تعالى بجميع محامده\" — I praise God with all His praiseworthy attributes. Metaphorical: \"أحمدت صنيعه\" — I found his deed praiseworthy; thus the tongue's praise must be matched by the heart's recognition of the praised one's perfection.\n- Root: غفر (gh-f-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The root denotes covering and shielding; al-mighfar is the helmet that protects the head in battle.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الغفر: إلباس ما يصونه عن الدنس\" — Forgiveness is the clothing of that which shields from filth. God's forgiveness (maghfirah) is His shielding of the servant from the touch of chastisement, covering the sin so that it is as though it never were.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"اللهم غفرًا\" — O God, forgive. Metaphorical: The she-beasts that \"did not forgive\" their heedlessness (lam taghfir la-hā ghaflātuhā) — i.e., they did not shield their young from destruction; thus forgiveness is active protection, not mere erasure.\n- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, the soul; that which breathes and has vital spirit; also used for the very essence of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح\" — the soul is the spirit; and in God's saying {«ويحذركم الله نفسه»} [آل عمران/ 28], \"His Self\" means His very essence (dhāt), which — though grammatically expressed as an annexation implying distinction — is in reality identical, with no multiplicity in the Divine Essence.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس\" — a precious thing. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه\" — he poured out his blood/life; thus nafs is the seat of life, passion, and moral responsibility.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الدعاء والخبر (The Chapter of Supplication and Assertion) — Supplications (duʿāʾ) are grammatically constructed as optative sentences (inshāʾ ṭalabī) using the imperative (rabbighfir), the jussive (lā tuʾākhidhnā), and the vocative (rabbanā), yet they may embed assertive clauses (khabar) of praise (al-ḥamdu lillāh) and attestation (lā ilāha illā anta). The periodic structure of these prayers alternates between direct address to God (munādāh) and self-referential confession, requiring the translator to preserve the vocative force of \"O God\" and \"Our Lord\" without flattening into mere description.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "105": [{"arabic": "الكتاب إلا أماني يعني التلاوة المجردة وقوله عز وجل وكأين من آية في السموات والأرض يمرون عليها وهم عنها معرضون لأن القرآن هو المبين لتلك الآيات في السموات والأرض ومهما تجاوزها ولم يتأثر بها كان معرضا عنها ولذلك قيل إن من لم يكن متصفا بأخلاق القرآن فإذا قرأ القرآن ناداه الله تعالى مالك ولكلامي وأنت معرض عني دع عنك كلامي إن لم تتب إلي ومثال العاصي إذا قرأ القرآن وكرره مثال من يكرر كتاب الملك في كل يوم مرات وقد كتب إليه في عمارة مملكته وهو مشغول بتخريبها ومقتصر على دراسة", "english": "And at the mention of God, His attributes, and His names, he bows low in humility before His majesty and in apprehension of His greatness. And at the mention of the disbelievers' sayings — those things impossible for God, Mighty and Majestic, such as their attributing to Him a son or a consort — he lowers his voice and inwardly recoils in shame at the ugliness of their speech. And at the description of Paradise, his innermost being surges forth with longing for it. And at the description of the Fire, his limbs tremble in fear of it. For when the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, said to Ibn Mas'ud, \"Recite to me,\" he said: \"I began reciting Surah al-Nisa'. When I reached {فكيف إذا جئنا من كل أمة بشهيد وجئنا بك على هؤلاء شهيدا} [How then shall it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?] (4:41), I saw his two eyes overflowing with tears. He then said to me: 'That is enough for you now.'\" And this was because the witnessing of that very state had wholly overwhelmed his heart.", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "section_title_ar": "Section 230", "section_title_en": "The States of the Heart During Qur'anic Recitation — The Condition of the True Recieter", "section_index": 230, "anchors": "- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of trembling fear, trepidation of the heart\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the inward apprehension of fear; cited in {إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم}\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال\" — a man fearful, a people fearful; the state of the heart's trembling before divine majesty\n- Root: وصف (w-ṣ-f)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Describing a thing by its attributes and qualities\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوصف: ذكر الشيء بحليته ونعته\" — description is the mention of a thing by its adornment and attribute; may be true or false\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical: \"وجهها يصف الحسن\" — metaphorical usage where the face itself \"describes\" beauty; likewise, the tongue may \"describe\" falsehood, as in {ولا تقولوا لما تصف ألسنتكم الكذب}\n- Root: وفي (w-f-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Completeness, fulfillment, reaching full measure\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوافي: الذي بلغ التمام\" — that which attains completion; \"أوفى: إذا تمم العهد ولم ينقض حفظه\" — fulfilled the covenant without breach\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"درهم واف\" — a full-weight dirham; Metaphorical: \"أوفى على المائة إذا زاد عليها\" — surpassed the hundred\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The separation between the governing preposition and its object by intervening clauses, as in \"فلما بلغت {فكيف إذا جئنا...}\" where the temporal clause governs the narrative sequence", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Insight"}], "107": [{"arabic": "عليه شيء مما يسرون وما يعلنون وحذرهم أن يأخذهم بغتة وهم لا يشعرون فقال {ما ينظرون إلا صيحة واحدة تأخذهم وهم يخصمون فلا يستطيعون توصية ولا إلى أهلهم يرجعون} والصلاة والسلام على محمد رسوله الذي يسير تحت لوائه النبيون وعلى آله وأصحابه الأئمة المهديين والسادة المرضيين صلاة يوازي عددها عدد ما كان من خلق الله وما سيكون ويحظى ببركتها الأولون والآخرون وسلم تسليما كثيرا أما بعد فإن الغضب شعلة نار اقتبست من نار الله الموقدة التي تطلع على الأفئدة وإنها لمستكنة في طي الفؤاد استكنان الجمر تحت الرماد ويستخرجه الكبر الدفي", "english": "In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Praise be to God, upon whose pardon and mercy none rely except the hopeful, and from whose evil wrath and assault none fear except the fearful — He who gradually seizes His servants from whence they know not, and who has given dominion over them to their lusts, commanding them to abandon what they desire, and who has tried them with anger while charging them to swallow their rage in what provokes them. Then He surrounded them with hardships and pleasures, and granted them respite to see how they would act. He tested their love through them, to make known the truth of what they claim. He made known to them that nothing is hidden from Him of what they conceal or proclaim, and warned them lest He seize them suddenly while they are unaware. For He said: {«They await but a single blast which will seize them while they are disputing; so they will not be able to make a bequest, nor to their families will they return»} (Q. 36:49-50). And prayers and peace be upon Muhammad, His Messenger, beneath whose banner the prophets walk, and upon his family and companions — the rightly-guided imams and the pleasing masters — prayers whose number equals the number of what has been of God's creation and what will be, and by whose blessing the first and the last are favored — and abundant peace.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "section_title_ar": "Section 700", "section_title_en": "The Book of Condemnation of Anger, Spite, and Envy — Book Five of the Quarter of Destroyers from The Revival of the Religious Sciences", "section_index": 700, "anchors": "- Root: غضب (ghadab)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of anger, rage, fury; the boiling and agitation of the blood\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — when attributed to God, it means retribution (intiqām) alone, not emotional agitation; the Prophet described it as \"a live coal kindled in the heart of the son of Adam\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal anger is the boiling of the blood in living beings; metaphorical usage extends to inanimate things like fire and the reins of a mount\n- Root: قلب (qalb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; also the turning, overturning, and transformation of a thing from one state to another\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — the heart is so named for its constant turning (taqallub) and fluctuation between states; it is the seat of understanding and the locus of divine address\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal is the physical organ; metaphorical is the subtle spiritual reality (laṭīfah rabbāniyyah) that is the locus of knowledge and will\n- Root: حسد (hasad)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Envy; the wishing for removal of another's blessing\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — envy is the desire for the removal of a blessing from one who deserves it, sometimes accompanied by striving to remove it; the believer envies (ghibṭah) while the hypocrite envies (hasad)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — \"Envy consumes the body as fire consumes wood\"; the envier is one who wishes evil upon the blessed\n- Root: هلك (halak)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Perdition, destruction, ruin; death\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — three senses: (1) loss of a thing from one's possession while it exists elsewhere, (2) corruption and dissolution of a thing, (3) death; the Quran uses it for all three\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal is physical destruction; metaphorical is the ruin of one's religion and afterlife through spiritual corruption\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of interposing elements between a preposition and its object when the intervening material constitutes a complete, meaningful unit, as in the Quranic pattern of extended periodic sentences that delay resolution for rhetorical effect.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "108": [{"arabic": "وإذا قلت وما أنا من المشركين فأخطر ببالك الشرك الخفي فإن قوله تعالى فمن كان يرجو لقاء ربه فليعمل عملا صالحا ولا يشرك بعبادة ربه أحدا نزل فيمن يقصد بعبادته وجه الله وحمد الناس وكن حذرا مشفقا من هذا الشرك واستشعر الخجلة في قلبك إن وصفت نفسك بأنك لست من المشركين من غير براءة عن هذا الشرك فإن اسم الشرك يقع على القليل والكثير منه وإذا قلت محياي ومماتي لله فاعلم أن هذا حال عبد مفقود لنفسه موجود لسيده وأنه إن صدر ممن رضاه وغضبه وقيامه وقعوده ورغبته في الحياة ورهبته من الموت لأمور ا", "english": "For this reason, he, peace be upon him, said: \"Give us rest, O Bilāl\" (1) — meaning, give us rest through it (the prayer) and through the call to it, for his delight, peace be upon him, was in it.", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 138", "section_title_en": "The Inner Works of Prayer: Unveiling the Heart's Secrets in the Ritual Prayer (Asrār al-Ṣalāh)", "section_index": 138, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (Q-L-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn a thing over, to revolve it, to divert it from one state to another; the heart as that which is constantly turning and fluctuating.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — The heart is that which is turned and diverted; its rectitude lies in its orientation towards God, its ruin in its turning towards other than Him.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical (Majaz): \"قلب المعلم الصبيان: صرفهم إلى بيوتهم\" (the teacher turned the boys towards their homes) — thus the heart's turning is its direction and intent.\n- Root: وجه (W-J-H)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The face; the foremost, noblest, and most apparent part of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"ولما كان الوجه أول ما يستقبلك، وأشرف ما في ظاهر البدن استعمل في مستقبل كل شيء، وفي أشرفه ومبدئه\" — The face is used metaphorically for the essence and the direction of a thing; the \"face of the heart\" is its intention and aspiration.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"واجهته مواجهة ووجاها\" (to face one another). Metaphorical: \"هذا وجه الثوب. ووجه القوم، وهؤلاء وجوه البلد\" (the face of a garment, the chiefs of a people) — thus the \"face\" of the heart is its foremost orientation.\n- Root: وجل (W-J-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: A trembling of the heart from fear or awe.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — The sensing of fear; the heart's tremor before the majesty of the Divine.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال، وقد وجل وجلا\" — A man trembling with fear.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The particle \"innamā\" restricts and confines the predicate to the subject alone, negating it from all else. This is crucial for understanding \"إنما هذه الظواهر تحريكات للبواطن\" — the outward acts are *only* movements to stir the inward realities, nothing more.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Insight"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 2281], [2, 2281, 3366], [3, 3366, 5464], [4, 5464, 7237], [5, 7237, 9336]], "2": [[1, 400, 2327], [2, 2327, 3980], [3, 3980, 5480], [4, 5480, 7312], [5, 7312, 8965], [6, 8965, 10669]], "3": [[1, 400, 1105], [2, 1105, 2123], [3, 2123, 3192], [4, 3192, 4193], [5, 4193, 5353], [6, 5353, 6754], [7, 6754, 9134], [8, 9134, 10203], [9, 10203, 11145], [10, 11145, 12715], [11, 12715, 13557], [12, 13557, 14240], [13, 14240, 14695], [14, 14695, 15685], [15, 15685, 16368], [16, 16368, 18087]], "4": [[1, 400, 874], [2, 874, 1657], [3, 1657, 2708], [4, 2708, 3862], [5, 3862, 5326], [6, 5326, 6388], [7, 6388, 7357], [8, 7357, 8037], [9, 8037, 8738], [10, 8738, 9995], [11, 9995, 11438], [12, 11438, 12675], [13, 12675, 14035], [14, 14035, 14550], [15, 14550, 15841]], "5": [[1, 400, 1258